const TEENHQ_DATA = {"advice": [{"id": "school-01-first-day-at-a-new-school", "uid": 1, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "01", "title": "First Day at a New School", "body": ["So. You're starting at a new school.", "And suddenly you're thinking about literally everything.", "What if everyone already has friends? What if you sit alone? What if you walk into the wrong classroom? What if your outfit looks weird? What if you say something embarrassing and everyone remembers it forever?", "First of all: breathe.", "Your first day is not an audition for your entire school career.", "You don't need to walk in and immediately become the funniest, prettiest, most popular person there. You don't even need to make a best friend.", "Honestly, your only job on day one is to get comfortable enough to come back on day two.", "Before school", "Do yourself a favour and make the morning as easy as possible.", "Pack your bag the night before. Check your timetable. Put your clothes out. Charge your phone. Figure out how you're getting there.", "And please don't stay up until 2 a.m. because you're nervous and then arrive at school looking like you just fought for your life 😭.", "If you can't sleep, that's okay. Just lie down, put your phone away, and let yourself rest.", "When you get there", "If you don't know where something is, ask.", "\"Hey, I'm new. Do you know where Room 14 is?\"", "That's not embarrassing. You're literally new. Nobody expects you to know the building.", "And when you're introduced to people, try to actually remember their names. You don't need to become besties immediately. Even remembering someone's name the next day gives you something to talk about.", "Making friends", "Don't walk into school thinking:", "\"I need to find my people TODAY.\"", "That's way too much pressure.", "Instead, aim for little interactions.", "\"Have you had this teacher before?\"", "\"What's the homework?\"", "\"Do you know what's next on the timetable?\"", "\"Is anyone sitting here?\"", "That's literally how friendships start. Not with some magical movie moment where you lock eyes across the cafeteria and suddenly have matching bracelets.", "Sometimes you talk to someone once.", "Then again the next day.", "Then you sit together.", "Then somehow three months later you're sending them seventeen TikToks at midnight.", "It happens slowly.", "What if lunch sucks?", "It might.", "And if you end up eating lunch alone on your first day, please don't go home and decide you have no friends.", "You had one lunch.", "That's it.", "You don't know what tomorrow looks like yet.", "If you see someone who seems nice, you can always ask if you can sit with them. You don't need a perfect excuse.", "One more thing", "Don't change your entire personality because you're scared people won't like you.", "If you're quiet, you don't suddenly have to become loud.", "If you love anime, don't pretend you hate it because you think it's embarrassing.", "If you're funny, be funny.", "If you're awkward, congratulations, you're a human being.", "You want people to like you, not the character you invented for the first week of school.", "Your first-day checklist", "☐ Know where your classes are", "☐ Talk to at least one person", "☐ Ask for help when you need it", "☐ Learn one or two names", "☐ Eat something", "☐ Drink water", "☐ Don't judge the entire school after one day", "And that's enough."], "bigSister": "Your first day might not be amazing. That's okay. You don't need an amazing first day. You just need a beginning.", "journal": "What would make me feel more comfortable at my new school?", "globalNum": "001"}, {"id": "school-02-moving-schools-halfway-through-the-year", "uid": 2, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "02", "title": "Moving Schools Halfway Through the Year", "body": ["Moving schools halfway through the year is a special kind of awkward because everyone else already seems settled.", "People already have their seats.", "Their lunch groups.", "Their inside jokes.", "Teachers already know everybody's names.", "And then there's you, walking in like:", "\"Hi guys! So apparently I'm here now.\"", "😭", "It's completely normal to feel like you're interrupting something.", "But here's the thing: you're not.", "Schools change all the time. People leave. People join. Friend groups change. Someone will be absent tomorrow. Someone will switch classes next month. The social world you're walking into isn't nearly as permanent as it looks.", "Don't expect instant friendships", "This is probably the biggest mistake you can make.", "You arrive, nobody immediately becomes your best friend, and your brain goes:", "\"Yep. Everyone hates me.\"", "No.", "You just haven't had enough time yet.", "Give yourself a few weeks before deciding whether you fit in.", "Use your classes", "Classes are actually your easiest way in.", "Ask someone about the work.", "\"Wait, what page are we on?\"", "\"Did she say this is due tomorrow?\"", "\"Do we have a test next week?\"", "It gives you a reason to talk without having to randomly walk up to someone and announce that you're looking for friends.", "Find one person first", "Forget trying to join the biggest group in school.", "Find one person who seems kind.", "One person is enough.", "Once you know one person, they might introduce you to someone else. That person introduces you to someone else.", "Suddenly you're not walking around completely alone anymore.", "And if you hate it?", "Give it time, but don't force yourself to pretend everything is amazing.", "Maybe the school genuinely isn't a good fit.", "Maybe you need help from a parent, teacher, counselor, or another adult.", "There's a difference between:", "\"This is uncomfortable because it's new.\"", "and", "\"I'm being treated badly and I don't feel safe.\"", "Don't ignore the second one just because you're trying to \"adjust.\""], "bigSister": "You are allowed to miss your old school while still giving the new one a chance. Those two things can exist at the same time. You don't have to decide immediately whether this is your new home. Just let yourself arrive first.", "journal": "What's one thing from my old school I miss, and what's one thing I'm curious about here?", "globalNum": "002"}, {"id": "school-03-moving-countries", "uid": 3, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "03", "title": "Moving Countries", "body": ["Moving countries is not just changing your address.", "You're changing your routine, your surroundings, your school, your friendships, the food you eat, the way people talk, the weather, the little things you didn't even realize you were used to.", "So if you're excited one day and crying because you miss home the next...", "Yeah.", "That makes sense.", "The weirdest part?", "You can miss something you didn't even think you liked.", "You might suddenly miss the supermarket you used to complain about.", "Your old bus route.", "A specific snack.", "The sound of your old neighbourhood.", "Someone's annoying voice.", "That's homesickness. It doesn't always make logical sense.", "Don't force yourself to \"get over it\"", "You don't have to stop missing your old country in order to enjoy your new one.", "Keep your old friendships.", "Call people.", "Save photos.", "Make playlists.", "Cook food you used to eat.", "Keep little traditions.", "But also give yourself permission to experience where you are now.", "Try the local food.", "Go somewhere new.", "Learn how things work.", "Find your favourite place.", "You don't have to choose between your old life and your new one.", "Make your room feel like yours", "This sounds small, but it genuinely helps.", "Put up pictures.", "Use your favourite bedding.", "Keep your favourite things around.", "Have somewhere that feels familiar when everything else feels new.", "Don't compare EVERYTHING", "Your brain is going to do this automatically.", "\"Back home, we did it like this.\"", "\"Back home, school was better.\"", "\"Back home, people were nicer.\"", "Sometimes that's true.", "But if you compare every single thing, you'll never actually experience the new place.", "Give yourself time to find things you like here too.", "And yes, you can be excited.", "Being excited about your new life doesn't mean you don't care about the old one.", "You aren't betraying anyone by being happy.", "You're allowed to build a new life."], "bigSister": "Moving doesn't erase your old life. You get to carry pieces of it with you while making new ones.", "journal": "What are three things I want to keep from my old life, and three things I want to discover in my new one?", "globalNum": "003"}, {"id": "school-04-feeling-left-out", "uid": 4, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "04", "title": "Feeling Left Out", "body": ["Okay, this one hurts.", "Especially when you can literally SEE people hanging out without you.", "You open Snapchat.", "They're together.", "You check Instagram.", "They're together.", "You walk into school.", "They're together.", "And suddenly you're wondering:", "\"Did I do something?\"", "Maybe.", "But also... maybe not.", "Sometimes people genuinely leave you out intentionally. Sometimes they don't. Sometimes they're closer to each other. Sometimes plans happened randomly. Sometimes people are just inconsiderate.", "The important thing is not immediately deciding which explanation is true without knowing.", "Ask yourself what actually happened", "Not:", "\"Nobody likes me.\"", "What actually happened?", "\"Three people went out and didn't invite me.\"", "That's a fact.", "\"Everyone hates me.\"", "That's an assumption.", "Keeping those separate can stop your brain from turning one situation into a whole story.", "If it's a one-time thing", "Don't explode.", "Don't send:", "\"Wow okay I see how it is.\"", "Don't subtweet them.", "Don't post something obviously aimed at them.", "And please don't start a group chat called \"fake friends\" 😭.", "Just see what happens next.", "If it keeps happening", "That's different.", "If you're constantly being excluded, ignored, or only invited when someone else cancels, you might need to rethink the friendship.", "You don't have to have a dramatic friendship breakup.", "You can simply stop putting 100% of your energy into people who give you 20%.", "Talk to other people.", "Join something.", "Sit somewhere different.", "Start conversations.", "Sometimes the reason you're stuck feeling left out is because you've decided that the only people who can make you feel included are the same people excluding you.", "They're not.", "Don't chase inclusion", "This is important.", "You shouldn't have to audition for a place in someone's life.", "If someone wants you around, you should be able to feel it.", "Not perfectly. Friendships aren't perfect.", "But you shouldn't constantly feel like you're begging for a seat at the table.", "And if you are genuinely being excluded on purpose?", "Talk to someone you trust.", "Especially if it's becoming bullying, harassment, or a coordinated attempt to isolate you.", "You don't have to handle everything alone just because you're a teenager."], "bigSister": "Being left out can make you question your entire personality. Don't. Someone not inviting you somewhere doesn't suddenly make you boring, annoying, ugly, or unlikeable. It means you weren't included in that thing. That's all you know. Don't turn one rejection into a verdict on yourself.", "journal": "Am I missing these specific people, or am I missing the feeling of belonging?", "globalNum": "004"}, {"id": "school-05-sitting-alone-at-lunch", "uid": 5, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "05", "title": "Sitting Alone at Lunch", "body": ["Okay.", "So you got to lunch, looked around, and somehow every single table was already occupied.", "Or maybe you did have somewhere to sit, but you still felt like the odd one out.", "Either way, lunch can be brutal when you don't really know anyone yet.", "And I need you to know something before your brain starts doing that thing where it goes:", "\"Everyone has friends except me.\"", "No they don't.", "It just looks that way when you're sitting alone.", "There are probably other people eating alone too. You just don't notice them because you're too busy worrying about yourself.", "If you're actually alone", "First: don't panic.", "You don't need to pretend you're texting someone important. You don't need to spend the entire lunch hiding in the bathroom. And you definitely don't need to skip eating because you're embarrassed.", "Get your food.", "Find somewhere comfortable.", "Put on music if you're allowed to.", "Read something.", "Watch something.", "Or just sit there.", "There is genuinely nothing wrong with eating lunch alone.", "The problem is when you start telling yourself that being alone means you're unwanted.", "It doesn't.", "But what if you WANT company?", "Then go find some.", "I know. Horrifying.", "But you can literally walk up to someone and say:", "\"Hey, can I sit here?\"", "That's it.", "You don't need a speech.", "If they say yes, sit down and start with something easy.", "\"Have you had science yet?\"", "\"What's your next class?\"", "\"Is the food here always this bad?\"", "Congratulations. You have now started a conversation.", "What if they say no?", "It'll sting.", "I'm not gonna hit you with \"don't care what people think 🥺.\"", "You probably will care.", "But one person saying no doesn't mean everyone will.", "Maybe the seats are taken. Maybe they're waiting for someone. Maybe they're just weird about their table.", "Find somewhere else.", "You survived.", "And don't make lunch your friendship deadline", "This is where people get themselves stressed.", "You think:", "\"If I don't have a lunch group by Friday, I'm a loser.\"", "Girl, no 😭.", "Friendships don't follow a school timetable.", "You could meet your closest friend three months from now.", "You could become friends with someone because you got paired together for a random project.", "You could sit beside someone in class one day and suddenly talk every single day.", "Let it happen."], "bigSister": "Sitting alone isn't embarrassing. Feeling like you have to hide it is what makes it worse. You don't owe anyone the appearance of having a huge friend group.", "journal": "If I wasn't worried about what other people thought, how would I actually want to spend my lunch?", "globalNum": "005"}, {"id": "school-06-being-the-new-kid", "uid": 6, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "06", "title": "Being the New Kid", "body": ["Being the new kid is weird because everyone else seems to have a history together.", "Someone says:", "\"Remember what happened last year?\"", "And you're sitting there like:", "\"No ❤️.\"", "You don't know who's dating who.", "You don't know which teacher is strict.", "You don't know where anything is.", "You don't know which friend groups are actually nice and which ones look nice from a distance.", "That's okay.", "You aren't supposed to know yet.", "Don't be embarrassed about being new", "You don't need to hide it.", "If someone asks:", "\"Are you new?\"", "Just say yes.", "People are usually curious about new students anyway, so use that to your advantage.", "\"Yeah, I moved here recently.\"", "\"Oh really? From where?\"", "Boom. Conversation.", "Learn the school slowly", "You don't need to memorize everything on day one.", "Figure out:", "Your classrooms", "The toilets", "The cafeteria", "The office", "Where you wait before/after school", "Who to ask when you're lost", "After a week, you'll know more.", "After a month, you'll probably wonder why the building ever seemed confusing.", "Be curious about people", "Instead of desperately trying to make people like you, actually get curious about them.", "Ask questions.", "What music do they like?", "What subjects do they hate?", "What do they do after school?", "What shows are they watching?", "You don't have to make yourself interesting every second.", "People generally love talking about themselves.", "Don't attach yourself to the first person who talks to you", "This one is important.", "If the first person who talks to you is nice, great.", "But don't immediately decide:", "\"THIS IS MY BEST FRIEND.\"", "You don't know them yet.", "Be friendly. Get to know different people. See who you actually click with.", "Give yourself time", "You might feel awkward for a while.", "That's not proof you made the wrong decision.", "You're literally learning an entire social environment from scratch.", "Give it time."], "bigSister": "Being new isn't a personality trait. It's just a temporary situation. Eventually you won't be \"the new kid.\" You'll just be you.", "journal": "What kind of person do I want to be around while I'm getting settled here?", "globalNum": "006"}, {"id": "school-07-bad-grades", "uid": 7, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "07", "title": "Bad Grades", "body": ["Getting a grade you're unhappy with can make you feel like you're stupid.", "Especially when you actually studied.", "You looked at the paper and thought:", "\"Yeah, I know this.\"", "Then the grade comes back and it's giving:", "absolutely not.", "😭", "But a bad grade doesn't automatically mean you're bad at the subject.", "It means something about your preparation, understanding, memory, exam technique, or circumstances didn't work this time.", "So instead of staring at the number for three days, figure out why.", "Ask yourself what went wrong", "Did you not understand the topic?", "Did you understand it but forget it?", "Did you run out of time?", "Did you misread questions?", "Did you barely study?", "Did you study for hours but only reread your notes?", "Those are completely different problems.", "And they need completely different solutions.", "If you didn't understand it", "Go back.", "Find the exact part that doesn't make sense.", "Ask your teacher.", "Ask a classmate.", "Use another explanation.", "Don't just stare at the same textbook paragraph hoping knowledge will enter your brain through osmosis 😭.", "If you forgot everything", "You probably need more active revision.", "Instead of reading your notes ten times, close them and try to explain the topic yourself.", "Make flashcards.", "Do practice questions.", "Test yourself.", "Your brain needs to actually retrieve the information.", "If you ran out of time", "Practice with a timer.", "You might know the material perfectly and still lose marks because you spent 20 minutes on one question.", "If you didn't study", "Okay.", "Don't make excuses.", "But also don't spend the next week hating yourself.", "Figure out why you procrastinated and change the system.", "Maybe you started too late.", "Maybe you didn't know where to start.", "Maybe you were overwhelmed.", "Fix that.", "Don't compare your grade to everyone else's", "Your friend getting 95% doesn't make your 70% worse.", "And someone getting 40% doesn't make your 70% better.", "Your grade is information.", "Use it."], "bigSister": "You're allowed to be disappointed. Just don't turn \"I did badly on this test\" into \"I'm bad at everything.\" Those are not the same sentence.", "journal": "What specifically cost me marks this time, and what can I do differently before the next test?", "globalNum": "007"}, {"id": "school-08-failing-a-test", "uid": 8, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "08", "title": "Failing a Test", "body": ["Okay, so you failed.", "That sucks.", "I'm not going to pretend it doesn't.", "You might feel embarrassed, especially if you thought you'd done well.", "But failing one test is not the same thing as failing at school.", "Your next move matters more than the grade itself.", "First: let yourself be annoyed", "You don't have to immediately become productive.", "Be upset.", "Talk to someone.", "Have your little dramatic moment.", "Then move on.", "Because staring at the paper and thinking:", "\"I'm actually so stupid.\"", "isn't going to add marks to it.", "Look at the test", "This is the part people skip.", "Go through every question you got wrong.", "Sort them into categories:", "Didn't know it.", "Knew it but forgot.", "Misread it.", "Careless mistake.", "Didn't understand the question.", "Now you actually know what needs fixing.", "Talk to your teacher", "If you're confused about why you got something wrong, ask.", "You don't need to say:", "\"Why did you give me this mark?\"", "Try:", "\"Could you show me where I went wrong on this question?\"", "That's a completely different conversation.", "Make the next test easier for yourself", "Don't wait until the night before.", "Even 15–20 minutes a few days a week can be better than five hours of panic revision the night before.", "And don't just reread.", "Test yourself.", "Cover the answer.", "Try the question.", "Explain the topic out loud.", "Do practice papers.", "Don't hide the grade", "If you need help from a parent or teacher, hiding it usually makes things worse.", "If you're worried about how they'll react, tell them what happened and what you're going to do next.", "Instead of:", "\"I failed.\"", "Try:", "\"I got 42%. I know I struggled with these two topics, so I'm going to ask my teacher about them and start revising earlier for the next test.\"", "You're showing that you're taking responsibility."], "bigSister": "A failed test is a problem. It's not a prophecy. You can recover from a bad grade. You can improve. You can change how you study. One piece of paper does not get to decide how smart you are.", "journal": "What did this test teach me about how I currently study?", "globalNum": "008"}, {"id": "school-09-when-you-feel-like-your-teacher-doesn-t-like-you", "uid": 9, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "09", "title": "When You Feel Like Your Teacher Doesn't Like You", "body": ["Sometimes you genuinely get the feeling that a teacher doesn't like you.", "Maybe they always seem annoyed with you.", "Maybe they call you out more than everyone else.", "Maybe you feel like they expect you to fail.", "Or maybe you just don't click with their personality.", "Either way, having a teacher you don't like—or who you think doesn't like you—can make school exhausting.", "First, separate facts from feelings", "Ask yourself:", "What have they actually done?", "If the answer is:", "\"They don't smile at me.\"", "That's not necessarily proof.", "If it's:", "\"They repeatedly embarrass me in front of the class.\"", "That's different.", "Try to figure out what's actually happening before deciding what they think about you.", "Remember that teachers are people", "Some teachers are naturally serious.", "Some are sarcastic.", "Some are warm.", "Some seem permanently one minor inconvenience away from quitting 😭.", "Their personality doesn't automatically mean they hate you.", "If you've actually had problems with them", "Think about your side too.", "Have you been late?", "Talking in class?", "Not doing homework?", "Arguing with them?", "If you know you've been doing something, fix it.", "Not because you have to \"win them over,\" but because making your own situation easier is worth it.", "What if they're genuinely unfair?", "If a teacher repeatedly treats you unfairly, humiliates you, discriminates against you, threatens you, or makes you feel unsafe, don't just tell yourself to tolerate it.", "Write down what happened.", "Talk to a parent, guardian, counselor, head of year, or another trusted adult.", "You deserve to be treated respectfully.", "You don't have to love your teacher", "Your goal can simply be:", "Get through the class. Learn the material. Keep things respectful. Go home.", "Not every teacher is going to be your favourite person.", "That's okay."], "bigSister": "You don't need your teacher to adore you. You need a workable relationship where you can learn and be treated fairly.", "journal": "What is actually happening between me and this teacher, and what part of it can I control?", "globalNum": "009"}, {"id": "school-10-group-projects", "uid": 10, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "10", "title": "Group Projects", "body": ["Group projects.", "The school system's favourite way of finding out who has been doing all the work while everyone else watches.", "😭", "You might get lucky and have a great group.", "Or you might get:", "The person who disappears", "The person who does nothing", "The person who wants to control everything", "The person who starts everything the night before", "You", "If you're the person who usually ends up doing everything, stop.", "Divide the work immediately", "Don't just say:", "\"Okay, we'll figure it out.\"", "You will regret that.", "Decide who is doing what.", "For example:", "Person 1: Research", "Person 2: Slides", "Person 3: Script", "Person 4: Presentation", "Everyone: Final review", "Write it somewhere everyone can see.", "Set an actual deadline", "If the project is due Friday, don't make your deadline Friday.", "Try:", "Wednesday = everything finished", "Thursday = review", "Friday = submit", "That gives you room when someone inevitably says:", "\"Wait I thought YOU were doing that.\"", "Don't silently do everyone's work", "If someone isn't contributing, tell them.", "Not:", "\"YOU'RE SO USELESS.\"", "Obviously 😭.", "Try:", "\"Hey, we still need your section. Can you finish it by tonight so we can put everything together?\"", "If they still don't do anything, keep records of what you've completed and tell your teacher if necessary.", "If someone takes over", "You can say:", "\"I think we should hear everyone's ideas before deciding.\"", "You don't need to fight.", "And if the group is actually good?", "Enjoy it.", "Communicate.", "Help each other.", "Don't disappear because everyone seems responsible.", "A good group project can actually be fun."], "bigSister": "Being responsible doesn't mean becoming the unpaid employee of your entire group.", "journal": "What role do I naturally take in group work, and is that actually helping me?", "globalNum": "010"}, {"id": "school-11-presentation-anxiety", "uid": 11, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "11", "title": "Presentation Anxiety", "body": ["Standing in front of an entire class while everyone looks at you?", "Yeah, no thanks.", "Your hands shake.", "Your voice sounds weird.", "You forget words you literally knew five minutes ago.", "Suddenly the slide you've practiced twenty times looks like it's written in another language.", "You're not broken.", "That's nerves.", "Prepare enough that you don't have to rely on memory", "Don't memorize every single word.", "If you forget one sentence, you'll panic.", "Instead, understand your points.", "Know:", "Point 1", "Point 2", "Point 3", "Then explain them naturally.", "Practice out loud", "Not just inside your head.", "Actually say the words.", "Your brain needs to get used to hearing you speak.", "Practice in front of a mirror if you want.", "Or record yourself.", "Yes, you'll cringe.", "Do it anyway.", "Have a backup plan", "Keep tiny notes with keywords.", "Not a whole essay.", "Just enough to remind yourself where you're going next.", "Slow down", "When you're nervous, you probably talk way faster than you realize.", "Pause.", "Breathe.", "Continue.", "A two-second pause feels like ten seconds to you.", "To everyone else, it just looks normal.", "If you mess up", "Keep going.", "You don't have to announce:", "\"OMG I messed up.\"", "Just correct yourself and continue.", "Most people will forget the mistake by the time the next person presents."], "bigSister": "Your goal isn't to look completely fearless. Your goal is to get to the end. You can be nervous and still give a good presentation. Those things can exist together.", "journal": "What's one thing I can prepare in advance that would make my next presentation easier?", "globalNum": "011"}, {"id": "school-12-exam-stress", "uid": 12, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "12", "title": "Exam Stress", "body": ["Exam season has a way of making everything feel urgent.", "Suddenly you're convinced you need to revise twelve subjects, clean your room, reorganize your life, drink two litres of water, become a morning person, and somehow sleep eight hours.", "No.", "Let's calm down.", "Start by getting everything out of your head", "Write down:", "Every subject", "Every topic", "Every exam date", "Anything you need to finish", "Your brain shouldn't have to remember everything.", "Prioritize", "Not every topic deserves equal time.", "If you already understand something, don't spend three hours revising it because it's comfortable.", "Spend more time on the things you genuinely don't know.", "Don't make a ridiculous schedule", "If your timetable says:", "4:00–5:00 Maths", "5:00–6:00 Science", "6:00–7:00 English", "7:00–8:00 History", "...and you haven't even had dinner...", "Girl 😭.", "You're not a machine.", "Build breaks into your schedule.", "Use active revision", "Try:", "Practice questions", "Flashcards", "Past papers", "Blurting", "Teaching the topic aloud", "Quizzing yourself", "Reading the same page repeatedly can make you feel productive without actually testing whether you know it.", "Sleep", "Pulling an all-nighter might make you feel like you're working hard.", "It can also leave you exhausted and unable to think properly the next day.", "Sleep is part of studying."], "bigSister": "You don't need to feel completely calm to do well. You just need a plan that's realistic enough to follow.", "journal": "What is the one thing I can do today that would make tomorrow less stressful?", "globalNum": "012"}, {"id": "school-13-homework-overload", "uid": 13, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "13", "title": "Homework Overload", "body": ["Sometimes homework isn't difficult.", "There's just...", "SO MUCH OF IT.", "You finish one assignment and somehow three more appear.", "When everything feels urgent, your brain can basically shut down.", "You stare at your homework for twenty minutes and somehow end up watching videos.", "That's procrastination, but sometimes it's also overwhelm.", "Make a dump list", "Write every task down.", "Don't keep them floating around in your head.", "Then label them:", "🔴 Due tomorrow", "🟡 Due soon", "🟢 Can wait", "Start with the red ones.", "Don't start with the easiest thing just because it feels good", "Sometimes people spend an hour decorating their history notes because it's satisfying while their Maths assignment due tomorrow sits untouched.", "You know what you're doing 😭.", "Start with what's important.", "Break huge assignments into pieces", "Instead of:", "\"Do science project.\"", "Write:", "☐ Find sources", "☐ Take notes", "☐ Write introduction", "☐ Write section one", "☐ Make slides", "☐ Proofread", "Now it's six small tasks instead of one giant monster.", "Use short work sessions", "Try 25 minutes working, then 5 minutes off.", "Or 40 minutes and 10 minutes.", "Find what works.", "The point isn't the exact number.", "It's giving your brain a finish line.", "Ask for help", "If you're genuinely drowning in work, tell someone.", "A teacher can't help with a problem they don't know exists."], "bigSister": "Being busy all the time isn't the same as being productive. You don't get bonus points for making yourself miserable.", "journal": "What homework is stressing me out the most, and what's the smallest step I can take on it right now?", "globalNum": "013"}, {"id": "school-14-picking-subjects", "uid": 14, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "14", "title": "Picking Subjects", "body": ["Picking subjects can feel way more serious than it actually is.", "Suddenly adults are asking:", "\"What do you want to do when you're older?\"", "And you're like:", "\"I don't even know what I want for dinner.\"", "😭", "You don't need your entire life planned.", "Think about what you actually enjoy", "Not just what you're good at.", "And not just what sounds impressive.", "Ask:", "Do I enjoy this?", "Am I willing to put effort into it?", "Do I like the actual work, not just the idea of it?", "Does it fit possible careers I'm interested in?", "Don't choose based entirely on your friends", "Your friend might be taking a subject because they love it.", "You might hate it.", "And then you're both sitting in the same classroom wondering why you did this.", "Choose for yourself.", "Don't choose something just because it's \"easy\"", "If you genuinely enjoy it, that's different.", "But if you're choosing a subject because you think you can avoid doing anything, you might regret it later.", "Don't let other people's opinions decide", "Someone saying:", "\"That's a useless subject.\"", "doesn't automatically make it useless.", "Different people want different things.", "And if you change your mind?", "People change.", "Your interests can change.", "Your career ideas can change.", "Your plans can change.", "That's normal."], "bigSister": "Choosing subjects matters, but it isn't a contract with your future. You're allowed to learn more about yourself and change direction.", "journal": "Which subjects make me curious enough that I'd actually want to learn more outside of school?", "globalNum": "014"}, {"id": "school-15-not-fitting-in", "uid": 15, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "15", "title": "Not Fitting In", "body": ["There's a difference between:", "\"I haven't found my people yet.\"", "and:", "\"There's something wrong with me.\"", "Please don't confuse the two.", "Maybe everyone around you is obsessed with something you don't care about.", "Maybe your humour is different.", "Maybe you're quieter.", "Maybe you moved somewhere with a completely different culture.", "Maybe you just haven't found people you click with.", "That doesn't mean you're defective.", "Stop trying to win everyone over", "You don't need the whole school to like you.", "You need a few people you can actually relax around.", "That's it.", "Look for people with shared interests", "Clubs.", "Sports.", "Art.", "Gaming.", "Music.", "Volunteering.", "School activities.", "Online communities with appropriate safety boundaries.", "Shared interests make conversation so much easier because you already have something to talk about.", "Don't shrink yourself", "If you constantly edit yourself depending on who's around, you'll eventually get exhausted.", "You don't need to announce every opinion you have.", "But you also don't need to hide everything you enjoy because you're scared someone will think it's weird.", "Sometimes the environment is the problem", "This is worth saying.", "If you genuinely feel like you don't fit into your current environment, that doesn't automatically mean you need to change yourself.", "Sometimes you need a different environment.", "Different people.", "Different activities.", "Different school.", "Don't immediately blame yourself."], "bigSister": "Being different from the people around you isn't automatically a problem. Sometimes you're just in the wrong room.", "journal": "What parts of myself do I hide when I'm around other people, and why?", "globalNum": "015"}, {"id": "school-16-school-gossip", "uid": 16, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "16", "title": "School Gossip", "body": ["School gossip spreads at terrifying speed.", "You tell one person something.", "Suddenly five people know.", "And somehow the story has changed completely.", "If you're involved in gossip, your first instinct might be to defend yourself immediately.", "Sometimes that's necessary.", "Sometimes the best response is actually to give it nothing.", "Figure out what kind of gossip it is", "Is it harmless?", "Someone saying you like a certain song?", "Whatever.", "Is it embarrassing but unimportant?", "Maybe ignore it.", "Is someone spreading lies, private information, sexual rumors, or trying to damage your reputation?", "That's more serious.", "Save screenshots if it's online.", "Write down what happened.", "Tell a trusted adult if it continues or becomes harassment.", "Don't fight rumors with more rumors", "If someone says:", "\"Apparently you did this.\"", "Don't respond:", "\"Well SHE did this.\"", "Now you're both spreading things.", "Instead:", "\"That's not true.\"", "Then stop.", "You don't need to write a five-page defence.", "Be careful who you trust", "This doesn't mean becoming paranoid.", "Just don't tell someone you've known for three days every private detail of your life.", "Trust is built."], "bigSister": "You cannot control everything people say about you. You can control what you participate in. Protect your peace and your privacy.", "journal": "Is there something I need to clear up, or am I giving attention to something that will disappear on its own?", "globalNum": "016"}, {"id": "school-17-school-drama", "uid": 17, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "17", "title": "School Drama", "body": ["School drama can feel like the entire world when you're inside it.", "Someone's mad at someone.", "Someone's dating someone's ex.", "Someone screenshotted something.", "Someone is crying in the bathroom.", "And suddenly your whole lunch period is a live episode of a reality show nobody asked for.", "Here's the thing:", "You don't have to participate in everything.", "Ask yourself one question", "\"Does this actually involve me?\"", "If no...", "You can simply stay out of it.", "You don't need to choose a side.", "You don't need to forward screenshots.", "You don't need to investigate.", "If your friend is involved", "Listen to them.", "You can support someone without automatically agreeing with everything they did.", "Try:", "\"I get why you're upset.\"", "instead of:", "\"You're definitely right and they're horrible.\"", "Sometimes people need someone to listen, not someone to help them escalate the situation.", "Don't react while angry", "If you're furious, don't immediately send the paragraph.", "Write it.", "Read it.", "Wait.", "Then decide whether it actually needs to be sent.", "Because once you've sent something, you can't unsend the screenshot someone already took.", "Know when it's serious", "Bullying, threats, harassment, sexual rumors, stalking, or anything that makes someone feel unsafe isn't just \"school drama.\"", "Get an adult involved."], "bigSister": "Peace can look boring from the outside. That's okay. You don't need a new crisis every Tuesday to have an interesting life.", "journal": "Is this something I need to solve, support someone through, or simply stay out of?", "globalNum": "017"}, {"id": "school-18-bullying", "uid": 18, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "18", "title": "Bullying", "body": ["Let's be really clear about this one.", "Bullying isn't:", "\"Someone didn't like me.\"", "It can involve repeated insults, humiliation, threats, exclusion, harassment, physical aggression, or targeting someone because of something about them.", "And if it's happening to you, it is not your fault.", "Don't blame yourself", "You didn't cause someone else's decision to treat you badly.", "You don't need to become funnier, prettier, quieter, louder, or more popular to deserve respect.", "Tell someone", "I know.", "You might be thinking:", "\"But they'll make it worse.\"", "Or:", "\"They're going to call me a snitch.\"", "Tell someone anyway.", "A parent.", "Guardian.", "Teacher.", "Counselor.", "Head of year.", "Another adult you trust.", "If the first person doesn't take it seriously, tell someone else.", "Keep telling people until someone helps.", "Save evidence", "If it's happening online, take screenshots.", "Don't delete everything immediately.", "If there are dates, messages, usernames, or posts involved, keep records.", "Don't put yourself in danger trying to prove something", "You don't need to fight someone.", "You don't need to meet them alone.", "You don't need to \"get revenge.\"", "Your safety matters more than winning an argument.", "If you're watching it happen", "You don't have to become the hero of the school.", "But you can avoid joining in.", "Don't laugh.", "Don't share the video.", "Don't add comments.", "If it's safe, check on the person afterwards.", "And tell an adult if someone is genuinely being targeted."], "bigSister": "Asking for help isn't weak. You shouldn't have to handle repeated cruelty by yourself.", "journal": "Who is one adult I could talk to if school ever stopped feeling safe?", "globalNum": "018"}, {"id": "school-19-cyberbullying", "uid": 19, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "19", "title": "Cyberbullying", "body": ["Online bullying can feel even worse because there's no real \"school day ending.\"", "You go home.", "Your phone is still there.", "You open an app.", "There it is again.", "A comment.", "A screenshot.", "A group chat.", "A rumor.", "Don't argue with the bully", "I know you want to.", "You want to type the perfect comeback that destroys them so badly they delete their account.", "Don't build your whole night around winning an argument with someone who is trying to upset you.", "Block and report", "Use the platform's blocking and reporting tools.", "If the behavior is serious, threatening, or persistent, save evidence before deleting or blocking where possible.", "Tell an adult", "Especially if someone is threatening you, sharing private information, impersonating you, blackmailing you, sharing sexual content involving you, or repeatedly targeting you.", "That's not something you should have to solve alone.", "Protect your accounts", "Check:", "Who can message you", "Who can comment", "Who can see your stories", "Location sharing", "Tagged posts", "Password security", "Two-factor authentication", "And don't share passwords with friends.", "Even your best friend.", "Don't retaliate", "Posting their private information because they posted yours can turn one person's bad behaviour into a situation involving both of you.", "Protect yourself instead."], "bigSister": "The fact that something happens through a screen doesn't make it less real. If it's hurting you, it's worth taking seriously.", "journal": "What could I change about my online boundaries that would make me feel safer?", "globalNum": "019"}, {"id": "school-20-graduation-anxiety", "uid": 20, "category": "school", "categoryLabel": "School", "num": "20", "title": "Graduation Anxiety", "body": ["Graduation is supposed to be exciting.", "So why does everyone suddenly start asking:", "\"What's next?\"", "And you're standing there thinking:", "\"I literally don't know.\"", "Maybe you're scared of leaving your friends.", "Maybe you're scared you'll choose the wrong career.", "Maybe you're worried everyone else has their life figured out.", "Maybe you're just sad that a chapter is ending.", "All of that is normal.", "You don't need the perfect plan", "You need a next step.", "That's different.", "You might know what you want to study.", "Great.", "You might have absolutely no idea.", "Also okay.", "You can research.", "Try things.", "Talk to people.", "Take time to figure out what you actually like.", "Friendships will change", "Some friendships will stay.", "Some will become long-distance.", "Some will fade.", "That doesn't automatically mean they weren't real.", "People grow in different directions.", "Let yourself be sad", "You can be excited and sad at the same time.", "Graduation is literally an ending.", "Of course it feels weird.", "Take pictures.", "Save messages.", "Have the stupid little traditions.", "Say goodbye properly.", "Don't spend the whole day worrying about the future and forget that you're currently living the moment you've been waiting years to reach."], "bigSister": "You don't need to know your entire life on graduation day. You just need to take the next step. Then another. Then another. You'll figure out more as you go.", "journal": "If I stopped worrying about having the \"right\" future, what would I actually want to try next?", "globalNum": "020"}, {"id": "friends-21-losing-a-best-friend", "uid": 21, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "21", "title": "Losing a Best Friend", "body": ["Losing a best friend is honestly a different kind of hurt.", "Because it's not just:", "\"Oh, we don't talk anymore.\"", "It's losing the person you used to tell everything to.", "The person who knew the random story behind that one photo.", "The person you expected to be there tomorrow.", "And suddenly you're supposed to act normal while your entire routine feels weird.", "First, don't immediately blame yourself", "You might replay everything.", "\"Was I too annoying?\"", "\"Should I have replied differently?\"", "\"What if I had just apologized?\"", "Sometimes you did something wrong.", "Sometimes they did.", "Sometimes both of you did.", "And sometimes a friendship just changes.", "You don't have to turn yourself into the villain just because it ended.", "If you had an argument", "Give both of you some time to cool down.", "Then, if you genuinely want to fix things, talk.", "Not through a 46-message paragraph at 1:13 a.m.", "Actually talk.", "You can say:", "\"I don't like how things ended between us. If you're willing, I'd like to talk about it.\"", "That's enough.", "You don't need to beg.", "What if they don't want to fix it?", "This is the part nobody likes.", "You have to respect that.", "You can miss someone without chasing them.", "You can wish things were different without forcing them to become different.", "And yes, you're allowed to cry about it.", "You're allowed to be angry.", "You're allowed to miss them even if you know the friendship wasn't good for you anymore.", "Don't immediately replace them", "You don't need to find a new \"best friend\" just to fill the empty space.", "Take your time.", "Talk to different people.", "Let new friendships develop naturally.", "Be careful with old memories", "Sometimes you'll look through old photos and suddenly think:", "\"Maybe it wasn't that bad.\"", "You might only be remembering the good parts.", "Remember the whole friendship.", "Not just the highlights."], "bigSister": "Losing a friendship doesn't mean you failed at friendship. Some people are part of your life for years. Some are there for one chapter. Both can matter.", "journal": "What do I miss about this person specifically, and what do I not miss about the friendship?", "globalNum": "021"}, {"id": "friends-22-fake-friends", "uid": 22, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "22", "title": "Fake Friends", "body": ["\"Fake friend\" gets thrown around a LOT.", "Someone doesn't reply once and suddenly:", "FAKE FRIEND 😡", "Let's not do that.", "People have bad days.", "People get busy.", "People misunderstand things.", "But there are actual patterns that should make you pause.", "Watch how you feel around them", "Do you constantly feel like you're walking on eggshells?", "Do you feel like you have to compete with them?", "Do they embarrass you in front of people and call it a joke?", "Do they only talk to you when they need something?", "Do they disappear when you need them?", "Do they tell you private things other people said?", "If you constantly feel worse after being around someone, pay attention.", "Friendship isn't supposed to be a transaction", "You shouldn't have to constantly prove your usefulness.", "You don't need to buy things for someone.", "Do their homework.", "Give them attention 24/7.", "Or agree with everything they say just to keep them around.", "But don't label someone \"fake\" over one mistake", "People mess up.", "The question is what happens after.", "Do they listen?", "Do they apologize?", "Do they change?", "That's more important than whether they made one mistake."], "bigSister": "A bad friend isn't always an evil mastermind. Sometimes they're just someone who isn't capable of being the kind of friend you need.", "journal": "Do I feel respected, safe, and comfortable around this person most of the time?", "globalNum": "022"}, {"id": "friends-23-jealous-friends", "uid": 23, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "23", "title": "Jealous Friends", "body": ["A little jealousy is normal.", "If your best friend gets something you've wanted forever, you might feel jealous for a second.", "That doesn't make you a bad person.", "The problem is what someone does with that feeling.", "Healthy jealousy sounds like:", "\"Ugh, I'm jealous because I wanted that too, but I'm happy for you.\"", "Unhealthy jealousy looks more like:", "\"You only got that because you're lucky.\"", "\"Why are you hanging out with them?\"", "\"You don't need to be friends with her.\"", "\"You think you're better than me now?\"", "That's different.", "You don't have to make yourself smaller", "If you're doing well, you don't need to hide it because your friend might feel bad.", "You can be excited.", "You can celebrate your achievements.", "You can make new friends.", "You can have other interests.", "A friendship shouldn't require you to stay at the same level forever.", "If you're the jealous one", "Be honest with yourself.", "Ask:", "\"Am I actually angry at them, or am I disappointed in myself?\"", "Sometimes jealousy is pointing at something you want.", "Use it as information.", "If your friend gets an amazing grade and you're jealous, maybe you want to improve your own grades.", "If they make new friends and you're jealous, maybe you're feeling insecure about your friendship.", "Figure out the actual feeling underneath it."], "bigSister": "Your friend's success isn't evidence that you're failing. Two people can win at the same time.", "journal": "What is this jealousy actually telling me that I want?", "globalNum": "023"}, {"id": "friends-24-toxic-friendships", "uid": 24, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "24", "title": "Toxic Friendships", "body": ["Not every difficult friendship is toxic.", "People argue.", "Friends get annoyed.", "People make mistakes.", "That's normal.", "A friendship becomes concerning when the unhealthy behaviour becomes a pattern.", "Maybe they constantly manipulate you.", "Maybe they threaten to stop being your friend if you don't do what they want.", "Maybe they embarrass you.", "Maybe they control who you're allowed to talk to.", "Maybe they make you feel guilty whenever you have plans without them.", "Maybe you're constantly scared they'll get angry.", "That's not healthy.", "Ask yourself:", "Can I say no?", "If you can't say no without being punished, that's a problem.", "Can I disagree?", "You shouldn't have to agree with everything to keep the friendship.", "Can I have other friends?", "You are allowed to have more than one friendship.", "Can I be myself?", "You shouldn't feel like you're performing constantly.", "Leaving doesn't have to be dramatic", "You don't need a public announcement.", "You can create distance.", "Reply less.", "Stop sharing personal information.", "Spend time with other people.", "Set boundaries.", "If the person is threatening you or making you feel unsafe, get a trusted adult involved."], "bigSister": "Missing someone doesn't automatically mean you should go back to them. You can love someone and still realize they're not good for you.", "journal": "If my friend described this exact friendship to me, what advice would I give them?", "globalNum": "024"}, {"id": "friends-25-feeling-replaced", "uid": 25, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "25", "title": "Feeling Replaced", "body": ["Your best friend gets a new friend.", "And suddenly you're thinking:", "\"So I'm basically obsolete now?\"", "😭", "It hurts because it can feel like you've been traded in.", "But someone gaining another friend doesn't automatically mean they've stopped caring about you.", "Friendships aren't usually a one-seat bus.", "There can be room for more people.", "Don't compete", "Please don't start trying to \"win\" your friend back.", "Don't become louder.", "Don't insult the new person.", "Don't suddenly buy them things.", "Don't create a secret campaign to prove you're the better friend.", "You're not in a competition.", "Talk to your friend", "If they've genuinely been distant, you can say:", "\"I've felt like we've been a little distant lately. Is everything okay?\"", "That's much healthier than silently becoming resentful.", "Build your own world too", "This is important.", "If your entire social life depends on one person, any change in that friendship will feel enormous.", "Have your own hobbies.", "Talk to other people.", "Make your own plans.", "Your friend having another friend shouldn't leave you with nobody."], "bigSister": "Being loved isn't about being someone's only friend. You don't have to be irreplaceable to be important.", "journal": "Am I actually being pushed away, or am I scared that I could be?", "globalNum": "025"}, {"id": "friends-26-making-friends", "uid": 26, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "26", "title": "Making Friends", "body": ["Okay, making friends sounds easy until you're actually standing next to someone thinking:", "\"So... you exist. I exist. Now what?\"", "😭", "The good news is you don't need amazing social skills.", "You need repetition.", "Start small", "Talk to the same people regularly.", "Say hi.", "Ask about homework.", "Compliment something.", "Make a joke.", "Sit near them.", "Friendship gets easier when you keep seeing someone.", "Ask questions", "People usually like people who make them feel interesting.", "Try:", "\"What music do you listen to?\"", "\"Do you watch anything good?\"", "\"What's your favourite subject?\"", "\"What are you doing after school?\"", "But don't turn it into an interview.", "Share things about yourself too.", "Find shared interests", "If you love football, join something football-related.", "If you like art, find art people.", "If you like gaming, talk to people who game.", "It's much easier to connect when you already have something in common.", "Don't chase people who clearly aren't interested", "You can make an effort.", "You shouldn't have to beg.", "If someone repeatedly gives you one-word answers, avoids you, or makes it obvious they don't want to talk, leave it.", "There are other people.", "Be the person you want to meet", "Be welcoming.", "Include people.", "Remember names.", "Ask someone how their test went.", "You'd be surprised how much tiny kindness matters."], "bigSister": "You don't need to become \"cooler\" to make friends. You need to find people who actually like the version of you that already exists.", "journal": "What kind of friend do I want to be to other people?", "globalNum": "026"}, {"id": "friends-27-being-ignored", "uid": 27, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "27", "title": "Being Ignored", "body": ["Being ignored is frustrating because you don't know what you're supposed to do with it.", "Did they miss the message?", "Are they mad?", "Are they busy?", "Are they purposely ignoring you?", "Your brain wants an answer immediately.", "Unfortunately, you might not have one.", "Don't send 14 messages", "Please.", "If you've already said:", "\"Hey\"", "and then:", "\"Are you okay?\"", "and then:", "\"Did I do something?\"", "Stop.", "Give them space.", "Look at the pattern", "One unanswered message?", "Probably nothing.", "They've been ignoring you for weeks while talking normally to everyone else?", "That's worth paying attention to.", "If it's a close friend", "Ask directly.", "\"Hey, I feel like you've been distant lately. Did I do something?\"", "You might get an actual explanation.", "Maybe they're upset.", "Maybe something happened in their life.", "Maybe nothing is wrong.", "At least you'll know.", "Don't beg for attention", "You shouldn't have to keep proving that you're worth replying to.", "If someone repeatedly chooses not to communicate with you, you can step back too."], "bigSister": "You can give someone space without spending the entire time staring at your phone waiting for them.", "journal": "What do I actually know about this situation, and what am I assuming?", "globalNum": "027"}, {"id": "friends-28-friendship-breakups", "uid": 28, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "28", "title": "Friendship Breakups", "body": ["Friendship breakups are weird because nobody gives you a card.", "There's no official ceremony.", "You just stop talking.", "And then you're expected to continue your normal life.", "But losing a friendship can genuinely hurt.", "Don't force yourself to hate them", "Sometimes people try to make themselves angry because anger feels easier than missing someone.", "You don't need to.", "You can say:", "\"That friendship mattered to me, and it still wasn't working anymore.\"", "Both can be true.", "If you need closure", "You might want one final conversation.", "That's okay.", "But closure doesn't always come from the other person.", "Sometimes they won't explain themselves.", "Sometimes their explanation won't make sense.", "Sometimes you just have to accept that you know enough.", "Don't turn the breakup into school entertainment", "You don't need everyone choosing sides.", "Don't post screenshots.", "Don't make indirect TikToks.", "Don't tell everyone every private thing they ever told you.", "Protect their privacy even if the friendship ended badly.", "Start filling the empty spaces", "If you used to text them every evening, that silence is going to feel strange.", "Make new routines.", "Talk to other people.", "Read.", "Go outside.", "Work on something.", "Not to \"replace\" them.", "Just to build a life that doesn't stop because one friendship did."], "bigSister": "A friendship ending doesn't erase everything good that happened during it.", "journal": "What did this friendship teach me about what I want—and don't want—in future friendships?", "globalNum": "028"}, {"id": "friends-29-setting-boundaries-with-friends", "uid": 29, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "29", "title": "Setting Boundaries With Friends", "body": ["Boundaries are basically rules for how you expect to be treated.", "And no, having boundaries doesn't mean becoming cold.", "It means being clear.", "Examples", "\"I don't like when you joke about that.\"", "\"I can't hang out today.\"", "\"Please don't share that.\"", "\"I don't want to talk about this right now.\"", "\"I need some time alone.\"", "You don't need a five-minute explanation every time you say no.", "The scary part", "Someone might get annoyed.", "That's okay.", "A boundary isn't really a boundary if you only keep it when everyone agrees with it.", "But be reasonable", "A boundary isn't:", "\"You aren't allowed to have other friends.\"", "That's control.", "A boundary is:", "\"If you keep insulting me, I'm going to leave the conversation.\"", "That's about your actions.", "Watch how people respond", "Good friends might not love every boundary, but they'll usually respect it.", "If someone constantly mocks your boundaries, guilt-trips you, or punishes you for having them, that's important information."], "bigSister": "Saying no doesn't make you mean. The right people won't require you to abandon yourself to keep them happy.", "journal": "Where do I say yes even when I really want to say no?", "globalNum": "029"}, {"id": "friends-30-friends-changing", "uid": 30, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "30", "title": "Friends Changing", "body": ["Sometimes you wake up one day and realize your friend isn't really the same person you met.", "Or maybe you're not.", "Different hobbies.", "Different priorities.", "Different personalities.", "Different friend groups.", "It can feel like you're losing someone even though they're still right there.", "Don't panic immediately", "People are allowed to change.", "Maybe your friend is trying something new.", "Maybe they're meeting new people.", "Maybe they're growing into a different version of themselves.", "You don't need to stay exactly the same to remain friends.", "But sometimes you grow apart", "And that's sad.", "Maybe you don't have anything to talk about anymore.", "Maybe being together feels forced.", "Maybe you're constantly trying to recreate the friendship you had two years ago.", "You can't always do that.", "Don't force old chemistry", "Sometimes the healthiest thing is letting a friendship become less intense.", "You don't have to turn every friendship into a dramatic breakup.", "Some friendships can simply become:", "\"We don't talk every day anymore, but I still care about you.\"", "That's okay.", "Keep growing too", "Don't freeze yourself because you're scared your friends won't like the new version of you.", "Try things.", "Meet people.", "Change your style.", "Discover new interests.", "You're allowed to evolve."], "bigSister": "Growing apart doesn't always mean someone did something wrong. Sometimes you're just becoming different people.", "journal": "Do I miss this person as they are now, or do I miss who we used to be?", "globalNum": "030"}, {"id": "friends-31-long-distance-friends", "uid": 31, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "31", "title": "Long-Distance Friends", "body": ["Having a friend who lives far away is weird because nothing is technically wrong...", "You just can't casually say:", "\"Wanna hang out?\"", "because they're approximately 700 business miles away 😭.", "Maybe you moved.", "Maybe they moved.", "Maybe you met online.", "Whatever the reason, distance can make a friendship feel different.", "And yes, sometimes it will change.", "Don't measure the friendship by how often you talk", "You might talk every day for a while.", "Then suddenly it's once a week.", "Then you disappear for two weeks because school is insane.", "That doesn't automatically mean the friendship is over.", "Some friendships are good at picking up exactly where they left off.", "Actually make plans", "\"OMG we need to call soon\" doesn't count.", "Pick a day.", "Even if it's just a 30-minute call.", "Watch a movie together.", "Play a game.", "Send each other photos from your day.", "Have a shared playlist.", "Find little ways to still be part of each other's lives.", "Don't panic if they make new friends", "They're allowed to have a life where they are.", "And so are you.", "You don't need to constantly prove that you're still best friends.", "And be realistic", "Sometimes long-distance friendships fade.", "It hurts, but it doesn't mean the friendship wasn't real.", "You don't have to hold onto something forever just because it used to matter."], "bigSister": "Distance can change a friendship without destroying it. The friendships that last usually learn how to exist differently.", "journal": "What is one small thing I could do this week to feel closer to a friend who lives far away?", "globalNum": "031"}, {"id": "friends-32-online-friends", "uid": 32, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "32", "title": "Online Friends", "body": ["Online friendships can be real friendships.", "You can genuinely care about someone you've never met in person.", "But because you've met them online, you also need to be a little more careful.", "Don't assume someone is who they say they are", "A profile picture is not proof of identity.", "Neither is a voice call.", "Don't send someone private information just because you've talked to them for months.", "Especially:", "Your home address", "Your school", "Your daily location", "Passwords", "Private photos", "Financial information", "Information about your family", "Be careful with photos", "If someone pressures you for private or sexual pictures, you do not owe them anything.", "Even if they say:", "\"If you trusted me, you would.\"", "That's manipulation.", "Don't send it.", "If someone threatens you over pictures or says they'll share something unless you do what they want, tell a trusted adult and report the account. Don't negotiate with them alone.", "Don't meet an online friend secretly", "If you ever meet someone you've known online in real life, a trusted adult should know and be involved.", "Don't go alone.", "Don't hide it from your family because you're worried they'll say no.", "Your safety matters more than keeping the friendship secret.", "You can still have fun", "Play games.", "Talk about music.", "Send memes.", "Watch shows.", "Just remember that being comfortable with someone doesn't mean you have to give them access to every part of your life."], "bigSister": "You can trust someone slowly. You don't have to choose between \"trust everyone\" and \"trust nobody.\"", "journal": "What information about myself do I keep private online?", "globalNum": "032"}, {"id": "friends-33-trust-issues", "uid": 33, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "33", "title": "Trust Issues", "body": ["Someone broke your trust once.", "Now your brain is like:", "\"Never again.\"", "Understandable.", "But there's a difference between being careful and assuming everyone will hurt you.", "Ask what actually happened", "If someone betrayed you, think about the specific behaviour.", "Did they lie?", "Share something private?", "Break a promise?", "Talk behind your back?", "Once you know what happened, you can figure out what you need to protect yourself from.", "Don't punish new people for old people's mistakes", "Your new friend isn't automatically going to behave like your old friend.", "Give them the opportunity to show you who they are.", "Not unlimited chances.", "Just an opportunity.", "Trust can be gradual", "You don't have to tell someone your deepest secrets immediately.", "Start small.", "See how they handle small things.", "Do they keep things private?", "Do they respect your boundaries?", "Do their actions match what they say?", "Over time, you'll have more information.", "And trust yourself too", "Sometimes people focus so much on:", "\"Can I trust them?\"", "that they forget:", "\"Can I trust myself to leave if something feels wrong?\"", "You don't need to predict everything.", "You need to know you can protect yourself."], "bigSister": "Trust isn't something you owe someone immediately. It's something people build with consistent behaviour.", "journal": "What would someone have to consistently do for me to feel safe trusting them?", "globalNum": "033"}, {"id": "friends-34-being-left-on-read", "uid": 34, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "34", "title": "Being Left on Read", "body": ["You sent the message.", "They saw it.", "Nothing.", "You check again.", "Still nothing.", "You check their status.", "Active.", "They posted a story.", "Active again.", "And now you're conducting a full FBI investigation 😭.", "Relax.", "Sometimes people just don't know what to say", "Or they're busy.", "Or they opened the message while doing something else and forgot.", "Or they saw it and thought:", "\"I'll reply later.\"", "Then three hours disappeared.", "It happens.", "Don't immediately double-text angrily", "Especially not:", "\"Okay.\"", "\"Wow.\"", "\"Never mind.\"", "\"Forget it.\"", "If it's genuinely important, send a normal follow-up later.", "Look at the pattern", "If they occasionally leave you on read, whatever.", "If they're consistently ignoring you while expecting instant replies from you, that's different.", "Don't make your self-worth depend on replies", "Someone taking six hours to respond doesn't tell you how interesting, pretty, funny, or valuable you are.", "It tells you they haven't replied for six hours.", "That's literally it."], "bigSister": "Your phone is not a mood detector. Don't let a little \"seen\" message decide how you feel about yourself.", "journal": "What story am I telling myself about being left on read, and do I actually have evidence for it?", "globalNum": "034"}, {"id": "friends-35-feeling-like-the-backup-friend", "uid": 35, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "35", "title": "Feeling Like the Backup Friend", "body": ["This one hurts because you can feel it.", "You're invited when someone else can't come.", "You're the person people text when everyone else is busy.", "You're always available.", "They're not.", "And eventually you're wondering:", "\"Am I actually their friend, or am I just convenient?\"", "Pay attention to patterns", "Ask:", "Who starts conversations?", "Who makes plans?", "Who checks in?", "Who remembers things about you?", "Who shows up when you're having a bad day?", "Friendship doesn't have to be perfectly 50/50 every single day.", "But if it's always you giving and them taking, that's worth noticing.", "Stop making yourself permanently available", "You don't have to answer immediately every time.", "You don't have to cancel your plans because someone suddenly remembered you exist.", "You don't have to say yes because you're scared they'll stop asking.", "Have your own life.", "Make other connections", "This is probably the best way to stop feeling like someone's backup.", "Don't put your entire social life in one person's hands.", "Talk to other people.", "Make plans.", "Join things.", "Find people who are excited to have you around.", "And if you want to address it?", "You can.", "\"Sometimes I feel like I'm only included when other people aren't available.\"", "That's vulnerable, but honest.", "Their reaction will tell you something."], "bigSister": "You don't have to fight for a place in someone's life that they're constantly making you earn.", "journal": "What would a friendship where I feel genuinely chosen look like?", "globalNum": "035"}, {"id": "friends-36-fomo", "uid": 36, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "36", "title": "FOMO", "body": ["FOMO is basically your brain saying:", "\"Everyone is having the best time without me.\"", "Meanwhile you're in bed eating cereal watching YouTube.", "And somehow you feel like you've missed the most important event in human history.", "😭", "Remember that you're seeing the highlight reel", "You see the pictures.", "You don't see:", "The awkward parts.", "The arguments.", "The boring ten minutes.", "The person who wanted to go home.", "The fact that half the group was scrolling on their phones.", "You see the best five seconds.", "Ask yourself what you're actually missing", "Do you genuinely want to go?", "Or do you just hate the idea of other people having fun without you?", "Those are different.", "If you actually wanted to go, maybe make plans next time.", "If you don't even like the activity, why are you upset?", "Don't ruin your own day", "If you're already having fun, don't spend the entire time checking what everyone else is doing.", "Put the phone down.", "Be where you are.", "You will miss things", "This is the annoying truth.", "You can't attend everything.", "You can't be everywhere.", "You can't be invited to everything.", "And that's okay.", "Missing one party doesn't mean you missed your entire teenage experience."], "bigSister": "You are allowed to have a life that isn't happening on your screen.", "journal": "Do I actually want what they have, or do I just want to know I wasn't excluded?", "globalNum": "036"}, {"id": "friends-37-dealing-with-rumors", "uid": 37, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "37", "title": "Dealing With Rumors", "body": ["Someone tells you:", "\"Apparently people are saying...\"", "And now you have 17 questions.", "Who said it?", "Why?", "How many people know?", "Is it true?", "Should you confront them?", "First: don't panic.", "Find out what you actually know", "There's a huge difference between:", "\"Someone said something about you.\"", "and:", "\"I know exactly what was said, who said it, and where it came from.\"", "Don't react to a vague rumor as if it's confirmed.", "If it's false", "You can correct it simply.", "\"That's not true.\"", "You don't necessarily need to publish a full explanation.", "If it's private information", "You don't owe everyone a response.", "If someone is spreading personal information about you, especially sexual or humiliating rumours, tell a trusted adult.", "Save evidence if it's online.", "Don't spread the rumor further", "Even if you're telling people:", "\"I can't believe they're saying this about me!\"", "you're still introducing the rumor to more people.", "Tell the people who genuinely need to know.", "Not the entire school.", "Don't retaliate", "If someone spreads a rumor about you, don't dig up something embarrassing about them and spread it back.", "Now you've created two problems."], "bigSister": "You don't need to convince every person in the building that a rumor is false. Protect yourself, correct what matters, and don't feed the gossip machine.", "journal": "What part of this situation is actually within my control?", "globalNum": "037"}, {"id": "friends-38-peer-pressure", "uid": 38, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "38", "title": "Peer Pressure", "body": ["Peer pressure isn't always someone literally saying:", "\"DO IT OR YOU'RE NOT COOL.\"", "Sometimes it's way quieter.", "Everyone's doing something.", "You don't really want to.", "But you don't want to be the boring one.", "So you go along with it.", "Here's the thing", "You are allowed to change your mind.", "Even if you said yes earlier.", "Even if everyone else is doing it.", "Even if someone says:", "\"Come onnn.\"", "Your answer can still be no.", "Have an exit line", "If you don't want to explain everything, keep it simple:", "\"Nah, I'm good.\"", "\"I'm not doing that.\"", "\"I don't want to.\"", "\"I'm leaving.\"", "You don't need a courtroom argument.", "If you're worried about looking uncool", "Real friends won't make your boundaries the price of staying in the group.", "Someone saying:", "\"You're scared.\"", "doesn't magically make something safe.", "And someone saying:", "\"Everyone does it.\"", "doesn't make it a good idea.", "Get yourself out if you need to", "If you feel unsafe, leave.", "Call someone you trust.", "Go somewhere with adults around.", "You don't need to stay because you're embarrassed about changing your mind."], "bigSister": "Being confident isn't always saying yes. Sometimes it's being willing to be the only person saying no.", "journal": "What situations make it hardest for me to say no?", "globalNum": "038"}, {"id": "friends-39-saying-no-without-feeling-guilty", "uid": 39, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "39", "title": "Saying No Without Feeling Guilty", "body": ["You said no.", "Then immediately:", "\"Wait... was I mean?\"", "No 😭.", "You're allowed to have limits.", "You don't need a giant explanation", "Try:", "\"I can't today.\"", "\"I'm not comfortable with that.\"", "\"No, thank you.\"", "\"I already have plans.\"", "And leave it there.", "But what if they get upset?", "Someone being disappointed doesn't automatically mean you did something wrong.", "People are allowed to feel disappointed.", "You're allowed to say no.", "Both can happen at the same time.", "Don't lie constantly just to avoid saying no", "You don't need a fake excuse every time.", "If you don't want to go somewhere, you can simply say you don't want to.", "You don't owe everyone access to your time.", "Remember that your time belongs to you", "You can spend it resting.", "Studying.", "With family.", "With another friend.", "Doing absolutely nothing.", "You don't need to be useful every second."], "bigSister": "\"No\" is a complete sentence, but you can still say it kindly.", "journal": "Where in my life do I feel like I have to say yes to keep people happy?", "globalNum": "039"}, {"id": "friends-40-outgrowing-friendships", "uid": 40, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "40", "title": "Outgrowing Friendships", "body": ["This one is complicated because nobody necessarily did anything wrong.", "You just...", "changed.", "Maybe you used to talk every day.", "Now you barely have anything to say.", "Maybe your interests are completely different.", "Maybe the friendship feels forced.", "Maybe you don't like who you are around them anymore.", "Don't panic because the friendship changed", "You're growing.", "They're growing.", "Neither of you is going to stay exactly the same forever.", "Ask yourself whether you're holding on because you still want the friendship", "Or because you're scared of losing it.", "Those are very different reasons.", "You don't always need a dramatic ending", "Sometimes you can let the friendship become less close naturally.", "You don't have to announce:", "\"I AM OFFICIALLY ENDING OUR FRIENDSHIP.\"", "😭", "You can simply stop forcing conversations.", "Spend more time with people you connect with now.", "Stay kind.", "Keep your memories.", "Move forward.", "But if you want to stay friends?", "Talk about it.", "Maybe the friendship just needs to change.", "You don't have to recreate the exact friendship you had at 11 when you're 15.", "You can build a new version.", "Don't feel guilty for growing", "You're allowed to become someone your younger self wouldn't recognize.", "You're allowed to discover new interests.", "You're allowed to want different things.", "You're allowed to choose people who make you feel comfortable being yourself."], "bigSister": "Outgrowing someone doesn't mean you never cared about them. Sometimes caring about someone and continuing to be close to them are two different things.", "journal": "Am I trying to save this friendship because I still love it, or because I'm afraid of what happens without it?", "globalNum": "040"}, {"id": "friends-51-when-your-friend-is-always-cancelling-plans", "uid": 41, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "51", "title": "When Your Friend Is Always Cancelling Plans", "body": ["There are two kinds of cancelling.", "\"I'm so sorry, something came up.\"", "And:", "\"Sorryyy can't come.\"", "for the fifth time in a row.", "Yeah. Those are not the same.", "Don't immediately assume they don't care", "People genuinely get busy.", "Family stuff happens.", "School happens.", "Plans change.", "But if someone repeatedly cancels on you and never tries to make another plan, that's when I'd start paying attention.", "Because the issue isn't really the cancelled plan.", "It's the lack of effort afterwards.", "Look for the pattern", "Do they say:", "\"Can we do Saturday instead?\"", "Or do they just disappear?", "Do they ever make plans with you?", "Do they show up for other people but constantly cancel on you?", "Those details matter.", "Don't keep chasing", "If you've suggested plans three times and they've cancelled three times, stop.", "Not as revenge.", "Just stop putting all the effort into something that's supposed to involve two people.", "Let them reach out.", "If they're a good friend otherwise", "Talk about it.", "\"I've noticed we've had plans cancelled a lot lately. Is everything okay?\"", "Maybe there's something going on that you don't know about."], "bigSister": "One cancelled plan means nothing. A pattern of cancelled plans with zero effort to reconnect tells you a lot.", "journal": "Is this friendship actually becoming one-sided, or am I reacting to one disappointing situation?", "globalNum": "041"}, {"id": "friends-52-when-your-friend-excludes-you-from-the-group-chat", "uid": 42, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "52", "title": "When Your Friend Excludes You From the Group Chat", "body": ["You find out there's another group chat.", "And apparently everyone is in it.", "Except you.", "Ouch.", "Especially when someone accidentally mentions something from the chat and you're sitting there like:", "\"Interesting...\"", "Don't immediately start a war", "You might want to ask:", "\"WHY AM I NOT IN THE GROUP CHAT?\"", "But first, figure out what the chat actually is.", "Sometimes there are smaller chats for specific plans.", "Sometimes someone genuinely forgot.", "Sometimes it's an old chat that became active again.", "And sometimes...", "Yeah, they intentionally left you out.", "If it bothers you, ask", "You can keep it casual:", "\"Wait, is there another group chat? I didn't know 😭.\"", "Their response will tell you something.", "If they say:", "\"OMG we literally forgot to add you.\"", "Cool.", "If they get weird or make excuses, pay attention.", "Don't beg for access", "If people intentionally don't want you in a particular chat, you don't need to campaign for membership.", "That doesn't mean you're unlikeable.", "It means that group chat isn't your space.", "Find your people", "If you're constantly trying to get accepted into one particular group, you might be overlooking people who would actually be happy to have you around."], "bigSister": "Being excluded from a group chat can hurt, but don't let a notification decide your entire social worth.", "journal": "Do I actually want to be part of this group, or do I just hate being excluded?", "globalNum": "042"}, {"id": "friends-53-when-your-friend-makes-everything-about-them", "uid": 43, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "53", "title": "When Your Friend Makes Everything About Them", "body": ["You tell them:", "\"I had such a horrible day.\"", "And somehow five minutes later you're listening to a 20-minute story about their problem.", "You talk about your achievement.", "They immediately tell you theirs.", "You share something exciting.", "They one-up you.", "It's exhausting.", "Friendship should have room for both people", "You don't need every conversation to be perfectly equal.", "Sometimes one person needs more support.", "That's normal.", "But if you never feel heard, that's different.", "Try changing the conversation", "If you tell them something and they immediately switch topics, bring it back.", "\"Wait, can I finish telling you what happened?\"", "Simple.", "They might not even realize they're doing it.", "If they constantly compete", "You can stop feeding the competition.", "You don't have to prove whose grades are better.", "Whose outfit is better.", "Whose relationship is better.", "Whose life is more exciting.", "You're friends.", "Not contestants on some weird reality show."], "bigSister": "You deserve friendships where someone asks: \"Okay, but how are YOU?\" and actually waits for the answer.", "journal": "When I talk to my friends, do I feel listened to?", "globalNum": "043"}, {"id": "friends-54-when-your-friend-gets-mad-when-you-hang-out-with-other-people", "uid": 44, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "54", "title": "When Your Friend Gets Mad When You Hang Out With Other People", "body": ["You make plans with someone else.", "Your friend finds out.", "Suddenly:", "\"Wow.\"", "\"Okay.\"", "\"I see how it is.\"", "😭", "A little jealousy can happen.", "But friendship isn't ownership.", "You are allowed to have multiple friends", "You don't need permission to talk to someone else.", "You can have another best friend.", "You can join a club.", "You can make friends your friend doesn't know.", "That doesn't mean you're replacing them.", "Reassure them if you want to", "You can say:", "\"You're still my friend. Hanging out with them doesn't change that.\"", "But you don't have to keep proving it forever.", "Watch for controlling behaviour", "If they constantly demand to know where you are, who you're with, or tell you who you're allowed to be friends with, that's not healthy.", "You can say:", "\"I'm not choosing between my friends.\""], "bigSister": "A friendship should add to your life, not shrink it.", "journal": "Do I feel free to have other friendships, or do I feel like I have to ask permission?", "globalNum": "044"}, {"id": "friends-55-when-you-and-your-friend-like-the-same-person", "uid": 45, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "55", "title": "When You and Your Friend Like the Same Person", "body": ["Oh brother.", "This is where things get messy 😭.", "You both like the same person.", "And suddenly you're wondering whether you have to choose between your crush and your friendship.", "First: talk about it", "Don't secretly compete.", "Don't start a race to see who can get their attention first.", "Just be honest.", "\"Okay this is awkward, but I think we both like them.\"", "Now you can actually talk about it.", "Remember that the person isn't a prize", "You can't \"win\" a person.", "They get to decide who they like too.", "So don't turn it into:", "\"I liked them first.\"", "That doesn't mean they're obligated to choose you.", "Don't let the crush destroy the friendship", "Especially if neither of you is dating them.", "You can both have feelings.", "You can both be disappointed.", "You can both decide how much you want to pursue it.", "And if they choose your friend?", "Yeah.", "That might hurt.", "You don't have to pretend you're thrilled.", "But you also don't need to sabotage them.", "Take some space if you need it."], "bigSister": "A crush is temporary. A friendship can last much longer. Don't let a person who isn't even dating you become the reason you lose someone you love.", "journal": "What matters more to me here: getting this person, or protecting a friendship I genuinely value?", "globalNum": "045"}, {"id": "friends-56-when-your-friend-shares-your-private-messages", "uid": 46, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "56", "title": "When Your Friend Shares Your Private Messages", "body": ["You sent a private text.", "Now someone else has screenshots.", "Your stomach drops.", "That's a trust problem", "If you clearly expected something to stay private, sharing it without permission isn't okay.", "Especially if it's personal.", "Don't immediately retaliate", "You might be tempted to screenshot their messages and post them too.", "Don't.", "You're angry, but revenge usually creates a bigger mess.", "Save evidence if necessary", "If the screenshots are being used to bully, threaten, embarrass, or harass you, keep evidence and tell a trusted adult.", "Especially if the messages contain private or sensitive information.", "Talk to the friend", "If you feel safe doing so:", "\"I trusted you with that conversation. I wasn't okay with you sharing it.\"", "Then decide what happens next based on their response.", "Learn the lesson without blaming yourself", "Trusting someone doesn't make you stupid.", "You just learned something about how they handle private information."], "bigSister": "Someone breaking your trust says something about their choices, not your intelligence.", "journal": "What boundaries do I need around private conversations from now on?", "globalNum": "046"}, {"id": "friends-57-when-your-friend-is-jealous-of-your-other-friend", "uid": 47, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "57", "title": "When Your Friend Is Jealous of Your Other Friend", "body": ["Sometimes two of your friends don't like each other.", "And you're somehow the United Nations.", "\"Who do you like more?\"", "\"Why were you hanging out with her?\"", "\"You always choose him.\"", "Please 😭.", "Don't pick sides automatically", "You can care about both people.", "You don't have to make one person the winner.", "Don't compare them", "Never say:", "\"Well, she's a better friend than you.\"", "That's just throwing gasoline on it.", "Set the boundary", "\"I'm not choosing between you two. You're both my friends.\"", "If they don't like each other, they don't have to hang out.", "Don't let them monitor you", "You shouldn't need to report:", "\"I was with Sarah from 4:00 to 5:30.\"", "You're allowed to have a life."], "bigSister": "Managing everyone else's jealousy is not your full-time job.", "journal": "Am I getting pulled into a conflict that isn't actually mine?", "globalNum": "047"}, {"id": "friends-58-when-you-realize-you-don-t-actually-like-your-friend-anymore", "uid": 48, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "58", "title": "When You Realize You Don't Actually Like Your Friend Anymore", "body": ["This is a weird one.", "Nothing huge happened.", "You just don't enjoy being around them anymore.", "Their jokes annoy you.", "You don't look forward to seeing them.", "You don't really want to tell them things.", "And then you feel guilty.", "You're not a bad person", "People change.", "Sometimes you simply stop clicking.", "That doesn't mean the other person is horrible.", "Don't manufacture a reason", "You don't need to find one massive betrayal just to justify wanting distance.", "\"Things changed\" can be enough.", "Be kind", "You don't need to suddenly become cold.", "You can slowly create distance.", "Talk less.", "Spend time with other people.", "Stop forcing plans.", "But if they ask directly", "Don't lie cruelly.", "You can say:", "\"I feel like we've grown apart a bit.\"", "You don't need to list every annoying thing they've ever done."], "bigSister": "You don't need someone to be a bad person before you're allowed to stop being close to them.", "journal": "What specifically changed in this friendship?", "globalNum": "048"}, {"id": "friends-59-when-your-friend-keeps-bringing-up-your-past-mistakes", "uid": 49, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "59", "title": "When Your Friend Keeps Bringing Up Your Past Mistakes", "body": ["You apologized.", "You changed.", "It's been months.", "And somehow every argument ends with:", "\"Well remember when YOU...\"", "Girl.", "We remember. 😭", "Past mistakes can matter", "If you genuinely hurt someone, they might still need time.", "That's fair.", "But if you've apologized, taken responsibility, and changed, they shouldn't be using the mistake forever as a weapon.", "Ask directly", "\"I know I messed up before, and I've apologized. Is there something we still need to talk about?\"", "That gives them an opportunity to explain.", "Don't let guilt become control", "Someone shouldn't be able to make you do whatever they want because:", "\"You owe me.\"", "Friendship isn't a debt."], "bigSister": "Taking responsibility doesn't mean accepting punishment forever.", "journal": "Have I actually repaired the damage, or is there something I still need to make right?", "globalNum": "049"}, {"id": "friends-60-when-you-feel-like-you-re-always-the-one-trying", "uid": 50, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "60", "title": "When You Feel Like You're Always the One Trying", "body": ["You text first.", "Plan first.", "Apologize first.", "Check in first.", "Invite first.", "And eventually you're like:", "\"If I stopped trying, would this friendship even exist?\"", "That's a painful question.", "Try stepping back", "Not to manipulate them.", "Not to see whether they'll \"chase\" you.", "Just stop carrying the entire friendship for a minute.", "See what happens.", "Sometimes people don't realize", "Your friend might genuinely think everything is fine.", "They might not notice how much effort you've been putting in.", "Talking about it could fix things.", "But sometimes you get your answer", "If you disappear and they don't notice for weeks...", "That tells you something.", "It doesn't mean you're unlovable.", "It means this particular friendship wasn't being maintained equally.", "Don't keep proving your value", "You shouldn't have to perform friendship to earn friendship.", "The right people will make an effort too."], "bigSister": "You deserve friendships that feel mutual, not like a group project where you're doing 94% of the work.", "journal": "If I stopped initiating everything, who would still reach out to me?", "globalNum": "050"}, {"id": "friends-61-when-your-friend-lies-to-you", "uid": 51, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "61", "title": "When Your Friend Lies to You", "body": ["Everyone lies sometimes.", "Even small stupid lies.", "But if your friend constantly lies about important things, it becomes hard to know what you can believe.", "Don't immediately accuse them", "If you only have a suspicion, don't act like it's fact.", "Find out what's actually happening.", "If you know they lied", "Talk to them.", "\"You told me ___, but I found out ___. I'm confused about what happened.\"", "Give them a chance to explain.", "Look at why they lied", "Maybe they were embarrassed.", "Maybe they were scared.", "Maybe they wanted attention.", "That doesn't automatically make the lie okay, but understanding the reason can help you decide what happens next.", "Repeated lying is different", "If someone lies constantly, especially about serious things, you don't have to pretend you trust them exactly the same way.", "Trust is based on behaviour."], "bigSister": "You don't have to hate someone to realize you can't rely on everything they tell you.", "journal": "What would I need to see from this person before I feel comfortable trusting them again?", "globalNum": "051"}, {"id": "friends-62-when-your-friend-makes-you-feel-insecure", "uid": 52, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "62", "title": "When Your Friend Makes You Feel Insecure", "body": ["You leave their house and suddenly hate your outfit.", "You compare your body.", "Your grades.", "Your face.", "Your life.", "Your followers.", "Everything.", "Sometimes that's because you're already insecure.", "But sometimes certain friendships genuinely make those feelings worse.", "Notice the difference", "Do they constantly compare you?", "Make comments about your appearance?", "Compete over grades?", "Point out things you're insecure about?", "Make \"jokes\" about your body?", "If yes, that's not something you have to accept.", "Good friends shouldn't require you to feel smaller", "A friend can tease you.", "But they should know when to stop.", "And you should feel safe telling them:", "\"Don't joke about that.\"", "Protect your mind too", "If you know scrolling through certain accounts makes you compare yourself constantly, mute them.", "If certain conversations always become competitions, stop participating.", "You don't have to expose yourself to things that repeatedly make you feel terrible."], "bigSister": "A friendship shouldn't require you to dislike yourself.", "journal": "How do I usually feel about myself after spending time with this person?", "globalNum": "052"}, {"id": "friends-63-when-your-friend-is-going-through-something-serious", "uid": 53, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "63", "title": "When Your Friend Is Going Through Something Serious", "body": ["Sometimes your friend is struggling.", "They're crying a lot.", "They're not acting like themselves.", "They're dealing with family problems.", "They might be talking about hurting themselves or not wanting to be here.", "Your first instinct might be:", "\"I have to save them.\"", "You don't.", "Be there, but don't become their only support", "Listen.", "Check in.", "Sit with them.", "Encourage them to talk to a trusted adult.", "If they're in immediate danger, get an adult involved.", "Even if they tell you:", "\"Don't tell anyone.\"", "If someone's safety is at risk, telling a trusted adult is more important than keeping the secret.", "You aren't a therapist", "You can care deeply about someone and still not know how to fix what they're going through.", "That's okay.", "Don't disappear because you don't know what to say", "You don't need a perfect speech.", "Sometimes:", "\"I don't know what to say, but I'm here.\"", "is enough."], "bigSister": "Supporting your friend does not mean carrying their entire life on your shoulders.", "journal": "Who can I go to for help if someone I care about is struggling?", "globalNum": "053"}, {"id": "friends-64-when-you-and-your-friend-have-different-values", "uid": 54, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "64", "title": "When You and Your Friend Have Different Values", "body": ["Maybe your friend believes something completely different from you.", "Different opinions.", "Different priorities.", "Different ways of living.", "You don't have to agree on everything.", "Ask yourself what actually matters", "Can you disagree respectfully?", "Do they respect your boundaries?", "Can you talk about differences without insulting each other?", "If yes, the friendship may be completely fine.", "But some differences affect how you're treated", "If someone constantly mocks something important to you or pressures you to abandon your values, that's different.", "You don't have to stay in every friendship just because you've known someone for years.", "Don't try to \"convert\" each other", "You can explain your perspective.", "You can listen.", "You can disagree.", "You don't need to win."], "bigSister": "Compatibility doesn't mean agreeing on every single thing. It means being able to disagree without disrespecting each other.", "journal": "Which differences can I accept, and which ones genuinely affect my ability to feel respected?", "globalNum": "054"}, {"id": "friends-65-when-your-friend-moves-away", "uid": 55, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "65", "title": "When Your Friend Moves Away", "body": ["This is basically grief with a school uniform on.", "One week they're there.", "Then suddenly their bedroom is empty.", "Their seat is empty.", "You don't get to see them after school anymore.", "And everyone says:", "\"You'll still keep in touch!\"", "Maybe.", "But you're still going to miss them.", "Let yourself be sad", "Don't pretend you're fine because nobody died.", "You're losing part of your everyday life.", "That can hurt.", "Make a plan", "Before they leave, figure out how you'll stay in contact.", "Weekly call.", "Monthly movie night.", "Shared playlist.", "Gaming together.", "Whatever actually works for you.", "But don't make impossible promises", "\"WE'LL TALK EVERY SINGLE DAY FOREVER.\"", "You might.", "You might not.", "Life changes.", "What matters is making a genuine effort.", "Keep living your own life", "This is important.", "Don't freeze your social life waiting for your friend to come back.", "Make new friends.", "Try things.", "Have experiences.", "You can miss someone and still keep moving."], "bigSister": "Distance can change how a friendship works without changing what it meant to you.", "journal": "What is one memory I want to keep from this friendship, and what is one new thing I want to experience next?", "globalNum": "055"}, {"id": "friends-66-when-your-friend-is-getting-more-popular", "uid": 56, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "66", "title": "When Your Friend Is Getting More Popular", "body": ["Suddenly everyone knows your friend.", "People follow them.", "Invite them places.", "Talk to them.", "And you're standing there like:", "\"Oh, so we're celebrities now?\" 😭", "Don't make their popularity your competition", "Their social life getting bigger doesn't automatically make yours smaller.", "They can have more friends without loving you less.", "But watch what changes", "Do they still talk to you?", "Still make time for you?", "Still treat you normally?", "If yes, don't create a problem that isn't there.", "If they've started treating you badly because they're suddenly \"popular,\" that's different.", "Don't change yourself to keep up", "You don't need to become louder, meaner, cooler, or more social just because your friend is getting attention.", "You aren't in the same race."], "bigSister": "Someone else's popularity doesn't subtract anything from you.", "journal": "Am I happy for my friend, or am I comparing their life to mine?", "globalNum": "056"}, {"id": "friends-67-when-your-friend-doesn-t-respect-your-boundaries", "uid": 57, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "67", "title": "When Your Friend Doesn't Respect Your Boundaries", "body": ["You already told them.", "\"Don't post that.\"", "They post it.", "\"Don't tell people.\"", "They tell someone.", "\"I don't want to go.\"", "They pressure you.", "That's not a misunderstanding anymore if it keeps happening.", "Repeat the boundary clearly", "\"I've already told you I'm not okay with this.\"", "You don't need to keep explaining.", "Add a consequence", "Remember: a boundary is about what you will do.", "\"If you keep sharing my private things, I'm going to stop telling you personal stuff.\"", "\"If you keep insulting me, I'm going to leave the conversation.\"", "Then follow through.", "Don't threaten things you won't do", "If you say you're going to leave, leave.", "If you say you're going to stop sharing private information, stop.", "Otherwise the boundary becomes a suggestion."], "bigSister": "You can't control whether someone respects your boundary. You can control how much access they get to you when they don't.", "journal": "What boundary have I communicated that I need to actually enforce?", "globalNum": "057"}, {"id": "friends-68-when-you-re-scared-your-friends-will-leave-you", "uid": 58, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "68", "title": "When You're Scared Your Friends Will Leave You", "body": ["Sometimes everything is going well...", "and somehow your brain decides:", "\"But what if they leave?\"", "So you become extra careful.", "You overthink every message.", "You apologize constantly.", "You panic when someone is quiet.", "You try to be the \"perfect friend.\"", "You cannot guarantee someone will stay", "That's the scary part.", "People change.", "Life changes.", "Friendships change.", "You can't control that.", "But you can stop abandoning yourself", "Don't become whoever you think someone wants you to be just to keep them.", "Don't agree with everything.", "Don't hide your feelings.", "Don't accept disrespect.", "A friendship that only survives when you're pretending isn't actually giving you security.", "Trust the friendship you're in", "If they're showing up.", "Talking to you.", "Including you.", "Caring about you.", "Let yourself enjoy it.", "You don't need to ruin today's friendship by preparing for tomorrow's breakup."], "bigSister": "Sometimes the fear of losing people makes you forget to actually enjoy having them.", "journal": "What would change if I stopped trying to predict whether people will leave?", "globalNum": "058"}, {"id": "friends-69-when-your-friend-is-mean-as-a-joke", "uid": 59, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "69", "title": "When Your Friend Is Mean as a Joke", "body": ["Some friendships are basically 90% roasting each other.", "That's fine.", "If both people are laughing.", "The problem is when the joke only works because one person is getting hurt.", "Ask yourself:", "Do I actually laugh?", "Or do I laugh because everyone else is?", "Do they stop when I ask?", "Do they know what I'm sensitive about and use it anyway?", "If you answer yes to the last two, that's a problem.", "Say something", "\"I know you're joking, but I don't like jokes about that.\"", "A good friend should care that you're uncomfortable.", "Don't feel pressured to become \"less sensitive\"", "People have different limits.", "You can enjoy jokes and still have boundaries."], "bigSister": "\"It's just a joke\" doesn't magically erase the fact that something hurt you.", "journal": "Which jokes do I genuinely find funny, and which ones do I pretend to laugh at?", "globalNum": "059"}, {"id": "friends-70-finding-your-people", "uid": 60, "category": "friends", "categoryLabel": "Friends", "num": "70", "title": "Finding Your People", "body": ["This is the one I want you to remember.", "You don't need to be liked by everyone.", "You don't need the biggest friend group.", "You don't need to be invited everywhere.", "You don't need hundreds of followers.", "You need people around whom you don't feel like you're performing.", "People who let you be weird.", "People who listen.", "People who can tell you when you're wrong without humiliating you.", "People who celebrate you without competing with you.", "People who respect your no.", "People who make room for you.", "And finding those people can take time.", "You might have to go through awkward friendships.", "People who aren't good for you.", "Friendships that fade.", "People you thought would be your best friend and weren't.", "That's part of it.", "Every friendship teaches you something about what you need.", "So don't settle just because you're lonely", "Being alone for a while is better than constantly feeling alone while surrounded by people who don't make you feel wanted.", "Keep meeting people.", "Keep trying things.", "Keep being open.", "And don't forget to become the kind of person you're hoping to find too.", "Be the person who notices someone sitting alone.", "The person who checks in.", "The person who doesn't spread someone's secret.", "The person who makes people feel welcome.", "Because eventually, you're going to meet people who do the same for you."], "bigSister": "Your people are out there. You don't need to find all of them at once.", "journal": "What are the three things I care about most in a friendship?", "globalNum": "060"}, {"id": "dating-1-your-first-crush", "uid": 61, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "1", "title": "Your First Crush", "body": ["Your first crush is SO unserious and SO serious at the exact same time.", "One second you're completely normal.", "The next you're analyzing the way they said \"hey\" like it's a government document.", "😭", "You might think about them constantly.", "You might suddenly care way more about what you wear to school.", "You might tell your friends every single detail.", "That's normal.", "Don't build an entire relationship in your head", "This is probably the biggest thing.", "You can have a crush on someone without knowing whether you'd actually work together.", "You might have imagined:", "Your first date", "Your wedding", "Your kids", "Your house", "Your dog", "And you've literally only exchanged three words.", "Please come back to Earth 😭.", "You don't know them that well yet.", "Get to know the actual person instead of only the version of them you've created in your head.", "You don't need to confess immediately", "You can just talk to them.", "Say hi.", "Ask about school.", "Make a joke.", "Find out what they're actually like.", "There's no deadline.", "Don't change your entire personality", "You don't suddenly need to become mysterious.", "Or super quiet.", "Or pretend you love football because they do.", "Let them get to know you.", "And if they don't like you back?", "It'll hurt.", "But it doesn't mean you're unattractive, boring, annoying, or \"not good enough.\"", "Someone not liking you romantically is not a rating of your worth."], "bigSister": "A crush is supposed to be exciting. Don't turn it into a full-time job.", "journal": "What do I actually like about this person besides how they look?", "globalNum": "061"}, {"id": "dating-2-talking-to-your-crush", "uid": 62, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "2", "title": "Talking to Your Crush", "body": ["Okay.", "You like them.", "Now what?", "Because apparently saying \"hi\" suddenly requires military preparation.", "Start normally", "You don't need some insane pickup line.", "Try:", "\"Did you understand the homework?\"", "\"What did you think of the test?\"", "\"Wait, what song is that?\"", "\"Are you going to ___?\"", "Literally anything natural.", "Don't interrogate them", "You don't want:", "\"What's your favourite colour?\"", "\"What's your favourite food?\"", "\"What's your mother's maiden name?\"", "Relax 😭.", "Have an actual conversation.", "Share things about yourself too.", "Match their energy", "If they're giving one-word answers every time, don't keep forcing the conversation.", "If they're asking questions back, joking with you, starting conversations, or finding reasons to talk to you, that's a better sign.", "Don't obsess over every text", "A person saying:", "\"lol\"", "doesn't necessarily mean they're secretly disgusted by you.", "People text differently.", "Look at the overall pattern instead of one message."], "bigSister": "You don't need to be smooth. You just need to be genuine and give them room to be interested too.", "journal": "What would I say to my crush if I wasn't scared of looking awkward?", "globalNum": "062"}, {"id": "dating-3-does-my-crush-like-me-back", "uid": 63, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "3", "title": "Does My Crush Like Me Back?", "body": ["Unfortunately, there is no magical \"THEY LIKE YOU\" notification.", "You have to look at behaviour.", "Possible signs", "They might:", "Start conversations", "Remember little things you said", "Look for reasons to be around you", "Ask questions about you", "Joke with you", "Seem genuinely interested in your life", "Make an effort to keep conversations going", "But none of these are guaranteed proof.", "Someone can be friendly without having a crush on you.", "Don't rely on TikTok \"signs\"", "\"IF HE LOOKS AT YOU FOR 0.3 SECONDS HE'S OBSESSED.\"", "Girl please 😭.", "Real life is more complicated.", "The clearest sign?", "Eventually, communication.", "If you want to know whether someone is interested, getting to know them and eventually being honest is much more reliable than decoding every blink.", "Don't stalk their socials for evidence", "Looking at someone's profile isn't illegal detective work.", "But if you're checking who they followed, liked, unfollowed, and commented on every five minutes...", "You are going to drive yourself insane."], "bigSister": "Don't turn uncertainty into a conspiracy theory.", "journal": "What do I actually know about their feelings, and what am I guessing?", "globalNum": "063"}, {"id": "dating-4-rejection", "uid": 64, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "4", "title": "Rejection", "body": ["Okay.", "This one sucks.", "There isn't really a cute way to say it.", "You liked someone.", "They don't feel the same.", "Ouch.", "Let yourself be disappointed", "You don't need to immediately say:", "\"Whatever, I didn't even like them.\"", "If you did like them, you liked them.", "It's okay to be sad.", "Don't beg", "Don't send:", "\"PLEASE just give me one chance.\"", "Don't try to convince someone to like you.", "You deserve someone who actually wants to be there.", "Don't turn it into humiliation", "You might feel embarrassed.", "But having feelings isn't embarrassing.", "You were brave enough to like someone.", "That's human.", "Don't become obsessed with changing yourself", "Don't suddenly decide:", "\"I need to lose weight.\"", "\"I need better hair.\"", "\"I need to become prettier.\"", "\"I need to dress differently.\"", "Their preference isn't a universal beauty ranking.", "You don't need to rebuild yourself because one person said no.", "Give yourself some distance", "Mute their stories if seeing them makes you spiral.", "Stop checking who they're talking to.", "Focus on your own life.", "Eventually, the intensity will fade."], "bigSister": "Rejection means \"this person isn't choosing me,\" not \"nobody will ever choose me.\"", "journal": "What did this rejection make me believe about myself, and is that belief actually true?", "globalNum": "064"}, {"id": "dating-5-mixed-signals", "uid": 65, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "5", "title": "Mixed Signals", "body": ["One day they're flirting.", "The next day they're acting like you're their math teacher.", "What are we doing here? 😭", "Stop trying to decode everything", "If someone is constantly hot and cold, you don't have to spend months figuring out what they \"really\" mean.", "Look at consistency.", "Do they actually make an effort?", "Or do they only flirt when they're bored?", "Don't let attention become your addiction", "Sometimes mixed signals are addictive because you're constantly waiting for the next good interaction.", "One cute message makes you forget the five times they ignored you.", "That's not a great cycle.", "Ask if you need clarity", "You don't have to confess your undying love.", "You can simply say:", "\"Sometimes I feel like we're flirting and sometimes I can't tell what this is.\"", "Their answer may tell you everything.", "If they say they don't know", "Believe them.", "You don't have to wait around hoping you'll eventually convince them."], "bigSister": "Confusion isn't always chemistry. Sometimes confusion is just confusion.", "journal": "Do their actions consistently match the attention they give me?", "globalNum": "065"}, {"id": "dating-6-situationships", "uid": 66, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "6", "title": "Situationships", "body": ["A situationship is basically:", "\"So... what are we?\"", "\"Idk.\"", "\"Okay but like—\"", "\"Let's just see where it goes.\"", "And six months later you're still \"seeing where it goes.\" 😭", "Situationships aren't automatically bad", "Sometimes two people genuinely aren't ready for a relationship and are okay keeping things casual.", "The problem is when you want different things.", "Be honest about what you want", "If you want an actual relationship, don't pretend you're fine with something casual just because you're scared they'll leave.", "You might think:", "\"Maybe if I act chill enough, they'll eventually choose me.\"", "Maybe.", "But that's not something you can guarantee.", "Pay attention to how you feel", "Are you constantly anxious?", "Wondering where you stand?", "Checking their location?", "Waiting for messages?", "Feeling jealous but having no right to say anything?", "That can get exhausting.", "You are allowed to leave", "You don't need a dramatic betrayal.", "You can simply say:", "\"I don't think this situation is good for me anymore.\"", "That's enough."], "bigSister": "Don't accept an arrangement you hate just because you're hoping it will eventually become the relationship you want.", "journal": "If this situation stayed exactly the same for six months, would I actually be happy?", "globalNum": "066"}, {"id": "dating-7-your-first-relationship", "uid": 67, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "7", "title": "Your First Relationship", "body": ["Your first relationship doesn't have to be perfect.", "Honestly, it probably won't be.", "You're both figuring things out.", "Don't rush everything", "You don't need to immediately:", "Spend every day together", "Tell each other every secret", "Share passwords", "Post each other constantly", "Make huge promises", "Plan your entire future", "You're teenagers.", "You have time.", "Keep your own life", "Still see your friends.", "Still do your hobbies.", "Still study.", "Still spend time with family.", "A relationship should become part of your life, not your entire life.", "Communicate", "If something bothers you, say it.", "Don't expect them to magically know.", "Instead of:", "\"Fine.\"", "say:", "\"That actually bothered me.\"", "Respect goes both ways", "You should feel comfortable saying no.", "They should too.", "Neither person should control the other."], "bigSister": "Your first relationship is supposed to teach you about relationships—not become your entire identity.", "journal": "What do I want my first relationship to feel like?", "globalNum": "067"}, {"id": "dating-8-first-breakup", "uid": 68, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "8", "title": "First Breakup", "body": ["Even if you're young, heartbreak can still hurt like crazy.", "People sometimes act like:", "\"You're only teenagers. You'll get over it.\"", "Okay??", "That doesn't make the feelings fake.", "Let yourself grieve", "You lost a relationship.", "Maybe you lost your daily conversations too.", "Your routines.", "Your plans.", "Your favourite person.", "Of course you're going to feel weird.", "Don't immediately become enemies", "You don't have to hate them to move on.", "And you don't have to stay best friends either.", "Sometimes some distance is healthier.", "Don't keep checking their socials", "This is probably the hardest part.", "You want to know:", "Who are they with?", "Are they sad?", "Did they move on?", "Are they posting?", "Do they miss you?", "You're probably going to make yourself feel worse.", "Mute them if you need to.", "Don't rush into another relationship", "You don't need someone new to prove you're okay.", "Take your time.", "Figure out what happened.", "Think about what you learned.", "Then move forward."], "bigSister": "Missing someone doesn't mean you should get back together with them.", "journal": "What do I miss about the person, and what do I not miss about the relationship?", "globalNum": "068"}, {"id": "dating-9-heartbreak", "uid": 69, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "9", "title": "Heartbreak", "body": ["Heartbreak can make your entire life feel smaller.", "Songs hit differently.", "Places remind you of them.", "You suddenly remember something random from six months ago and get sad.", "It's annoying.", "But it gets better.", "Don't romanticize everything", "Your brain will probably show you the highlights.", "The cute conversations.", "The funny moments.", "The first time they said something sweet.", "Remember the whole relationship.", "Not just the best parts.", "Let yourself cry", "Cry.", "Journal.", "Talk to someone.", "Listen to sad music for a bit.", "Then eventually get up and do something.", "Don't spend every day feeding the sadness.", "Take care of your body", "Eat.", "Sleep.", "Drink water.", "Go outside.", "Shower.", "Move around.", "Heartbreak can make you neglect yourself because you don't feel like doing anything.", "Don't.", "Give it time", "There is no correct number of days you're supposed to be over someone.", "You might feel better and then randomly feel sad again.", "That's normal.", "Healing isn't a straight line."], "bigSister": "You don't need to stop missing someone before you can start moving forward.", "journal": "What would taking care of myself look like today, even if I still feel sad?", "globalNum": "069"}, {"id": "dating-10-being-single", "uid": 70, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "10", "title": "Being Single", "body": ["Being single can feel amazing.", "And sometimes it feels like everyone around you is dating except you.", "Especially when your entire For You Page is couples doing matching everything.", "😭", "You are not behind", "There is no age where you're supposed to have had:", "Your first kiss", "Your first relationship", "Your first date", "Your first breakup", "Everyone has different experiences.", "Don't date someone just because you're lonely", "Being in a bad relationship can feel much lonelier than being single.", "You shouldn't have to accept someone who doesn't respect you just because you want someone.", "Use the time", "Make friends.", "Find hobbies.", "Work on yourself.", "Figure out what you actually like.", "Learn what your boundaries are.", "Have fun.", "And don't make being single your entire personality either", "You don't need to say:", "\"I DON'T NEED ANYONE.\"", "every time someone mentions dating.", "You can want love and be happy alone.", "Both can exist."], "bigSister": "Being single isn't the waiting room before your real life starts. Your life is already happening.", "journal": "What would I do differently if I stopped treating being single like something I need to fix?", "globalNum": "070"}, {"id": "dating-11-first-date-nerves", "uid": 71, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "11", "title": "First Date Nerves", "body": ["First dates are awkward.", "Like, objectively.", "Two people who like each other are suddenly sitting across from each other thinking:", "\"So... what do humans normally talk about?\"", "😭", "Don't try to make it perfect", "You're not filming a rom-com.", "There might be awkward silences.", "Someone might spill something.", "The conversation might randomly die.", "That's fine.", "A good date doesn't require everything to go perfectly.", "Choose somewhere comfortable", "Especially for a first date, somewhere public and familiar is a much better idea than going somewhere isolated.", "You should always have your own way home or a trusted adult who knows where you are.", "And if you're meeting someone you've only known online, don't meet them secretly or alone.", "Have a few conversation starters", "Not a script.", "Just things you can fall back on:", "\"What have you been listening to lately?\"", "\"What shows are you watching?\"", "\"What do you actually like doing after school?\"", "\"What's something you've always wanted to try?\"", "And remember to answer too.", "You're having a conversation, not conducting an interview.", "Don't ignore discomfort", "If something feels wrong, you can leave.", "You don't owe someone extra time because they paid for something.", "You don't owe physical affection because you went on a date.", "You can say no."], "bigSister": "The goal of a first date isn't to make them obsessed with you. It's to figure out whether you actually enjoy being around each other.", "journal": "What would make me feel comfortable and safe on a first date?", "globalNum": "071"}, {"id": "dating-12-healthy-vs-unhealthy-relationships", "uid": 72, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "12", "title": "Healthy vs. Unhealthy Relationships", "body": ["A healthy relationship doesn't mean you never argue.", "You will disagree.", "You will annoy each other.", "You'll misunderstand each other.", "That's normal.", "The difference is how you handle it.", "Healthy looks like:", "You can say no.", "You can have other friends.", "You can disagree.", "You feel respected.", "You can talk about problems.", "You don't constantly fear upsetting them.", "They respect your privacy.", "You both make an effort.", "You can be yourself.", "Unhealthy can look like:", "Constant jealousy", "Controlling who you talk to", "Checking your phone without permission", "Demanding passwords", "Making you feel guilty for having friends", "Pressuring you into things you don't want", "Insulting you during arguments", "Threatening to leave to control you", "Making you feel like you have to \"prove\" your love", "Don't confuse intensity with love", "Someone being obsessed with where you are, who you're with, and what you're doing isn't automatically romantic.", "Sometimes control gets dressed up as:", "\"I just care about you.\"", "Caring still needs boundaries."], "bigSister": "A relationship shouldn't make your world smaller.", "journal": "Do I feel more like myself in this relationship, or less like myself?", "globalNum": "072"}, {"id": "dating-13-red-flags", "uid": 73, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "13", "title": "Red Flags", "body": ["Red flags aren't always dramatic.", "Sometimes they're tiny behaviours that keep happening.", "Pay attention if someone:", "Constantly insults you and calls it a joke", "Doesn't respect \"no\"", "Gets angry when you spend time with friends", "Tries to control what you wear", "Demands access to your phone", "Makes you feel guilty for having boundaries", "Lies constantly", "Threatens you", "Pressures you into sexual things", "Tries to isolate you", "Makes you scared of their reaction", "One bad day doesn't automatically mean someone is terrible.", "But repeated behaviour matters.", "Trust patterns, not excuses", "Anyone can say:", "\"I'll change.\"", "The important part is whether their behaviour actually changes.", "And don't ignore your gut", "You don't need a PowerPoint presentation proving that someone is bad before you can leave.", "If you consistently feel unsafe, uncomfortable, or controlled, that's enough reason to step back.", "If someone threatens you, pressures you sexually, or makes you feel unsafe, tell a trusted adult."], "bigSister": "You don't need to wait until something becomes \"bad enough\" to protect yourself.", "journal": "What behaviour would make me uncomfortable enough to leave a relationship?", "globalNum": "073"}, {"id": "dating-14-green-flags", "uid": 74, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "14", "title": "Green Flags", "body": ["Okay, let's talk about the stuff that's actually good.", "Because sometimes people think healthy relationships are boring.", "They're not.", "They're just not constantly giving you anxiety 😭.", "Green flags include:", "They respect your boundaries.", "They listen when you talk.", "They don't make you feel guilty for having other friends.", "They apologize when they're wrong.", "They don't pressure you into physical affection.", "They celebrate your achievements.", "They can disagree without insulting you.", "They respect your privacy.", "They make you feel comfortable saying no.", "They don't expect instant replies.", "They have their own life too.", "Look at consistency", "Someone being amazing for three days doesn't tell you much.", "Someone consistently treating you well over time does.", "Green flags should feel normal", "You shouldn't have to constantly think:", "\"Wow, they're doing the bare minimum!\"", "Respect should be the baseline."], "bigSister": "The healthiest relationships aren't necessarily the ones with the most drama. Sometimes they're the ones where you feel safe enough to relax.", "journal": "What behaviours make me feel genuinely respected by someone?", "globalNum": "074"}, {"id": "dating-15-when-your-crush-likes-your-friend", "uid": 75, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "15", "title": "When Your Crush Likes Your Friend", "body": ["Ouch.", "You liked them.", "They like your friend.", "And now every time those two talk, your brain is doing:", "💔🥀", "You're allowed to be hurt", "Don't force yourself to be happy about it immediately.", "You can be happy for your friend eventually while still being disappointed.", "Both feelings can exist.", "Don't blame your friend", "Unless they knew you liked the person and deliberately tried to hurt you, they haven't done anything wrong by being liked.", "You don't own a crush.", "Don't compete", "Don't start trying to prove you're prettier, funnier, cooler, or more interesting.", "If someone chooses someone else, let them.", "Take space if you need it", "You can tell your friend:", "\"I'm happy for you, I just need a little time because I had feelings too.\"", "That's honest."], "bigSister": "Someone choosing your friend doesn't mean they rejected your entire existence. They simply have their own feelings.", "journal": "What am I actually sad about—the person, the rejection, or feeling compared to my friend?", "globalNum": "075"}, {"id": "dating-16-when-your-crush-has-a-girlfriend-boyfriend", "uid": 76, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "16", "title": "When Your Crush Has a Girlfriend/Boyfriend", "body": ["Okay.", "They've already got someone.", "That means the situation is pretty simple:", "Respect the relationship.", "You can still have feelings", "You can't always control who you like.", "You can control what you do about it.", "You don't need to hate yourself because you have a crush on someone unavailable.", "Don't try to break them up", "No fake rumours.", "No trying to turn them against each other.", "No:", "\"They're actually toxic, you deserve better.\"", "unless there is genuinely something serious happening and you're concerned for their safety.", "Don't become their secret option", "If they're flirting with you while they're in a relationship, that's not automatically flattering.", "Think about what that behaviour says about how they might treat you if you were the person dating them.", "Let yourself move on", "Mute their stories.", "Stop checking their relationship.", "Focus on other people and other things.", "You don't have to wait around."], "bigSister": "You deserve someone who's actually available to choose you—not someone you have to compete for.", "journal": "What would help me stop feeding this crush and give myself some space?", "globalNum": "076"}, {"id": "dating-17-when-they-like-you-but-you-don-t-like-them-back", "uid": 77, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "17", "title": "When They Like You But You Don't Like Them Back", "body": ["This is the opposite problem.", "And honestly, it can be uncomfortable because you don't want to hurt them.", "You don't owe someone a relationship because they like you", "You can appreciate their feelings without returning them.", "You can say:", "\"I'm flattered, but I don't feel the same way.\"", "That's enough.", "Don't give fake hope", "If you know you don't want a relationship, don't say:", "\"Maybe someday.\"", "just because you're scared they'll be upset.", "That usually makes things harder later.", "Be kind, but clear", "Don't publicly embarrass them.", "Don't tell everyone.", "Don't make jokes about their confession.", "Having feelings for someone isn't humiliating.", "Give them space", "They might need some distance afterwards.", "Let them have it."], "bigSister": "Saying no kindly is much better than saying yes because you feel guilty.", "journal": "Am I being clear about my feelings, or am I accidentally giving them hope?", "globalNum": "077"}, {"id": "dating-18-when-you-re-too-scared-to-make-the-first-move", "uid": 78, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "18", "title": "When You're Too Scared to Make the First Move", "body": ["You want to talk to them.", "But your brain says:", "\"What if they think I'm weird?\"", "Here's the truth:", "They might.", "Or they might be happy you did.", "You don't know until you try.", "Start tiny", "You don't need to confess everything.", "Start a conversation.", "Say hi.", "Reply to their story.", "Ask about something you already have in common.", "See how they respond.", "You don't have to perform", "Don't become a completely different person because you're nervous.", "If you normally make jokes, make jokes.", "If you're quiet, that's okay too.", "Rejection isn't the worst thing", "The worst part is often the uncertainty.", "Once you know, you can move forward.", "But don't pressure yourself", "You don't have to make a move just because your friends think you should.", "If you're not ready, you're not ready."], "bigSister": "Being brave doesn't mean being fearless. It means doing something even though you're nervous.", "journal": "What's the smallest step I could take instead of trying to make a huge confession?", "globalNum": "078"}, {"id": "dating-19-overthinking-texts-from-your-crush", "uid": 79, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "19", "title": "Overthinking Texts From Your Crush", "body": ["They said:", "\"okay\"", "And suddenly you're analyzing punctuation.", "Was the lowercase intentional?", "Why no emoji?", "Why didn't they say \"okayyy\"?", "Are they mad?", "Do they hate me?", "😭", "Please step away from the phone.", "Texting is terrible for reading emotions.", "People have different texting styles.", "They could be:", "Busy", "Tired", "At school", "Distracted", "Bad at texting", "Literally just saying \"okay\"", "Look at patterns", "One dry message doesn't tell you much.", "If someone is consistently uninterested, that's more meaningful.", "Don't send messages just to test them", "Don't intentionally stop replying to see whether they'll chase you.", "Don't post something just to see if they'll react.", "Don't make them jealous.", "That's exhausting.", "If something actually feels wrong", "Ask.", "A normal conversation will tell you more than 45 minutes of staring at a message."], "bigSister": "Your brain is very talented at turning a three-word text into a five-season Netflix series. Don't let it.", "journal": "What facts do I actually have, separate from what I'm assuming?", "globalNum": "079"}, {"id": "dating-20-when-your-crush-suddenly-stops-talking-to-you", "uid": 80, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "20", "title": "When Your Crush Suddenly Stops Talking to You", "body": ["This one hurts because there's no explanation.", "You were talking.", "Things seemed fine.", "Then suddenly...", "nothing.", "Don't immediately blame yourself", "You don't automatically know why someone became distant.", "Maybe something happened in their life.", "Maybe they're interested in someone else.", "Maybe they changed their mind.", "Maybe they're just busy.", "Give them some space", "One message is enough.", "You don't need to send:", "\"What did I do?\"", "\"Are you mad?\"", "\"Hello??\"", "\"Did I do something?\"", "\"Why are you ignoring me?\"", "over and over.", "If you need clarity", "You can ask once:", "\"Hey, I feel like we've been talking less lately. Is everything okay?\"", "Then leave the ball in their court.", "Don't chase someone who keeps choosing distance", "If they repeatedly ignore you, you have your answer even if they never officially explain it.", "It sucks.", "But chasing them won't make you feel better."], "bigSister": "Sometimes the closure is realizing someone isn't making an effort anymore. You don't need to turn yourself into a detective to understand that.", "journal": "If they never gave me an explanation, what would I need to tell myself so I could still move forward?", "globalNum": "080"}, {"id": "dating-21-long-distance-relationships", "uid": 81, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "21", "title": "Long-Distance Relationships", "body": ["Long-distance relationships sound cute until you're staring at your phone like:", "\"It's been 47 minutes. Are they alive?\"", "😭", "Being far away can work, but it requires communication and trust.", "Don't make constant texting the entire relationship", "You both have school.", "Family.", "Friends.", "Your own lives.", "You don't need to be on FaceTime 24/7 to prove you care.", "Make actual time for each other", "Maybe you call on certain days.", "Watch something together.", "Play games.", "Send photos of random parts of your day.", "Talk about things that aren't just:", "\"wyd\"", "\"nm u\"", "Trust matters", "If you're constantly checking their followers, location, likes, and activity because you're scared they'll talk to someone else, you're going to exhaust yourself.", "If you don't trust them, that's something to address.", "Don't forget your own life", "Keep your friends.", "Keep your hobbies.", "Keep your routines.", "You shouldn't spend the entire relationship waiting for the next call."], "bigSister": "Distance is difficult, but constantly monitoring someone isn't how you make it easier.", "journal": "What would make me feel connected to someone without needing constant contact?", "globalNum": "081"}, {"id": "dating-22-jealousy-in-relationships", "uid": 82, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "22", "title": "Jealousy in Relationships", "body": ["Jealousy happens.", "You see your partner talking to someone attractive and your brain immediately goes:", "\"Interesting.\"", "That's human.", "Feeling jealous isn't the problem", "What you do with the feeling matters.", "Healthy:", "\"I felt a little insecure when that happened.\"", "Unhealthy:", "\"You're not allowed to talk to them anymore.\"", "Don't make jealousy into control", "You don't get to demand someone's passwords, location, or entire phone just because you're scared.", "And they don't get to demand yours either.", "Figure out what's underneath it", "Are you scared they'll leave?", "Have they actually given you a reason not to trust them?", "Are you comparing yourself to someone else?", "Sometimes jealousy is about insecurity rather than the other person.", "Communicate instead of accusing", "Instead of:", "\"You obviously like them.\"", "Try:", "\"I felt insecure when I saw that. Can we talk about it?\"", "Huge difference."], "bigSister": "You can tell someone you're jealous without making them responsible for fixing every insecurity you have.", "journal": "What am I actually afraid will happen when I feel jealous?", "globalNum": "082"}, {"id": "dating-23-when-your-partner-is-jealous-of-your-friends", "uid": 83, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "23", "title": "When Your Partner Is Jealous of Your Friends", "body": ["Your partner says:", "\"I don't like you hanging out with them.\"", "And now you're confused because you've known your friend for years.", "Ask why", "There might be something specific bothering them.", "Maybe your friend has crossed a boundary.", "Maybe your partner feels left out.", "Maybe they're insecure.", "Find out.", "But listen carefully to the difference", "\"I feel uncomfortable because ___.\"", "is very different from:", "\"You're not allowed to have friends.\"", "One is communication.", "The other is control.", "Don't isolate yourself", "A healthy relationship should not require you to abandon your friendships.", "If someone repeatedly tries to separate you from everyone else, that's a serious red flag.", "Keep your independence", "Your partner can be important without becoming your entire social world."], "bigSister": "Love doesn't require you to disappear from everyone else's life.", "journal": "Does this relationship make room for the other people I care about?", "globalNum": "083"}, {"id": "dating-24-physical-affection-and-boundaries", "uid": 84, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "24", "title": "Physical Affection and Boundaries", "body": ["Let's make this extremely clear:", "You never owe someone physical affection.", "Not because you're dating.", "Not because you've kissed before.", "Not because you said yes yesterday.", "Not because they bought you something.", "Not because you're scared they'll be upset.", "You can change your mind", "You can say yes and then change your mind.", "You can say no.", "You can say \"not right now.\"", "You can say \"I don't want to.\"", "And that's enough.", "Respect goes both ways", "If your partner says no, you respect that too.", "No guilt-tripping.", "No:", "\"But you love me.\"", "No:", "\"If you really liked me...\"", "No pressure.", "If someone doesn't respect your no", "That's serious.", "Get away from the situation and tell a trusted adult.", "You don't have to handle it alone."], "bigSister": "Consent isn't something you earn by being in a relationship. It's something that applies every time.", "journal": "What boundaries make me feel comfortable, and can I communicate them clearly?", "globalNum": "084"}, {"id": "dating-25-being-pressured-into-sending-private-photos", "uid": 85, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "25", "title": "Being Pressured Into Sending Private Photos", "body": ["This deserves its own page because people don't talk about it enough.", "If someone asks you for a private or sexual photo, you do not owe them one.", "Not your boyfriend.", "Not your girlfriend.", "Not your crush.", "Not someone you've been talking to for six months.", "\"Trust me\" isn't a reason", "Neither is:", "\"Everyone does it.\"", "\"I won't save it.\"", "\"I'll delete it.\"", "\"You're no fun.\"", "\"If you loved me, you would.\"", "Those are pressure tactics.", "Once something is sent, you lose control of where it goes", "Even if someone promises to keep it private, you cannot guarantee that.", "Screenshots exist.", "Phones get lost.", "Accounts get hacked.", "People fall out.", "If someone is threatening you", "Don't send more.", "Don't negotiate.", "Save evidence.", "Block/report them where appropriate.", "Tell a trusted adult immediately.", "And remember: you are not the one doing something wrong by refusing."], "bigSister": "Anyone who genuinely cares about you will respect your boundary instead of trying to pressure you past it.", "journal": "What would I say if someone pressured me for something I didn't want to send?", "globalNum": "085"}, {"id": "dating-26-when-someone-wants-to-keep-your-relationship-secret", "uid": 86, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "26", "title": "When Someone Wants to Keep Your Relationship Secret", "body": ["There's a difference between wanting privacy and wanting secrecy.", "Privacy:", "\"We don't want everyone at school involved in our relationship.\"", "Fair.", "Secrecy:", "\"Nobody can know about us, and you can't tell anyone.\"", "That's different.", "Especially if they're telling you to hide the relationship from trusted adults or making you feel like you have to lie constantly.", "Ask why", "Maybe they're nervous.", "Maybe they aren't ready.", "Maybe they have complicated circumstances.", "But you deserve to understand what you're agreeing to.", "Be careful if secrecy is being used against you", "If someone says:", "\"If you tell anyone, I'll...\"", "or threatens you, that's not normal relationship privacy.", "Get help from a trusted adult."], "bigSister": "You don't have to live like you're in witness protection just because you're dating someone.", "journal": "Am I comfortable with the amount of privacy this relationship has, and why?", "globalNum": "086"}, {"id": "dating-27-when-your-partner-doesn-t-respect-your-friends", "uid": 87, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "27", "title": "When Your Partner Doesn't Respect Your Friends", "body": ["Your partner doesn't have to love every friend you have.", "But they should still treat them respectfully.", "Ask what the actual issue is", "Maybe your friend has genuinely behaved badly.", "Listen.", "But if your partner simply doesn't want you to have friends because they're jealous, that's different.", "Don't let them create unnecessary drama", "You don't need:", "\"Tell your friend I said...\"", "\"Don't talk to her.\"", "\"Block him.\"", "Your relationships shouldn't become a constant battlefield.", "Keep boundaries", "You can say:", "\"I hear that you don't like them, but I'm still allowed to have my own friendships.\"", "That's reasonable."], "bigSister": "Your partner doesn't need to approve every person in your life. They do need to respect that you're your own person.", "journal": "Is my partner concerned about something specific, or are they trying to control who I spend time with?", "globalNum": "087"}, {"id": "dating-28-when-you-don-t-know-if-you-re-ready-to-date", "uid": 88, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "28", "title": "When You Don't Know If You're Ready to Date", "body": ["Everyone seems to be dating.", "So naturally you're thinking:", "\"Wait... should I be dating too?\"", "No.", "Not automatically.", "Ask yourself:", "Do I actually want a relationship?", "Or do I just want someone to like me?", "Do I feel comfortable saying no?", "Can I handle someone not texting me constantly?", "Can I still focus on school and friends?", "Am I choosing someone because I like them, or because I don't want to feel left out?", "There's no deadline", "You can date at 13.", "You can date later.", "You can not want to date at all right now.", "None of these makes you weird.", "Don't let friends pressure you", "\"You're the only single one.\"", "Okay?", "And?", "😭", "Your timeline is your timeline."], "bigSister": "Being ready for a relationship isn't about reaching a certain age. It's about knowing what you want and being able to protect your boundaries.", "journal": "If nobody else around me was dating, would I still want a relationship right now?", "globalNum": "088"}, {"id": "dating-29-dating-someone-your-friends-don-t-like", "uid": 89, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "29", "title": "Dating Someone Your Friends Don't Like", "body": ["Your friends say:", "\"We don't like them.\"", "And now you're stuck.", "Don't immediately ignore your friends", "If several people who care about you are noticing the same behaviour, listen.", "They might see something you don't because you're emotionally involved.", "But don't blindly obey either", "Ask:", "\"What specifically worries you?\"", "Not:", "\"Do you like them?\"", "You want actual examples.", "Look at the evidence", "Do they control you?", "Lie constantly?", "Disrespect you?", "Make you uncomfortable?", "Pressure you?", "Or do your friends simply think they're annoying?", "Those are very different situations.", "You make the final decision", "Your friends can advise you.", "They can't live your relationship for you."], "bigSister": "Good friends won't just say \"dump them.\" They'll explain what they're seeing and let you think about it.", "journal": "What specific behaviour are my friends concerned about?", "globalNum": "089"}, {"id": "dating-30-when-you-keep-going-back-to-someone", "uid": 90, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "30", "title": "When You Keep Going Back to Someone", "body": ["You broke up.", "Then got back together.", "Then broke up.", "Then somehow you're talking again.", "At this point even your friends are tired 😭.", "Ask what actually changed", "Not:", "\"Do we still love each other?\"", "That's probably yes.", "Ask:", "\"What was causing us to break up, and has that actually changed?\"", "Because love doesn't automatically fix incompatibility.", "Look at actions", "If someone says:", "\"I'll change.\"", "What did they actually change?", "If nothing is different, you're probably going to repeat the same cycle.", "Don't confuse missing someone with needing them back", "You can miss someone terribly and still know the relationship wasn't healthy.", "Sometimes the healthiest ending is permanent", "That doesn't mean you never cared.", "It means you finally accepted that caring wasn't enough to make the relationship work."], "bigSister": "Before getting back together, don't ask only \"Do we miss each other?\" Ask \"Would this actually be different this time?\"", "journal": "What would genuinely need to change for this relationship to work?", "globalNum": "090"}, {"id": "dating-31-when-your-partner-gives-you-the-silent-treatment", "uid": 91, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "31", "title": "When Your Partner Gives You the Silent Treatment", "body": ["There's a difference between:", "\"I'm upset and need some time to cool down.\"", "and:", "\"I'm going to ignore you until you panic and apologize.\"", "The first is taking space.", "The second can be manipulation.", "Healthy space has communication", "Someone might say:", "\"I'm annoyed right now. Can we talk later?\"", "That's fair.", "You don't have to chase", "If someone intentionally ignores you to make you beg for forgiveness, don't spend hours sending messages trying to fix it.", "Give them space.", "Then talk when both of you are ready.", "If it keeps happening", "That's a pattern.", "You deserve relationships where problems can actually be discussed."], "bigSister": "Taking time to calm down is healthy. Using silence to punish someone isn't.", "journal": "When we have conflict, do we eventually communicate or just punish each other?", "globalNum": "091"}, {"id": "dating-32-arguments-in-relationships", "uid": 92, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "32", "title": "Arguments in Relationships", "body": ["Every couple argues.", "The goal isn't:", "\"Never fight.\"", "It's learning how to disagree without destroying each other.", "Don't attack the person", "Say:", "\"That hurt me.\"", "Not:", "\"You're literally the worst person ever.\"", "Talk about the behaviour.", "Don't bring up everything they've ever done", "If you're arguing about Tuesday, you don't need to resurrect an argument from February.", "Stay on the actual problem.", "Take a break if needed", "If you're both too angry to communicate properly:", "\"I need a little time. Let's talk later.\"", "Then actually come back to the conversation.", "Never use threats casually", "\"Maybe we should break up.\"", "\"Fine, I'll leave.\"", "\"If you loved me...\"", "Those shouldn't be weapons you use whenever you're angry."], "bigSister": "A good argument isn't one where somebody wins. It's one where both people understand what happened and figure out what to do next.", "journal": "What do I tend to do when I'm angry, and does it actually help?", "globalNum": "092"}, {"id": "dating-33-when-your-relationship-is-affecting-school", "uid": 93, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "33", "title": "When Your Relationship Is Affecting School", "body": ["You're staying up until 2 a.m. texting.", "Can't focus in class.", "Checking your phone every five seconds.", "Your grades are dropping.", "You're stressed constantly.", "That's a sign something needs to change.", "A relationship shouldn't consume your entire life", "You still need sleep.", "School matters.", "Friends matter.", "Family matters.", "Your own goals matter.", "Set boundaries around your time", "You can say:", "\"I'm going to study now. I'll talk to you later.\"", "That's completely normal.", "Don't feel guilty for prioritizing yourself", "You can care about someone and still say:", "\"I have homework.\"", "😭", "If the relationship only works when you sacrifice everything", "That's not balance."], "bigSister": "Someone who genuinely cares about you should want you to succeed—not make you feel guilty for having a life outside the relationship.", "journal": "What parts of my life have I been neglecting because of this relationship?", "globalNum": "093"}, {"id": "dating-34-when-you-re-comparing-yourself-to-their-ex", "uid": 94, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "34", "title": "When You're Comparing Yourself to Their Ex", "body": ["You find their ex's account.", "Now you're looking at pictures thinking:", "\"Oh.\"", "Then you zoom in.", "Then you compare hair.", "Face.", "Body.", "Style.", "Everything.", "Stop.", "😭", "Their ex isn't your competition", "They dated that person.", "They chose to be with you.", "Those are two different relationships.", "You don't need to be \"better\"", "You don't need to look better than their ex.", "You don't need more followers.", "You don't need to dress differently.", "You're not auditioning for the role of \"best girlfriend/boyfriend ever.\"", "If your partner constantly compares you", "That's different.", "Someone saying:", "\"My ex was prettier.\"", "or:", "\"My ex never did that.\"", "is disrespectful.", "You deserve to be treated as yourself."], "bigSister": "You're not supposed to recreate someone else's relationship with the same person.", "journal": "What am I comparing about myself, and why do I feel like I need to win?", "globalNum": "094"}, {"id": "dating-35-self-worth-after-rejection", "uid": 95, "category": "dating", "categoryLabel": "Dating", "num": "35", "title": "Self-Worth After Rejection", "body": ["This is the final one I really want you to keep.", "Someone can reject you.", "A crush can choose someone else.", "A relationship can end.", "Someone can stop liking you.", "And none of that changes your value.", "Rejection can make you look for something wrong with yourself", "\"Maybe I'm ugly.\"", "\"Maybe I'm boring.\"", "\"Maybe I'm too annoying.\"", "\"Maybe I'm not enough.\"", "But romantic attraction isn't a school exam.", "There isn't a universal score.", "Don't let one person's opinion become your identity", "You can improve things about yourself because you want to.", "Not because you think becoming prettier, thinner, cooler, quieter, or more interesting will finally make someone choose you.", "The right relationship shouldn't require you to audition", "You shouldn't constantly be thinking:", "\"Am I good enough for them?\"", "You should also be asking:", "\"Are they good for me?\"", "That question matters just as much.", "And remember:", "You are going to like people who don't like you back.", "People are going to like you when you don't like them back.", "Relationships will work.", "Some won't.", "You'll get attached.", "You'll get hurt.", "You'll learn.", "That's part of growing up.", "None of it determines your worth."], "bigSister": "Being rejected doesn't make you less lovable. It just means that particular person wasn't your person.", "journal": "If I completely separated my worth from other people's opinions of me, what would I believe about myself?", "globalNum": "095"}, {"id": "family-1-strict-parents", "uid": 96, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "1", "title": "Strict Parents", "body": ["Having strict parents can feel like living under a 24/7 security investigation.", "\"Where are you going?\"", "\"Who is going?\"", "\"Who else is going?\"", "\"What time?\"", "\"Why?\"", "\"Who invited you?\"", "\"Send me their mother's number.\"", "😭", "And sometimes you're genuinely thinking:", "\"Can I breathe?\"", "First, understand what kind of strictness you're dealing with", "Some parents are strict because they're protective.", "Some are strict because of how they were raised.", "Some are worried about safety.", "Some have cultural or religious expectations.", "And sometimes... they're just genuinely being unreasonable.", "Knowing which one you're dealing with helps.", "Don't have every conversation during an argument", "If you ask for more freedom while everyone's already angry, you're probably going to get:", "\"Because I said so.\"", "Instead, choose a calm moment.", "Try:", "\"Can we talk about giving me a little more independence?\"", "Then explain what you're actually asking for.", "Not:", "\"You never let me do anything.\"", "But:", "\"Could I go to ___ with my friends if I give you the address and come home by ___?\"", "Specific requests are easier to negotiate.", "Build trust gradually", "If you want more freedom, showing that you can handle smaller responsibilities helps.", "Be where you said you'd be.", "Communicate if plans change.", "Do what you're supposed to do.", "Not because you need to become perfect to deserve freedom, but because trust usually grows through consistency.", "And sometimes...", "Your parents are going to say no.", "That sucks.", "But not every \"no\" means you have to start World War III.", "Sometimes you wait.", "Sometimes you negotiate.", "Sometimes you accept it and try again later."], "bigSister": "Wanting more independence doesn't make you disrespectful. You're growing up. Your parents just have to learn how to grow with you.", "journal": "What specific freedom do I want, and what could I do to show I'm ready for it?", "globalNum": "096"}, {"id": "family-2-when-your-parents-say-no-to-everything", "uid": 97, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "2", "title": "When Your Parents Say No to Everything", "body": ["At some point it starts feeling like:", "\"Can I go out?\"", "\"No.\"", "\"Can I get this?\"", "\"No.\"", "\"Can I—\"", "\"No.\"", "Okay bro 😭.", "Don't turn every \"no\" into a fight", "If you're constantly arguing about everything, your parents may start expecting conflict before you've even finished asking.", "Pick the things that genuinely matter.", "Ask why", "Instead of:", "\"WHY NOT?\"", "Try:", "\"Can you tell me what's making you uncomfortable about it?\"", "Sometimes the reason is actually fixable.", "Maybe they don't know where you'll be.", "Maybe they don't know who you'll be with.", "Maybe they think something costs too much.", "Now you have something to work with.", "Offer solutions", "If they're worried about safety:", "\"I'll share my location.\"", "If they're worried about timing:", "\"I'll be home by 6.\"", "If they're worried about money:", "\"I'll pay for part of it.\"", "Make it easier for them to say yes.", "But don't assume every no can be negotiated", "Sometimes the answer is genuinely no.", "You can be disappointed without turning the house into a courtroom."], "bigSister": "You're allowed to disagree with your parents without making every disagreement a war.", "journal": "What is the real reason behind the last \"no\" I got?", "globalNum": "097"}, {"id": "family-3-when-your-parents-don-t-understand-you", "uid": 98, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "3", "title": "When Your Parents Don't Understand You", "body": ["You try explaining something.", "They don't get it.", "You explain again.", "Still nothing.", "Eventually you're just:", "\"Never mind.\"", "Remember that your parents grew up in a different world", "They may not understand:", "Social media", "Friend group drama", "School pressure", "Trends", "Online friendships", "Why certain things matter to you", "That doesn't automatically mean they don't care.", "Sometimes they genuinely don't understand what your life feels like.", "Explain instead of expecting them to know", "You can say:", "\"I know this might not seem like a big deal to you, but it matters to me because...\"", "That gives them context.", "But sometimes they still won't understand", "And that's painful.", "You don't need everyone to completely understand your feelings for those feelings to be real.", "Talk to another trusted adult if you need someone who gets it.", "A relative.", "Teacher.", "School counsellor.", "Another safe adult."], "bigSister": "Sometimes the goal isn't getting someone to agree with you. Sometimes it's just making sure you aren't carrying everything alone.", "journal": "What do I wish my parents understood about my life right now?", "globalNum": "098"}, {"id": "family-4-when-your-parents-compare-you-to-other-kids", "uid": 99, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "4", "title": "When Your Parents Compare You to Other Kids", "body": ["\"Why can't you be more like ___?\"", "You already know that sentence.", "😭", "Comparison doesn't motivate everyone", "Sometimes it just makes you feel like nothing you do is enough.", "And that's exhausting.", "Don't turn it into a competition", "You don't need to become better than the person they compare you to.", "Their grades aren't your grades.", "Their personality isn't yours.", "Their life isn't yours.", "If you can, explain how it affects you", "Try:", "\"When I'm compared to other people, I feel like what I do isn't good enough. I'd rather know what I can improve myself.\"", "That is much more useful than:", "\"STOP COMPARING ME.\"", "even though you absolutely want to scream that 😭.", "Remember your own progress", "Compare yourself to who you were before.", "Did you improve?", "Learn something?", "Become more responsible?", "Get better at something?", "Those things count."], "bigSister": "You don't need to become somebody else to be worth being proud of.", "journal": "What are three things I've improved at that nobody else gets to take credit for?", "globalNum": "099"}, {"id": "family-5-when-your-parents-argue", "uid": 100, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "5", "title": "When Your Parents Argue", "body": ["Hearing your parents argue can make the whole house feel unsafe, even when the argument isn't about you.", "You might sit there listening.", "Wondering:", "\"Are they going to break up?\"", "\"Is someone going to leave?\"", "\"Is this my fault?\"", "First: it's not your job to fix them", "You are their child.", "You are not their therapist.", "You don't need to choose sides.", "You don't need to carry messages between them.", "You don't need to solve their relationship.", "Take yourself somewhere calmer if you can", "Go to your room.", "Put on headphones.", "Read.", "Watch something.", "Call someone you trust.", "Do something that makes you feel grounded.", "If things become unsafe", "If there is physical violence, threats, weapons, or you genuinely fear someone could be hurt, get yourself somewhere safe and contact a trusted adult or emergency support.", "You don't have to physically intervene.", "And don't blame yourself", "Parents have problems that existed before you and that aren't caused by you."], "bigSister": "Their relationship is their responsibility. Your responsibility is taking care of yourself.", "journal": "What do I need when things at home feel tense?", "globalNum": "100"}, {"id": "family-6-when-your-parents-are-fighting-because-of-money", "uid": 101, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "6", "title": "When Your Parents Are Fighting Because of Money", "body": ["Money problems can change the atmosphere of an entire house.", "You hear adults discussing bills.", "Jobs.", "Rent.", "School fees.", "Moving.", "And suddenly you're worried about everything.", "Remember: adult finances aren't your responsibility", "You can care.", "You can help where it's reasonable.", "But you aren't supposed to carry the financial pressure of the whole family.", "Don't assume every argument means disaster", "Adults can disagree about money and still figure things out.", "Your brain might immediately jump to:", "\"We're going to lose everything.\"", "You don't know that.", "Try not to fill in missing information with the worst possible scenario.", "Focus on what you can control", "School.", "Your responsibilities.", "Helping around the house.", "Being thoughtful with money.", "That's enough.", "If you're genuinely worried", "Ask a trusted adult what is actually happening.", "You don't need to silently panic."], "bigSister": "Caring about your family doesn't mean you have to carry adult problems on your back.", "journal": "What am I actually responsible for, and what belongs to the adults?", "globalNum": "101"}, {"id": "family-7-sibling-fights", "uid": 102, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "7", "title": "Sibling Fights", "body": ["Having siblings is basically having a permanent roommate who knows exactly how to annoy you.", "They know your embarrassing stories.", "They know what makes you mad.", "And somehow they always touch your stuff.", "😭", "Fighting doesn't automatically mean you don't love each other", "Siblings annoy each other.", "That's normal.", "But there are limits", "Constant humiliation, threats, physical violence, or deliberately hurting you isn't something you should just accept because:", "\"They're your sibling.\"", "Pick your battles", "Sometimes:", "\"Can you please stop?\"", "works better than a 45-minute argument.", "Sometimes you genuinely need space.", "Take it.", "Don't involve your parents in every tiny disagreement", "If you can solve something yourselves, do.", "But if the situation becomes unsafe or seriously unfair, get an adult involved.", "And remember:", "Your sibling isn't your enemy.", "You're both growing up.", "You're going to annoy each other.", "You're also probably going to have moments where you need each other."], "bigSister": "You can be furious with your sibling and still love them. Both can exist.", "journal": "What's one thing I wish my sibling understood about me?", "globalNum": "102"}, {"id": "family-8-when-you-feel-like-your-sibling-is-the-favourite", "uid": 103, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "8", "title": "When You Feel Like Your Sibling Is the Favourite", "body": ["Your sibling gets something.", "You don't.", "They get praised.", "You don't.", "And suddenly you're convinced:", "\"Okay so apparently I was adopted.\"", "😭", "Parents don't always treat every child exactly the same", "Different ages mean different rules.", "Different responsibilities.", "Different needs.", "That doesn't automatically mean one child is loved more.", "But your feelings still matter", "If you're consistently feeling overlooked, talk about it.", "Don't start with:", "\"You love them more.\"", "Try:", "\"I've been feeling like I'm getting less attention lately, and I don't really know how to explain it.\"", "That's much easier to respond to.", "Don't compete with your sibling", "Their achievement doesn't take yours away.", "If they get praised, it doesn't mean you're failing.", "Your relationship with your parents is its own thing", "You don't need to become exactly like your sibling to deserve love."], "bigSister": "Different treatment isn't always different love.", "journal": "What specifically makes me feel overlooked?", "globalNum": "103"}, {"id": "family-9-feeling-like-the-responsible-child", "uid": 104, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "9", "title": "Feeling Like the \"Responsible Child\"", "body": ["Maybe you're the one who always gets trusted.", "You help with siblings.", "You do chores.", "You keep things organized.", "Everyone says:", "\"You're so mature.\"", "That's nice...", "until being \"mature\" starts meaning you're expected to handle everything.", "Being responsible doesn't mean you don't need help", "You can be capable and still get tired.", "You can help your family and still want someone to take care of you sometimes.", "Don't be afraid to say:", "\"I can help, but I need a break.\"", "That's reasonable.", "Watch for parentification", "If you're regularly expected to take on responsibilities that are really an adult's job, especially emotional or financial responsibilities, that's something to talk about with a trusted adult.", "You shouldn't have to become your family's second parent."], "bigSister": "Being the responsible one doesn't mean you have to be the strong one every second.", "journal": "What responsibilities am I okay with, and which ones are becoming too much?", "globalNum": "104"}, {"id": "family-10-having-too-many-responsibilities", "uid": 105, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "10", "title": "Having Too Many Responsibilities", "body": ["School.", "Homework.", "Chores.", "Siblings.", "Activities.", "Family stuff.", "And somehow you're also supposed to sleep eight hours and \"practice self-care.\"", "Girl when 😭?", "Write everything down", "Literally everything.", "Seeing it outside your head makes it easier to figure out what's actually urgent.", "Separate:", "Must do", "School deadlines.", "Important family responsibilities.", "Things that genuinely cannot wait.", "Should do", "Cleaning.", "Extra studying.", "Other useful tasks.", "Can wait", "Things that aren't urgent.", "Ask for help", "You can say:", "\"I have ___ due tomorrow and I'm also supposed to do ___. Can we figure out what should come first?\"", "That's better than silently drowning.", "Don't expect yourself to perform perfectly everywhere", "You are one person.", "You cannot be the perfect student, perfect sibling, perfect friend, perfect daughter, and perfectly rested human simultaneously."], "bigSister": "Sometimes being responsible means admitting you have too much on your plate.", "journal": "What can I remove, delay, or ask for help with this week?", "globalNum": "105"}, {"id": "family-11-when-your-family-is-moving", "uid": 106, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "11", "title": "When Your Family Is Moving", "body": ["Moving can be exciting and still feel horrible.", "You might be excited about the new house, new room, new city...", "while also thinking:", "\"Wait. I'm actually leaving everything?\"", "Both feelings can exist.", "Don't force yourself to feel one way", "You don't have to be grateful every second.", "You can be excited and sad.", "You can love the new place and miss the old one.", "You can be ready to leave and still cry about it.", "Say goodbye properly", "Take pictures.", "Visit your favourite places.", "See people you care about.", "Save little things that remind you of your old life.", "Not because you're never going to be happy again, but because that chapter mattered.", "Don't expect yourself to adjust instantly", "A new home might feel weird for a while.", "Your room won't feel like yours immediately.", "Your routine will change.", "Give yourself time."], "bigSister": "A new beginning doesn't erase the old one.", "journal": "What am I most excited about, and what am I most scared of losing?", "globalNum": "106"}, {"id": "family-12-moving-countries", "uid": 107, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "12", "title": "Moving Countries", "body": ["Moving countries is a whole different level.", "New school.", "New accent around you.", "New food.", "New slang.", "New rules.", "New people.", "And sometimes you're expected to just walk in and act normal.", "Yeah... no 😭.", "Culture shock is real", "You might love your new country and still miss your old one.", "You might suddenly miss things you didn't even appreciate before.", "Your favourite supermarket.", "Your old school.", "A certain snack.", "The way people spoke.", "Your friends.", "Your routine.", "Don't compare everything", "It's tempting to constantly think:", "\"Back home we did it like this.\"", "Sometimes comparisons are useful.", "Sometimes they stop you from actually experiencing your new environment.", "Give the new place a chance.", "Keep pieces of your old life", "Stay in touch with friends.", "Keep traditions.", "Make your favourite foods.", "Listen to music you associate with home.", "You don't have to erase one identity to create another.", "And don't expect instant friendships", "Being new is awkward.", "You may feel like everyone already has their people.", "Give it time."], "bigSister": "You don't have to choose between your old home and your new home. Both can matter to you.", "journal": "What part of my old life do I want to keep with me?", "globalNum": "107"}, {"id": "family-13-homesickness", "uid": 108, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "13", "title": "Homesickness", "body": ["Homesickness can hit at random.", "You could be having a completely normal day and suddenly miss home so badly it hurts.", "Don't shame yourself", "Missing somewhere doesn't mean you hate where you are now.", "It just means something familiar matters to you.", "Create little pieces of home", "Listen to familiar music.", "Cook something you used to eat.", "Call someone.", "Look through old photos.", "Keep familiar decorations around you.", "Build routines that make your new environment feel more yours.", "Don't isolate yourself", "When you're homesick, hiding away can make it worse.", "Even if you don't feel like it, try going outside.", "Talk to someone.", "Explore.", "Do something.", "Let yourself miss people", "You don't have to pretend you're fine.", "Say:", "\"I miss them.\"", "That's okay."], "bigSister": "Homesickness isn't proof that you made the wrong decision. Sometimes it just means you're adjusting.", "journal": "What exactly am I missing right now, and is there a small way I can bring some of it into my current life?", "globalNum": "108"}, {"id": "family-14-missing-relatives", "uid": 109, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "14", "title": "Missing Relatives", "body": ["Maybe your grandma lives far away.", "Maybe your cousins moved.", "Maybe you used to see your relatives constantly and now you barely do.", "That can hurt.", "Make contact intentional", "Don't rely on:", "\"We'll call sometime.\"", "Actually plan it.", "A weekly call.", "Voice notes.", "Family group chats.", "Video calls.", "Send pictures of random things from your day.", "Keep relationships alive through little things", "You don't need a two-hour emotional conversation every time.", "Send:", "\"Look what I saw today 😂.\"", "That's still connection.", "And don't panic if things change", "People grow.", "Families get busy.", "Some relationships become less close.", "That doesn't erase the memories you had."], "bigSister": "Distance makes relationships require more effort, not necessarily less love.", "journal": "Who do I miss most, and what's one small thing I could do to feel closer to them?", "globalNum": "109"}, {"id": "family-15-living-with-extended-family", "uid": 110, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "15", "title": "Living With Extended Family", "body": ["Living with grandparents, aunties, uncles, cousins, or other relatives can be... interesting.", "Because suddenly:", "privacy has left the chat.", "😭", "Remember that everyone has different habits", "Different people have different:", "Routines", "Rules", "Standards", "Personal space", "Ways of communicating", "Some things will annoy you.", "That doesn't necessarily mean anyone is terrible.", "Create boundaries where you can", "Keep your important belongings somewhere safe.", "Ask before people use your things.", "Have a place where you can study or decompress.", "Even if you can't have complete privacy, you can still create little boundaries.", "Don't take every comment personally", "Extended family can sometimes have VERY strong opinions.", "Your clothes.", "Your hair.", "Your grades.", "Your hobbies.", "Your phone.", "You don't have to react to every single comment.", "Sometimes:", "\"Okay.\"", "and moving on is genuinely the best response.", "But speak up when something actually matters", "If someone is consistently disrespecting your boundaries or making you feel unsafe, tell a trusted adult."], "bigSister": "You can respect your family without letting every family member have unlimited access to you.", "journal": "What part of living with other relatives is hardest for me?", "globalNum": "110"}, {"id": "family-16-family-expectations", "uid": 111, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "16", "title": "Family Expectations", "body": ["Maybe your family expects you to become a doctor.", "Or lawyer.", "Or engineer.", "Or whatever career they think sounds impressive.", "Meanwhile you're sitting there like:", "\"I don't even know what I'm doing tomorrow.\"", "😭", "Their expectations may come from love", "Parents often want security for their children.", "They might believe a certain career guarantees a good future.", "That doesn't mean they automatically know what's right for you.", "You don't need your entire future figured out", "You're allowed to explore.", "Try things.", "Change your mind.", "Be interested in something random.", "Talk about your reasoning", "Instead of:", "\"I DON'T WANT TO DO THAT.\"", "try:", "\"I've been thinking about ___ because I enjoy ___, and I'd like to explore it more.\"", "Parents are often more willing to listen when they can see that you aren't just making a random decision.", "Your future is ultimately your life", "Advice is valuable.", "Pressure isn't the same thing as guidance."], "bigSister": "You can respect your parents' dreams for you without making their dreams your entire identity.", "journal": "What would I choose if I wasn't scared of disappointing anyone?", "globalNum": "111"}, {"id": "family-17-cultural-differences-at-home", "uid": 112, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "17", "title": "Cultural Differences at Home", "body": ["Sometimes your family has traditions and expectations that don't always match the world around you.", "You might think:", "\"Why do we do this?\"", "while your parents are thinking:", "\"Because this is how we were raised.\"", "You don't have to reject your culture to question something", "You can love your culture and still disagree with certain expectations.", "You can appreciate traditions while deciding which ones you want to continue.", "Ask questions", "Instead of immediately assuming something is stupid, ask:", "\"Why is this important to our family?\"", "You might learn something you didn't know.", "But questioning isn't disrespect", "You're growing.", "Part of growing up is figuring out which beliefs and traditions you genuinely want to carry forward.", "Find balance", "You don't have to choose:", "old ways OR new ways.", "Sometimes you can create your own version."], "bigSister": "Growing up between different expectations can be confusing, but it can also teach you how to think for yourself.", "journal": "Which family traditions matter most to me, and why?", "globalNum": "112"}, {"id": "family-18-step-parents", "uid": 113, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "18", "title": "Step-Parents", "body": ["Having a step-parent can be complicated.", "You might like them.", "You might dislike them.", "You might feel awkward.", "You might feel like they're trying to replace your biological parent.", "You might feel guilty for getting close to them.", "There isn't one correct reaction.", "You don't have to force a relationship", "You don't have to suddenly call them \"Mom\" or \"Dad.\"", "You can build a relationship at your own pace.", "Respect doesn't mean instant closeness", "You can be respectful without pretending you're emotionally comfortable immediately.", "If they're trying to replace someone", "You can communicate that.", "\"I appreciate you, but I already have a parent and I'm not looking for someone to replace them.\"", "If they're actually kind to you", "It's okay to let yourself like them.", "You aren't betraying your biological parent by caring about another adult.", "Love isn't a limited supply."], "bigSister": "You don't have to choose between people. You can have complicated feelings about your family and still care about everyone involved.", "journal": "What would make me feel more comfortable in my relationship with my step-parent?", "globalNum": "113"}, {"id": "family-19-divorce", "uid": 114, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "19", "title": "Divorce", "body": ["When parents divorce, it can feel like your entire idea of family has changed.", "Even if you knew it was coming.", "Even if you think divorce is the right choice.", "It can still hurt.", "Don't blame yourself", "This is one of the biggest things to remember.", "Their relationship problems are not your fault.", "You didn't cause them.", "You can't fix them.", "You don't have to choose sides", "You can love both parents.", "You can be angry with both.", "You can feel closer to one.", "You can feel confused.", "You don't need to make everything emotionally neat.", "Don't become the messenger", "You shouldn't have to carry:", "\"Tell your dad...\"", "\"Ask your mom...\"", "If adults need to communicate, they need to handle that themselves.", "Your routine may change", "New homes.", "Different schedules.", "Different holidays.", "Different traditions.", "It may take time to get used to.", "Talk to someone", "A trusted adult, counsellor, teacher, relative, or another safe person can help you process everything.", "You don't need to act like you're fine."], "bigSister": "Your family changing doesn't mean you stop being loved.", "journal": "What part of this change scares me the most?", "globalNum": "114"}, {"id": "family-20-when-your-parents-separate-and-you-miss-the-other-one", "uid": 115, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "20", "title": "When Your Parents Separate and You Miss the Other One", "body": ["Maybe you're staying with one parent and constantly thinking about the other.", "The house feels different.", "Meals feel different.", "Everything feels slightly wrong.", "Make a routine", "Knowing when you'll talk or see the other parent can make things feel less uncertain.", "Keep little connections", "Call.", "Text.", "Send photos.", "Share music.", "Talk about your day.", "It doesn't have to be a huge conversation every time.", "Let yourself say you miss them", "You don't need to protect your parent from your feelings.", "You can say:", "\"I miss you today.\"", "That's okay.", "And remember:", "Missing one parent doesn't mean you don't love the other.", "You don't have to divide your heart into percentages."], "bigSister": "You're allowed to miss someone without making anyone else feel guilty about it.", "journal": "What do I miss most when I'm away from them?", "globalNum": "115"}, {"id": "family-21-when-your-family-moves-without-asking-you", "uid": 116, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "21", "title": "When Your Family Moves Without Asking You", "body": ["Sometimes adults make huge decisions and you're informed afterward.", "New city.", "New country.", "New school.", "New house.", "And you're like:", "\"Oh. Cool. So I apparently had no vote.\"", "😭", "Your feelings are still valid", "Even if the adults have a legitimate reason, you're allowed to be upset.", "Ask questions", "You deserve to understand what's happening.", "Where will you live?", "What school?", "When?", "Why?", "What will change?", "What won't?", "Knowing the details can make something scary feel more manageable.", "Focus on what you can influence", "Maybe you can't choose whether the family moves.", "But perhaps you can choose:", "Your room setup.", "Some activities.", "How you stay in contact with friends.", "Things you bring with you.", "How you decorate your new space.", "Small choices can give you some control."], "bigSister": "You don't have to control the whole situation to have a voice in your own life.", "journal": "What part of this change can I actually influence?", "globalNum": "116"}, {"id": "family-22-family-financial-stress", "uid": 117, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "22", "title": "Family Financial Stress", "body": ["When money is tight, you may notice things changing.", "Fewer outings.", "Less shopping.", "Parents being stressed.", "Arguments about expenses.", "You might even feel guilty asking for things.", "You don't need to feel guilty for existing", "You have needs.", "Food.", "School.", "Clothes.", "Healthcare.", "Basic things.", "Wanting something doesn't make you selfish.", "Learn the difference between needs and wants", "It's okay to say:", "\"I don't need this right now.\"", "That's maturity.", "But don't start thinking:", "\"My family is struggling, so I shouldn't ever ask for anything.\"", "You are still allowed to have needs.", "Help where you reasonably can", "Save money.", "Avoid unnecessary waste.", "Take care of things you already own.", "Help around the house.", "But don't take responsibility for fixing the family's finances.", "That's an adult responsibility."], "bigSister": "Being financially responsible doesn't mean feeling guilty every time you want something.", "journal": "What money habits could I build now that would help me later?", "globalNum": "117"}, {"id": "family-23-wanting-more-independence", "uid": 118, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "23", "title": "Wanting More Independence", "body": ["You're getting older.", "You want to choose your clothes.", "Go places.", "Manage your money.", "Make your own decisions.", "Have privacy.", "And your parents are still like:", "\"You're a child.\"", "Pain 😭.", "Independence is built, not magically granted", "Start with smaller things.", "Manage your schedule.", "Take care of your belongings.", "Learn basic cooking.", "Learn how money works.", "Plan your own schoolwork.", "Keep track of important things.", "Show that you can handle freedom", "If you constantly lose things, miss deadlines, or ignore rules, your parents may understandably worry about giving you more freedom.", "That doesn't mean you have to be perfect.", "Just become more consistent.", "Ask for specific independence", "Instead of:", "\"I want more freedom.\"", "Try:", "\"Could I manage my own study schedule?\"", "or:", "\"Could I choose my own clothes within the budget?\"", "Specific independence is easier to negotiate."], "bigSister": "Independence isn't doing whatever you want. It's being trusted to handle more responsibility.", "journal": "What is one adult skill I could learn this month?", "globalNum": "118"}, {"id": "family-24-wanting-privacy-from-your-family", "uid": 119, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "24", "title": "Wanting Privacy From Your Family", "body": ["Wanting privacy does not automatically mean you're hiding something.", "Sometimes you just want to exist without someone asking:", "\"What are you doing?\"", "every seven minutes.", "😭", "Explain what privacy means to you", "Maybe you want:", "A door that gets knocked on", "Private journaling", "Your belongings left alone", "Time alone", "Private conversations with friends", "Tell your family what you're actually asking for.", "Privacy isn't secrecy", "You can have private thoughts and conversations while still being honest with your parents about important things.", "Be responsible with privacy", "If you're given trust, don't use it to put yourself in unsafe situations.", "Especially online.", "And remember:", "Parents may have legitimate safety concerns.", "The goal isn't:", "\"You can never check anything.\"", "It's finding a balance between safety and growing independence."], "bigSister": "Wanting privacy is a normal part of growing up. You don't need to feel guilty for wanting your own space.", "journal": "What kind of privacy do I actually need, and how can I explain it calmly?", "globalNum": "119"}, {"id": "family-25-feeling-like-nobody-in-your-family-gets-you", "uid": 120, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "25", "title": "Feeling Like Nobody in Your Family Gets You", "body": ["Sometimes you're surrounded by people and still feel completely alone.", "Everyone knows you.", "But nobody seems to understand you.", "Start with one person", "You don't need the whole family to understand you.", "Find one person you trust.", "A sibling.", "Parent.", "Cousin.", "Aunt.", "Teacher.", "Counsellor.", "Anyone safe.", "Tell them specifically", "Don't just say:", "\"Nobody understands me.\"", "Try:", "\"I've been feeling ___ because ___, and I don't know what to do about it.\"", "Specific feelings are easier for someone to respond to.", "Give people a chance", "Sometimes people don't know you need support because you've never told them.", "But if you genuinely aren't being heard", "Keep looking for support outside the immediate situation.", "You deserve somewhere safe to talk."], "bigSister": "Feeling misunderstood doesn't mean you're impossible to understand. Sometimes you just haven't found the right person to talk to yet.", "journal": "What is one thing I wish someone would ask me about?", "globalNum": "120"}, {"id": "family-26-when-your-parents-don-t-approve-of-your-friends", "uid": 121, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "26", "title": "When Your Parents Don't Approve of Your Friends", "body": ["You make a new friend and your parents immediately go:", "\"I don't like them.\"", "And you're like:", "\"You met them for twelve seconds.\"", "😭", "Ask why", "Don't immediately assume they're being unreasonable.", "Ask:", "\"What makes you uncomfortable about them?\"", "Maybe they noticed something you didn't.", "Maybe your friend has been disrespectful.", "Maybe they don't know the person yet.", "Let your parents get to know them", "Sometimes parents are less worried once they actually know who your friends are.", "Tell them about your friend.", "Let them meet.", "Be open about where you're going.", "But parents can also be wrong", "They're human.", "They might judge someone based on appearance, background, rumours, or assumptions.", "You can listen to their concerns without automatically agreeing.", "Look at the actual behaviour", "Ask yourself:", "Does this friend respect me?", "Do they pressure me?", "Do they lie constantly?", "Do they get me into trouble?", "Do I feel safe around them?", "That's more important than whether your parents simply \"vibe\" with them."], "bigSister": "Don't blindly choose your parents or your friends. Look at the actual situation.", "journal": "What specifically does my parent dislike about this friend, and do I agree?", "globalNum": "121"}, {"id": "family-27-when-your-parents-don-t-like-your-style", "uid": 122, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "27", "title": "When Your Parents Don't Like Your Style", "body": ["You finally find an outfit you love.", "Your parent:", "\"You're not wearing that.\"", "😭", "Remember that style is personal", "You are figuring out who you are.", "Clothes, hair, accessories, makeup, etc. can be part of that.", "But understand their concern", "Sometimes parents are worried about:", "Dress codes", "Safety", "Cost", "Where you're going", "Age-appropriateness", "Cultural expectations", "Knowing the actual issue helps.", "Compromise can work", "Maybe you can wear the outfit somewhere else.", "Maybe you change one part.", "Maybe you agree on a budget.", "Maybe you find something similar that they're comfortable with.", "Don't make every clothing disagreement about your identity", "Your outfit being rejected doesn't mean:", "\"My parents don't let me be myself.\"", "Sometimes they just don't like the shirt 😭."], "bigSister": "You're allowed to develop your own style while still learning how to negotiate with the people you're living with.", "journal": "What does my style say about me, and what part of it matters most to me?", "globalNum": "122"}, {"id": "family-28-when-your-family-criticizes-your-appearance", "uid": 123, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "28", "title": "When Your Family Criticizes Your Appearance", "body": ["Comments about your:", "Weight", "Skin", "Hair", "Height", "Clothes", "Body", "Face", "can stick with you way longer than people realize.", "You don't have to accept every comment as truth", "Someone saying:", "\"You've gained weight.\"", "doesn't mean you suddenly need to hate your body.", "Someone saying:", "\"Your skin looks bad.\"", "doesn't determine your beauty.", "Set boundaries when possible", "You can say:", "\"I don't really want comments about my body.\"", "or:", "\"I'm working on feeling better about myself, so I'd rather not discuss my appearance.\"", "Don't punish yourself", "Don't skip meals.", "Don't obsessively exercise.", "Don't change your body because someone made one comment.", "Your body is still developing.", "Find people who make you feel safe", "Talk to people who don't constantly make you feel like your appearance is something that needs fixing."], "bigSister": "You don't have to spend your entire childhood trying to become a version of yourself that everyone approves of.", "journal": "What do I like about myself that has nothing to do with appearance?", "globalNum": "123"}, {"id": "family-29-when-your-parents-don-t-take-your-problems-seriously", "uid": 124, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "29", "title": "When Your Parents Don't Take Your Problems Seriously", "body": ["You say:", "\"I'm really stressed.\"", "And they respond:", "\"You're too young to be stressed.\"", "Girl what 😭.", "Your feelings can be real even when your problems look small to adults", "Something doesn't need to be an adult-sized crisis to affect you.", "School pressure can feel huge.", "Friend problems can hurt.", "Moving can be overwhelming.", "Growing up is confusing.", "Explain the impact", "Instead of:", "\"You never take me seriously.\"", "Try:", "\"I know this might not seem huge to you, but it's been affecting my sleep/school/mood.\"", "Concrete examples can help adults understand.", "If they still don't listen", "Talk to another trusted adult.", "You don't need to keep everything inside just because one person didn't understand."], "bigSister": "Being young doesn't make your feelings fake.", "journal": "What problem have I been minimizing because I don't think people will take me seriously?", "globalNum": "124"}, {"id": "family-30-when-your-parents-are-disappointed-in-you", "uid": 125, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "30", "title": "When Your Parents Are Disappointed in You", "body": ["You got a bad grade.", "Made a mistake.", "Forgot something.", "Didn't do what they expected.", "And now you feel like you've ruined everything.", "A mistake is an event, not an identity", "You made a mistake.", "You aren't a mistake.", "There's a difference.", "Listen to useful criticism", "If you genuinely messed up, own it.", "Say:", "\"I know I should've handled that differently.\"", "Then figure out what you'll do next.", "But don't spiral", "One bad grade doesn't mean you're stupid.", "One mistake doesn't mean you're irresponsible forever.", "One bad decision doesn't define your whole personality.", "Give yourself a chance to recover", "Apologize if necessary.", "Fix what you can.", "Learn from it.", "Then move forward."], "bigSister": "You don't need to punish yourself forever to prove that you're sorry.", "journal": "What did I learn from this mistake, and what can I do differently next time?", "globalNum": "125"}, {"id": "family-31-when-you-disappoint-yourself", "uid": 126, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "31", "title": "When You Disappoint Yourself", "body": ["Sometimes your parents aren't even the problem.", "You're disappointed in you.", "You expected better.", "You thought you'd get the grade.", "You thought you'd stay consistent.", "You thought you'd handle something differently.", "Don't turn disappointment into self-hatred", "You can say:", "\"I'm disappointed.\"", "without saying:", "\"I'm useless.\"", "Figure out what actually happened", "Did you not prepare?", "Were you overwhelmed?", "Did you procrastinate?", "Did something unexpected happen?", "Be honest without being cruel to yourself.", "Make the next attempt better", "Don't just sit in the guilt.", "Ask:", "\"What can I change?\"", "That's where improvement actually happens."], "bigSister": "Holding yourself accountable doesn't require bullying yourself.", "journal": "What would I tell my best friend if they made the same mistake?", "globalNum": "126"}, {"id": "family-32-when-you-feel-responsible-for-your-parents-happiness", "uid": 127, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "32", "title": "When You Feel Responsible for Your Parents' Happiness", "body": ["You might feel like you need to:", "Keep everyone happy.", "Avoid arguments.", "Get perfect grades.", "Never cause problems.", "Always be cheerful.", "You are not responsible for everyone's emotions", "Your parents are adults.", "They have their own emotions, problems, relationships, and responsibilities.", "You can be considerate without becoming responsible for their happiness.", "You are allowed to have bad days", "You don't need to pretend you're fine so nobody else gets uncomfortable.", "You can say:", "\"I'm not feeling great today. I just need some space.\"", "That's okay.", "Especially during family conflict", "Don't feel like you have to choose the \"right\" parent or fix everything.", "You are their child."], "bigSister": "Being a good kid does not mean keeping everyone around you happy 24/7.", "journal": "Whose emotions have I been taking responsibility for lately?", "globalNum": "127"}, {"id": "family-33-when-your-family-doesn-t-respect-your-boundaries", "uid": 128, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "33", "title": "When Your Family Doesn't Respect Your Boundaries", "body": ["You say:", "\"Please don't go through my things.\"", "They do.", "You say:", "\"I don't want to talk about that.\"", "They keep asking.", "You say:", "\"I need some space.\"", "They follow you around.", "It can be frustrating.", "Start by making the boundary clear", "People can't always know what you need unless you tell them.", "Try:", "\"I'd really appreciate it if you'd knock before coming into my room.\"", "or:", "\"I'm not ready to talk about this yet.\"", "Keep your boundary realistic", "You may not be able to have complete privacy while you're still living with your parents.", "Especially when it comes to safety.", "But you can still ask for reasonable respect.", "If a boundary isn't respected", "Don't escalate into a screaming match if you can avoid it.", "Repeat yourself calmly.", "Get another trusted adult involved if necessary.", "Remember:", "A boundary isn't:", "\"I control what you do.\"", "It's:", "\"This is what I will do to protect myself if this continues.\""], "bigSister": "Boundaries aren't about controlling people. They're about communicating what you are and aren't comfortable with.", "journal": "What boundary do I need to communicate more clearly?", "globalNum": "128"}, {"id": "family-34-when-your-family-doesn-t-support-your-interests", "uid": 129, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "34", "title": "When Your Family Doesn't Support Your Interests", "body": ["You love art.", "Or music.", "Or gaming.", "Or coding.", "Or fashion.", "Or sports.", "Or something your family doesn't understand.", "And they're like:", "\"That's not a real career.\"", "😭", "Don't immediately give up", "You don't need to prove your entire future right now.", "Explore the interest.", "Learn.", "Practice.", "Build skills.", "See where it takes you.", "But listen to practical concerns too", "Sometimes adults are worried about stability.", "You can show them you're thinking seriously about it.", "For example:", "\"I know this is competitive, so I'm also learning ___ as a backup skill.\"", "That's different from:", "\"I'm dropping everything to become famous.\"", "Your interests don't need permission to exist", "You are allowed to enjoy something even if it never becomes your career.", "Not every hobby needs to make money."], "bigSister": "Something doesn't have to become your job to be worth doing.", "journal": "What would I spend more time doing if I wasn't worried about whether it was \"useful\"?", "globalNum": "129"}, {"id": "family-35-when-family-members-gossip-about-you", "uid": 130, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "35", "title": "When Family Members Gossip About You", "body": ["Sometimes family gossip is somehow worse than school gossip because these people know EVERYTHING.", "😭", "Don't react to every comment", "You don't need to defend yourself against every random opinion.", "Sometimes silence protects your peace.", "But if something false is being spread", "You can correct it directly.", "\"That's not actually what happened.\"", "Then leave it there.", "Be careful with what you share", "If someone constantly repeats private information, you don't have to tell them everything.", "You can love someone and still keep certain things private.", "Don't become part of the cycle", "If you hate when people gossip about you, try not to spread other people's secrets either."], "bigSister": "You don't have to attend every family argument you're invited to.", "journal": "What information do I want to keep private from certain relatives?", "globalNum": "130"}, {"id": "family-36-when-a-family-member-is-constantly-criticizing-you", "uid": 131, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "36", "title": "When a Family Member Is Constantly Criticizing You", "body": ["Some people have commentary for EVERYTHING.", "Your clothes.", "Your hair.", "Your grades.", "Your voice.", "Your room.", "Your hobbies.", "At some point you're like:", "\"Do you actually like me?\"", "Remember that criticism isn't always truth", "Some people simply communicate through criticism.", "That doesn't mean every comment deserves your attention.", "Decide what's useful", "If someone says:", "\"Your room is messy.\"", "Maybe there's something useful there.", "If they say:", "\"You're lazy and you'll never achieve anything.\"", "That's not constructive criticism.", "That's just hurtful.", "Don't internalize every comment", "You can mentally say:", "\"That's their opinion.\"", "and move on.", "If it becomes constant", "Tell someone you trust.", "Especially if the comments are cruel, humiliating, threatening, or affecting your confidence."], "bigSister": "You don't have to turn every criticism into a personal improvement project.", "journal": "Which criticism is actually useful, and which criticism am I carrying for no reason?", "globalNum": "131"}, {"id": "family-37-when-you-need-to-apologize-to-your-family", "uid": 132, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "37", "title": "When You Need to Apologize to Your Family", "body": ["Sometimes you genuinely messed up.", "Maybe you lied.", "Snapped at someone.", "Broke something.", "Ignored a responsibility.", "A real apology isn't:", "\"I'm sorry you feel that way.\"", "😭", "That's not an apology.", "Try:", "\"I'm sorry I ___. I know it affected you because ___. I should have ___. I'll try to ___ next time.\"", "Short.", "Specific.", "Real.", "Don't add 15 excuses", "You can explain why something happened without using the explanation to avoid responsibility.", "\"I was stressed\" explains it.", "It doesn't automatically excuse hurting someone.", "And remember:", "Apologizing doesn't make you weak.", "It shows maturity."], "bigSister": "A genuine apology isn't losing an argument. It's taking responsibility.", "journal": "Is there anyone I owe a real apology to?", "globalNum": "132"}, {"id": "family-38-when-your-parents-won-t-apologize", "uid": 133, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "38", "title": "When Your Parents Won't Apologize", "body": ["This one is harder.", "Because sometimes adults make mistakes too.", "And sometimes they absolutely refuse to admit it.", "Their lack of apology doesn't mean you imagined what happened", "You can recognize that something hurt you even if they don't acknowledge it.", "Don't spend forever trying to force an apology", "You might never get the exact words you want.", "That doesn't mean you can't heal.", "Focus on what you can control", "You can decide:", "What boundaries you need.", "What conversations you will have.", "What behaviour you will repeat.", "What kind of person you want to become.", "But don't confuse forgiveness with pretending", "You can forgive someone eventually without acting like what happened was okay.", "And you don't have to rush forgiveness."], "bigSister": "Sometimes closure doesn't come from someone saying sorry. Sometimes it comes from understanding that you deserved better and choosing what happens next.", "journal": "What do I wish they would acknowledge, and what can I do even if they never do?", "globalNum": "133"}, {"id": "family-39-when-you-feel-guilty-for-wanting-more", "uid": 134, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "39", "title": "When You Feel Guilty for Wanting More", "body": ["You have food.", "A home.", "School.", "Family.", "And you're still unhappy about something.", "Then you think:", "\"I'm so ungrateful.\"", "No.", "Gratitude and dissatisfaction can exist together", "You can appreciate what you have and still want something to improve.", "You can be grateful for your family and still want more privacy.", "You can appreciate your home and still want your own space.", "You can be grateful for your life and still struggle sometimes.", "Don't use gratitude to silence yourself", "Instead ask:", "\"What am I grateful for?\"", "and:", "\"What would make my life better?\"", "Both questions are valid.", "Be careful with comparison", "Someone always has more.", "Someone always has less.", "Comparing yourself endlessly won't make you happier."], "bigSister": "Being grateful doesn't mean you have to pretend everything is perfect.", "journal": "What am I grateful for, and what is one thing I genuinely want to improve?", "globalNum": "134"}, {"id": "family-40-growing-up-while-still-being-a-kid", "uid": 135, "category": "family", "categoryLabel": "Family", "num": "40", "title": "Growing Up While Still Being a Kid", "body": ["This is probably the biggest family thing of all.", "Everyone keeps telling you:", "\"You're growing up.\"", "But sometimes you don't feel grown.", "You still want to watch stupid videos.", "Eat snacks.", "Laugh at dumb jokes.", "Have your parents take care of things.", "And that's okay.", "You don't have to rush adulthood", "Being mature doesn't mean becoming serious all the time.", "You can learn responsibility while still having fun.", "You can become independent while still needing help.", "You can have big goals while still being young.", "Don't let the internet convince you that you need your entire life figured out", "You don't.", "You are still learning who you are.", "Your opinions will change.", "Your style will change.", "Your friendships will change.", "Your goals will change.", "That's normal.", "Growing up isn't becoming a completely different person", "It's learning more about yourself.", "Learning how to make decisions.", "Learning from mistakes.", "Learning how to treat people.", "Learning how to take care of yourself.", "You have time", "Seriously.", "You do.", "You don't need to know your career.", "Your future partner.", "Where you'll live.", "What you'll become.", "All of it.", "Right now, you just need to keep learning."], "bigSister": "You don't have to speedrun childhood just because adulthood is coming. Let yourself be young. You'll have plenty of time to be grown later.", "journal": "What part of being young do I want to enjoy more before I grow up?", "globalNum": "135"}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "1", "title": "Puberty", "body": ["Puberty is basically your body deciding:", "\"Let's change literally everything at once.\"", "😭", "Your skin changes.", "Your body shape changes.", "You grow hair in places you didn't have it before.", "Your emotions can feel completely random.", "You might suddenly feel awkward in your own body.", "And guess what?", "That's normal.", "Everyone develops differently", "Some people get their period earlier.", "Some later.", "Some grow taller quickly.", "Some barely grow for a while.", "Some get acne.", "Some don't.", "Some develop curves early.", "Some develop later.", "There isn't one correct puberty timeline.", "Don't compare your body to your friends", "You might look around school and think:", "\"Why don't I look like them?\"", "Because you're not them.", "Your body has its own schedule.", "Things might feel weird for a while", "Your body isn't supposed to look exactly the same from age 11 to 18.", "You're literally developing.", "Give yourself time.", "Ask questions", "If something about puberty confuses you, ask a trusted adult, doctor, nurse, or another reliable source.", "Being curious about your body isn't embarrassing."], "bigSister": "You aren't \"behind\" because your body hasn't developed exactly like someone else's.", "journal": "What change in my body am I still getting used to?", "id": "growing-up-1-puberty", "globalNum": "136", "uid": 136}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "2", "title": "Your First Period", "body": ["Getting your first period can be exciting, terrifying, annoying, confusing, or all four.", "Especially if it happens somewhere inconvenient.", "Like school.", "Of course it would.", "😭", "First: don't panic", "Periods are a normal part of growing up.", "You might have:", "☐ Bleeding", "☐ Cramps", "☐ Mood changes", "☐ Bloating", "☐ Tiredness", "☐ Headaches", "☐ Sore breasts", "Not everyone experiences all of these.", "Have an emergency kit", "Keep a small pouch with:", "☐ Pads", "☐ Spare underwear", "☐ Tissues/wipes", "☐ A plastic or reusable bag", "☐ Pain relief that you're allowed to take", "☐ Maybe an extra pair of shorts", "You don't need a giant suitcase.", "Just enough to feel prepared.", "If it happens at school", "Ask a teacher, school nurse, friend, or trusted adult for help.", "You are not the first person this has happened to at school.", "Track your period", "You don't need to obsess over it.", "Just knowing approximately when it comes can help you prepare.", "Know when to ask for help", "If your periods are extremely painful, very heavy, make you regularly miss school, or something feels seriously wrong, tell a trusted adult and speak to a healthcare professional.", "You don't have to silently suffer because:", "\"Periods are supposed to hurt.\"", "Some discomfort can be normal.", "Severe problems deserve attention.", "It's literally biology."], "bigSister": "Your period isn't something you need to hide like you're committing a crime.", "journal": "What would make my period days easier and less stressful?", "id": "growing-up-2-your-first-period", "globalNum": "137", "uid": 137}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "3", "title": "Body Changes", "body": ["One day your clothes fit perfectly.", "Then suddenly:", "\"Why are these jeans fighting for their lives?\"", "😭", "Your body can change quickly during puberty.", "Clothes fitting differently doesn't mean something is wrong", "Your body might grow taller.", "Your hips may change.", "Your chest may develop.", "Your waist may change.", "Your body proportions can shift.", "That's normal.", "Don't panic over every change", "You might look different from a photo you took six months ago.", "That's because six months passed.", "You're growing.", "Don't let the internet become your measuring tape", "Social media is full of:", "☐ Posing", "☐ Filters", "☐ Angles", "☐ Editing", "☐ Makeup", "☐ Lighting", "☐ Carefully selected photos", "Comparing your everyday body to somebody's most curated photo is unfair.", "Your body is not a project you need to finish", "You don't have to reach some magical \"perfect\" body.", "Your body is going to keep changing."], "bigSister": "Growing into your body takes time. You don't need to love every single thing about it every day. Start by treating it like it's yours, not like it's your enemy.", "journal": "What does my body allow me to do that I'm grateful for?", "id": "growing-up-3-body-changes", "globalNum": "138", "uid": 138}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "4", "title": "Acne", "body": ["Acne can make you feel like your face is the first thing everyone notices.", "You wake up.", "Look in the mirror.", "And there's a new spot.", "\"Oh, so we're fighting today.\"", "😭", "First: acne is normal", "It doesn't mean you're dirty.", "It doesn't mean you don't wash your face.", "It doesn't mean you're unattractive.", "Hormones can play a huge role in acne.", "Don't pick everything", "I KNOW.", "You want to.", "But constantly squeezing spots can irritate your skin and increase the chance of marks.", "Keep your routine simple", "You don't need 17 skincare products.", "A basic routine can be enough:", "☐ Gentle cleanser", "☐ Moisturizer", "☐ Sunscreen", "Then add acne treatments if appropriate.", "Be patient", "Skincare isn't usually:", "Day 1: acne", "Day 2: glass skin", "😭", "It can take time.", "Don't let acne control your life", "You can still take pictures.", "Go outside.", "Wear makeup if you want.", "Go to school.", "Talk to people.", "Your face does not need to be perfectly clear for you to live your life.", "Get help if it's severe", "If acne is painful, severe, scarring, or really affecting your confidence, talk to a doctor or dermatologist.", "There are treatments."], "bigSister": "Your skin is allowed to have bad days without you deciding you're ugly.", "journal": "How would I treat my friend if they felt ugly because of acne?", "id": "growing-up-4-acne", "globalNum": "139", "uid": 139}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "5", "title": "Braces", "body": ["Braces can make you feel like:", "\"Great. Now my teeth have accessories.\"", "😭", "Maybe you hate how they look.", "Maybe you're worried people will notice.", "Maybe you're scared they'll hurt.", "You're not the only one", "A LOT of people have braces.", "And most people notice them way less than you think.", "Don't hide your smile", "You don't need to spend two years covering your mouth every time you laugh.", "Smile.", "Take pictures.", "Be normal.", "Follow your orthodontist's instructions", "Yes, the boring stuff matters.", "Brush properly.", "Follow food restrictions.", "Wear elastics if you're told to.", "Go to appointments.", "Your future teeth will thank you.", "And remember:", "Braces aren't permanent.", "They're literally there because you're working toward something."], "bigSister": "You don't have to wait until your teeth are \"perfect\" before you're allowed to smile.", "journal": "What would I do differently if I stopped worrying about people noticing my braces?", "id": "growing-up-5-braces", "globalNum": "140", "uid": 140}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "6", "title": "Body Hair", "body": ["Leg hair.", "Arm hair.", "Armpit hair.", "Facial hair.", "Pubic hair.", "Suddenly you're basically a human chia pet.", "😭", "Body hair is normal", "Some people have lots.", "Some have very little.", "Some have dark hair.", "Some have light hair.", "Genetics plays a huge role.", "Removing it is a choice", "You can:", "☐ Shave", "☐ Trim", "☐ Wax", "☐ Use hair-removal products", "☐ Bleach some body hair", "☐ Leave it alone", "None of these makes you more or less feminine, attractive, clean, or grown.", "Don't let people shame you", "Someone might prefer shaved legs.", "Someone else might not care.", "That's their preference.", "Your body doesn't exist to meet everyone's preference.", "If you remove hair, do it safely", "Use products correctly.", "Don't use harsh chemicals on sensitive areas.", "Don't shave aggressively just because you want perfectly smooth skin.", "Irritation is not the goal."], "bigSister": "Having body hair doesn't make you dirty. Removing it doesn't make you vain. It's your choice.", "journal": "Am I removing body hair because I want to, or because I feel like I'm supposed to?", "id": "growing-up-6-body-hair", "globalNum": "141", "uid": 141}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "7", "title": "Feeling Ugly", "body": ["This feeling can hit HARD during your teenage years.", "You look in the mirror and suddenly decide:", "\"Yeah, I'm actually hideous.\"", "Then three days later you're taking 47 selfies.", "Human beings are weird 😭.", "Your perception changes", "Your mood can affect how you see yourself.", "When you're tired, stressed, insecure, or comparing yourself to people online, you may judge yourself much more harshly.", "Don't make permanent decisions based on temporary insecurity", "Don't suddenly cut all your hair.", "Change everything about yourself.", "Crash diet.", "Spend money you don't have.", "Because you hated one picture.", "Give yourself time.", "Find things you genuinely like", "Not:", "\"I'm the prettiest person alive.\"", "You don't need to convince yourself of that.", "Start smaller:", "\"I like my eyes.\"", "\"I like my hair today.\"", "\"I like how this outfit looks.\"", "\"I like my smile.\"", "Small confidence is still confidence.", "And remember:", "Attractiveness isn't one specific face.", "There isn't a single correct way to look."], "bigSister": "You don't need to think you're gorgeous every morning. You just need to stop treating yourself like someone you hate.", "journal": "What is one feature I can learn to appreciate instead of constantly criticizing?", "id": "growing-up-7-feeling-ugly", "globalNum": "142", "uid": 142}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "8", "title": "Comparing Yourself to Other Girls", "body": ["She's prettier.", "She's thinner.", "Her hair is better.", "She has more friends.", "Her outfits are better.", "She's more confident.", "Her life looks perfect.", "And suddenly you're competing in a competition she doesn't even know exists.", "😭", "Comparison usually shows you one side", "You see her:", "☐ Best outfit", "☐ Best selfie", "☐ Best grades", "☐ Best friend group", "☐ Best moments", "You don't see everything else.", "Don't turn admiration into self-hatred", "You can think:", "\"Her hair is gorgeous.\"", "without:", "\"Mine is disgusting.\"", "You can think:", "\"She's really good at school.\"", "without:", "\"I'm stupid.\"", "Someone else's strengths don't cancel yours.", "Use comparison as information", "If you genuinely admire something, ask:", "\"What exactly do I like about this?\"", "Maybe it's her style.", "Her confidence.", "Her organization.", "Her creativity.", "Then learn from it instead of hating yourself."], "bigSister": "You can admire someone without turning them into proof that you're not enough.", "journal": "What exactly am I jealous of, and is there a healthy way to work toward it?", "id": "growing-up-8-comparing-yourself-to-other-girls", "globalNum": "143", "uid": 143}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "9", "title": "Social Media Pressure", "body": ["Social media can make it feel like everyone is:", "Beautiful.", "Rich.", "Popular.", "Dating.", "Travelling.", "Getting amazing grades.", "Having perfect rooms.", "And somehow drinking green juice at 6 a.m.", "Meanwhile you're in bed eating cereal.", "😭", "Remember what you're seeing", "Social media is a highlight reel.", "People choose what to post.", "They don't usually upload:", "\"Here's me crying because I feel behind.\"", "Curate your feed", "If an account constantly makes you feel bad about yourself:", "Mute it.", "Unfollow it.", "Block it if necessary.", "You don't owe anyone your attention.", "Don't measure your life in likes", "Likes aren't a measurement of:", "☐ Beauty", "☐ Worth", "☐ Popularity", "☐ Success", "☐ Importance", "The algorithm doesn't know your value.", "Take breaks", "You don't need to delete every app forever.", "Even putting your phone down for an hour can help your brain breathe."], "bigSister": "If an app consistently makes you hate your life, you're allowed to use it less.", "journal": "Which accounts make me feel good about myself, and which ones make me feel worse?", "id": "growing-up-9-social-media-pressure", "globalNum": "144", "uid": 144}, {"category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "10", "title": "Finding Your Own Style", "body": ["Finding your style can be confusing because suddenly everyone has an aesthetic.", "Clean girl.", "Streetwear.", "Y2K.", "Coquette.", "Old money.", "Whatever TikTok has decided is the new personality this week 😭.", "You don't need one aesthetic", "You can like baggy jeans AND cute dresses.", "Sneakers AND heels.", "Pink AND black.", "You don't need to fit into one category.", "Start with what you actually like", "Save outfits.", "Notice patterns.", "What colours do you wear?", "What silhouettes do you like?", "What shoes do you keep choosing?", "What outfits make you feel comfortable?", "That's how you start figuring yourself out.", "Don't buy an entire new wardrobe every time TikTok changes its mind", "Trends disappear.", "Build around pieces you genuinely love.", "Your style will change", "You might look back at your old outfits and think:", "\"Girl... who let me leave the house?\"", "That's normal.", "You were experimenting."], "bigSister": "Style is supposed to be fun, not another exam you're scared of failing.", "journal": "If nobody could judge my clothes, what would I actually wear?", "id": "growing-up-10-finding-your-own-style", "globalNum": "145", "uid": 145}, {"id": "growing-up-11-learning-to-say-no", "uid": 146, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "11", "title": "Learning to Say No", "body": ["Saying no sounds easy until you actually have to do it.", "Someone asks you to go somewhere.", "You don't want to.", "Your friend asks you for a favour.", "You don't have the energy.", "Someone wants you to do something you're uncomfortable with.", "And suddenly your mouth says:", "\"Yeah, sure.\"", "while your brain is screaming:", "\"WHY DID WE AGREE??\"", "😭", "You don't need a dramatic reason", "\"No\" is a complete answer.", "You can also say:", "\"I can't.\"", "\"I'm not comfortable with that.\"", "\"I don't want to.\"", "\"Maybe another time.\"", "You don't have to make everyone happy", "People might be disappointed.", "That doesn't automatically mean you did something wrong.", "Someone being upset because you said no doesn't mean you should've said yes.", "Start small", "Say no to little things.", "Don't want to lend something?", "\"No.\"", "Don't want to go somewhere?", "\"I can't today.\"", "The more you practice, the easier it becomes.", "You can be kind AND have boundaries", "You don't need to become rude.", "You can say:", "\"I love you, but I can't do that.\"", "That's still a boundary."], "bigSister": "If saying yes makes you resent someone, while saying no makes you feel guilty, you probably need to practice saying no more.", "journal": "Where in my life do I say yes when I actually mean no?", "globalNum": "146"}, {"id": "growing-up-12-perfectionism", "uid": 147, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "12", "title": "Perfectionism", "body": ["You want the perfect grade.", "Perfect room.", "Perfect outfit.", "Perfect skin.", "Perfect routine.", "Perfect everything.", "And when you don't achieve it:", "\"I'm a failure.\"", "No 😭.", "Perfectionism can look productive", "Sometimes it makes you work really hard.", "But it can also make you procrastinate because you're scared you won't do something perfectly.", "You think:", "\"If I can't do it perfectly, why start?\"", "That's the trap.", "Aim for good, not impossible", "A finished assignment is better than a perfect assignment that never gets submitted.", "A messy drawing is better than an empty page.", "A 30-minute workout is better than waiting for the perfect hour.", "Mistakes are part of learning", "You're supposed to be bad at things before you become good.", "Nobody starts amazing.", "Don't make your achievements your personality", "You can get a bad grade and still be smart.", "You can fail something and still be capable.", "You can make mistakes and still be proud of yourself."], "bigSister": "\"Perfect\" is a moving target. You'll spend forever chasing it.", "journal": "What am I afraid will happen if I do something imperfectly?", "globalNum": "147"}, {"id": "growing-up-13-overthinking-everything", "uid": 148, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "13", "title": "Overthinking Everything", "body": ["You said something weird.", "They looked at you funny.", "Your friend replied differently.", "Your teacher sounded annoyed.", "Now your brain has opened 37 tabs.", "😭", "Ask yourself: What do I know?", "Not what you think.", "Not what you're afraid happened.", "What do you actually know?", "Example:", "Fact: They haven't replied.", "Thought: They're angry with me.", "Those aren't the same thing.", "Don't solve imaginary problems", "If you don't have evidence something is wrong, don't spend three hours preparing for the worst.", "Give your brain somewhere else to go", "Take a shower.", "Go outside.", "Clean something.", "Draw.", "Listen to music.", "Talk to someone.", "Sometimes you need to physically interrupt the thought loop.", "If you're stuck in the same worry constantly", "Write it down.", "Then write:", "\"Can I control this?\"", "If yes, decide one action.", "If no, practice letting it sit without trying to solve it."], "bigSister": "Your brain can make a guess feel like a fact. Check the evidence before believing it.", "journal": "What am I worried about right now, and what evidence do I actually have?", "globalNum": "148"}, {"id": "growing-up-14-anxiety-before-sleeping", "uid": 149, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "14", "title": "Anxiety Before Sleeping", "body": ["It's 11:47 p.m.", "Suddenly your brain remembers every embarrassing thing you've done since birth.", "Perfect.", "😭", "Your brain gets louder when everything else gets quiet", "During the day, you're distracted.", "At night, there's nothing else happening.", "So your brain starts thinking.", "Create a \"brain dump\"", "Before bed, write down:", "Things you need to remember", "Things you're worried about", "Things you need to do tomorrow", "Your brain doesn't need to keep repeating them if they're written somewhere.", "Don't argue with every thought", "If your brain says:", "\"What if something goes wrong tomorrow?\"", "You don't need to spend 30 minutes proving that it won't.", "Try:", "\"Maybe. I'll deal with it if it happens.\"", "Then return to what you're doing.", "Make your room feel like a sleep zone", "Dim lights.", "Put your phone away when you can.", "Get comfortable.", "Do something calm.", "If anxiety is regularly stopping you from sleeping", "Tell a trusted adult.", "Constant sleep problems deserve support."], "bigSister": "You don't have to solve your entire life at 1 a.m. Tomorrow exists.", "journal": "What can I leave for tomorrow instead of trying to solve tonight?", "globalNum": "149"}, {"id": "growing-up-15-feeling-lonely", "uid": 150, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "15", "title": "Feeling Lonely", "body": ["Loneliness isn't always being physically alone.", "You can be surrounded by people and still feel lonely.", "Don't wait until someone magically notices", "Send the message.", "\"Wanna call?\"", "\"Do you want to hang out?\"", "\"I haven't talked to you in forever.\"", "People are often waiting for someone else to make the first move too.", "Try joining something", "A club.", "Sport.", "Class.", "Volunteer activity.", "Online community with appropriate safety boundaries.", "Anywhere you can repeatedly see the same people.", "Friendships usually grow through repeated interaction.", "Don't settle for terrible friends just because you're lonely", "Being surrounded by people who make you feel unwanted can be worse than having a little alone time.", "Learn to enjoy your own company too", "Watch something.", "Read.", "Make something.", "Go for a walk.", "Listen to music.", "Have a little solo time.", "Being alone and being lonely aren't identical."], "bigSister": "Loneliness is a feeling, not proof that nobody likes you.", "journal": "What kind of connection am I actually missing right now?", "globalNum": "150"}, {"id": "growing-up-16-feeling-left-behind", "uid": 151, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "16", "title": "Feeling Left Behind", "body": ["Everyone seems to be doing something before you.", "Someone has their first relationship.", "Someone's already good at makeup.", "Someone has their driver's permit.", "Someone has amazing grades.", "Someone is already making money.", "And you're like:", "\"Uh... am I late?\"", "No.", "There is no universal timeline", "People develop different skills at different ages.", "Someone being ahead in one area doesn't mean they're ahead in life.", "Social media makes this worse", "You might see someone your age making money online and think:", "\"I should already be doing that.\"", "But you don't know their circumstances.", "And you don't need to copy their timeline.", "Ask:", "\"What do I actually want?\"", "Not:", "\"What am I supposed to have by now?\"", "That's a completely different question.", "Focus on your next step", "Not your entire future.", "Just the next thing.", "Study.", "Practice.", "Apply.", "Learn.", "Try."], "bigSister": "You're not behind. You're just not living the same timeline as everyone else.", "journal": "What am I rushing myself to achieve, and why?", "globalNum": "151"}, {"id": "growing-up-17-phone-addiction", "uid": 152, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "17", "title": "Phone Addiction", "body": ["You check your phone.", "Five minutes later:", "\"Wait... why am I still here?\"", "😭", "Phones are literally designed to keep you coming back.", "So don't treat this like you're just \"weak.\"", "Notice your triggers", "Do you grab your phone when you're:", "Bored?", "Sad?", "Stressed?", "Avoiding homework?", "Lonely?", "Tired?", "Once you know the trigger, you can replace the habit.", "Make your phone slightly harder to reach", "Put it across the room.", "Turn off unnecessary notifications.", "Move distracting apps away from your home screen.", "Use app limits if they're helpful.", "Don't try to go from 7 hours to zero", "You'll probably last two days and then go feral.", "Start smaller.", "Maybe no phone during meals.", "No phone during the first 30 minutes after waking.", "Phone away while studying.", "Give yourself something else to do", "If you remove your phone and have absolutely nothing else planned, boredom will win.", "Read.", "Draw.", "Clean.", "Exercise.", "Play music.", "Talk to someone.", "Make something."], "bigSister": "The goal isn't to hate your phone. It's to make sure your phone isn't controlling your attention.", "journal": "When do I reach for my phone without actually wanting to use it?", "globalNum": "152"}, {"id": "growing-up-18-procrastination", "uid": 153, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "18", "title": "Procrastination", "body": ["You have an assignment due tomorrow.", "You have known about it for two weeks.", "Suddenly cleaning your entire room sounds extremely important.", "😭", "Procrastination usually isn't laziness", "Sometimes you're overwhelmed.", "Sometimes you're scared you'll do badly.", "Sometimes the task feels too boring or complicated.", "Make the task smaller", "Don't think:", "\"I have to finish this entire project.\"", "Think:", "\"I'm going to open the document.\"", "Then:", "\"I'm going to write the title.\"", "Then:", "\"I'm going to write three bullet points.\"", "Starting is often the hardest part.", "Try the 10-minute rule", "Tell yourself:", "\"I'll do this for ten minutes.\"", "After ten minutes, you can decide whether to continue.", "Usually you've already built some momentum.", "Don't wait to feel motivated", "Motivation is unreliable.", "Sometimes you have to start first.", "Then motivation catches up."], "bigSister": "You don't need to feel ready to begin. Start badly. Improve it later.", "journal": "What's the smallest possible step I can take on the thing I'm avoiding?", "globalNum": "153"}, {"id": "growing-up-19-building-a-routine", "uid": 154, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "19", "title": "Building a Routine", "body": ["You make a beautiful routine.", "Wake up at 6.", "Exercise.", "Read.", "Study.", "Skincare.", "Journal.", "Meditate.", "Drink 47 litres of water.", "Day 3:", "\"Yeah so that didn't happen.\"", "😭", "Make your routine realistic", "Don't build a routine for your imaginary most productive self.", "Build one for you.", "Maybe:", "Morning: Get ready, Eat, School", "After school: Rest, Homework, Dinner", "Night: Shower, Skincare, Prepare for tomorrow, Relax, Sleep", "That's already a routine.", "Anchor habits to things you already do", "After brushing your teeth → skincare.", "After getting home → change clothes.", "After dinner → pack your bag.", "This makes habits easier to remember.", "Don't restart every time you mess up", "Missed Monday?", "Cool.", "Continue Tuesday.", "You don't need:", "\"I'll restart next month.\"", "😭", "Consistency beats intensity", "Doing something small regularly is better than doing an insane routine twice."], "bigSister": "A routine should make your life easier, not become another thing you're failing at.", "journal": "What three habits would genuinely make my days better?", "globalNum": "154"}, {"id": "growing-up-20-learning-discipline", "uid": 155, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "20", "title": "Learning Discipline", "body": ["Discipline sounds scary until you realize it's mostly:", "\"Doing something even when I don't feel like it.\"", "Start tiny", "Want to study? Do 15 minutes.", "Want to exercise? Do 10 minutes.", "Want to clean? Clean one area.", "Make good choices easier", "Put your schoolwork somewhere visible.", "Keep your water bottle nearby.", "Put your workout clothes where you can see them.", "Remove distractions when you need to focus.", "Don't depend entirely on motivation", "Some days you'll feel productive.", "Some days you'll feel like a potato.", "You still need to do the important things.", "But discipline doesn't mean never resting", "Rest is not laziness.", "You aren't supposed to be productive every second.", "Learn your limits", "If you're exhausted, sometimes the disciplined thing is sleeping.", "Not forcing yourself through another three hours of work."], "bigSister": "Discipline isn't being harsh with yourself. It's keeping promises to yourself while still knowing when you need rest.", "journal": "What is one small promise I can keep to myself every day this week?", "globalNum": "155"}, {"id": "growing-up-21-self-care", "uid": 156, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "21", "title": "Self-Care", "body": ["Self-care has somehow become:", "\"Buy a $60 candle, do a 14-step skincare routine and wake up at 5 a.m.\"", "Girl, no 😭.", "Real self-care is usually much less aesthetic.", "Sometimes self-care is:", "Taking a shower because you've been putting it off.", "Eating something because you haven't eaten properly.", "Going to bed instead of staying up scrolling.", "Cleaning your room because the mess is stressing you out.", "Taking a break.", "Saying no.", "Talking to someone.", "Getting help.", "You don't need to spend money", "You don't need a shopping haul to take care of yourself.", "A shower, clean clothes, music, food and sleep can genuinely change your whole mood.", "Self-care isn't always fun", "Sometimes it's doing something you don't want to do because future-you will be grateful.", "Studying.", "Cleaning.", "Going to an appointment.", "Drinking water.", "Putting your phone down.", "Don't use self-care as another way to judge yourself", "You don't need a perfect morning routine to be doing okay."], "bigSister": "Self-care isn't making your life look perfect. It's taking care of the person who actually has to live it.", "journal": "What do I need today: rest, fun, connection, organisation, or help?", "globalNum": "156"}, {"id": "growing-up-22-building-confidence", "uid": 157, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "22", "title": "Building Confidence", "body": ["Confidence isn't waking up thinking:", "\"I'm the most amazing person alive.\"", "Confidence is more like:", "\"I'm nervous, but I'm doing it anyway.\"", "Start keeping promises to yourself", "If you say you're going to study for 20 minutes, do it.", "If you say you're going to clean your room, do it.", "If you say you're going to stop texting someone who treats you badly, actually stop.", "Every time you keep a promise to yourself, you build trust with yourself.", "Do things that scare you a little", "Answer a question in class.", "Talk to someone new.", "Wear the outfit.", "Try the hobby.", "Ask the question.", "Not terrifying things.", "Just small things that make you uncomfortable.", "Stop waiting to \"feel confident\"", "Confidence often comes after you do something.", "You don't always feel brave first.", "And don't confuse confidence with being loud", "Quiet people can be confident.", "Shy people can be confident.", "You don't have to become the loudest person in the room."], "bigSister": "Confidence is trusting yourself, not thinking you're better than everyone else.", "journal": "What would I do if I trusted myself a little more?", "globalNum": "157"}, {"id": "growing-up-23-not-knowing-what-you-want-to-do-with-your-future", "uid": 158, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "23", "title": "Not Knowing What You Want to Do With Your Future", "body": ["Someone asks:", "\"What do you want to be when you grow up?\"", "And you're like:", "\"Um... alive?\"", "😭", "You don't need a career plan at 13", "Seriously.", "You can have interests without knowing your exact career.", "Maybe you like: Design, Medicine, Business, Technology, Writing, Fashion, Law, Art, Science", "Explore.", "Try things before committing", "Watch tutorials.", "Take classes.", "Make little projects.", "Read about careers.", "Talk to people who actually work in those fields.", "Your first idea doesn't have to be your final idea", "People change careers.", "You can change your mind.", "You can discover something completely random later.", "Focus on skills", "Instead of:", "\"I need to know my exact career.\"", "Ask:", "\"What skills would help me in almost any future?\"", "Communication. Writing. Problem-solving. Technology. Financial literacy. Organisation. Creativity.", "Those travel with you."], "bigSister": "You don't need to know where you're going to start walking.", "journal": "What are three things I'm curious enough to explore?", "globalNum": "158"}, {"id": "growing-up-24-feeling-pressure-to-have-your-life-figured-out", "uid": 159, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "24", "title": "Feeling Pressure to Have Your Life Figured Out", "body": ["Sometimes it feels like everyone expects you to already know:", "What school. What career. What country. What university. What relationship. What your entire life will look like.", "Relax 😭.", "You're allowed to be undecided", "Being undecided doesn't mean you're unmotivated.", "It can mean you're still gathering information.", "Don't confuse other people's certainty with actual certainty", "Someone saying:", "\"I'm definitely going to become a surgeon.\"", "doesn't mean they actually know their future.", "They may change their mind later.", "Make short-term plans", "Instead of planning your entire life:", "This year: What do I want to improve?", "Next year: What do I want to try?", "Later: What options do I want to keep open?", "That's enough.", "Your future isn't one decision", "Your life is a bunch of decisions over time."], "bigSister": "You don't need a five-year plan when you're still figuring out what you like.", "journal": "What do I want my life to feel like, even if I don't know what it will look like?", "globalNum": "159"}, {"id": "growing-up-25-turning-18-anxiety", "uid": 160, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "25", "title": "Turning 18 Anxiety", "body": ["Eighteen sounds like some magical deadline where the government hands you a suitcase and says:", "\"Good luck.\"", "😭", "Being 18 doesn't instantly make you an adult expert", "You won't wake up knowing how to:", "Pay every bill. Cook 40 meals. Understand taxes. Pick the perfect career. Manage every emotion. Know what you're doing.", "Nobody does.", "Learn things gradually", "You can start learning:", "Money. Cooking. Laundry. Appointments. Basic documents. Communication. Time management. Personal safety.", "You don't need to master everything immediately.", "Adulthood is a process", "You'll still call people for help.", "You'll still make mistakes.", "You'll still have questions.", "That's normal."], "bigSister": "Turning 18 is a birthday, not a personality update. You don't suddenly become a different species.", "journal": "What adult skill would make me feel more prepared?", "globalNum": "160"}, {"id": "growing-up-26-becoming-more-independent", "uid": 161, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "26", "title": "Becoming More Independent", "body": ["Independence sounds like freedom.", "But it also means:", "\"Wait... I have to remember this myself?\"", "😭", "Start practicing now", "Learn how to: Make simple meals, Wash clothes, Keep track of appointments, Organise schoolwork, Manage money, Take care of belongings, Communicate with adults, Make decisions", "Don't wait until you desperately need a skill", "Learn it when the stakes are low.", "Burning toast at 13 is funny.", "Burning your first meal when you're responsible for feeding yourself every day?", "Less funny.", "😭", "Ask adults to teach you", "Instead of:", "\"I'll figure it out.\"", "Say:", "\"Can you show me how to do this?\"", "That's actually smart.", "Independence doesn't mean never asking for help", "Adults ask for help too."], "bigSister": "Being independent isn't doing everything alone. It's knowing what you can handle and knowing when to ask.", "journal": "What is one thing my parents usually do for me that I could learn myself?", "globalNum": "161"}, {"id": "growing-up-27-learning-about-money", "uid": 162, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "27", "title": "Learning About Money", "body": ["Money is one of those things school somehow forgets to teach you.", "You can solve algebra but nobody explained budgeting.", "😭", "Start with the basics", "When you get money, think:", "Spend — Things you actually need or want.", "Save — Money you're keeping for later.", "Give — If you want to and are able to.", "You don't need complicated spreadsheets.", "Don't spend everything immediately", "If you get ₦20,000 and immediately spend ₦20,000, future-you gets nothing.", "Even saving a small amount teaches the habit.", "Learn the difference between wanting something and needing it", "Before buying something, ask:", "\"Would I still want this in a week?\"", "If yes, maybe.", "If no, it might've just been impulse.", "Don't compare spending", "Someone having expensive things doesn't mean they're financially successful.", "You don't know their situation."], "bigSister": "Learning about money early gives you a huge advantage later.", "journal": "What do I usually spend money on, and which purchases do I actually value?", "globalNum": "162"}, {"id": "growing-up-28-being-scared-of-failure", "uid": 163, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "28", "title": "Being Scared of Failure", "body": ["You want to try something.", "But what if you suck?", "What if people laugh?", "What if you fail?", "Here's the annoying truth:", "You probably WILL fail at some things.", "Everyone does.", "The goal isn't avoiding failure.", "It's learning how to survive it.", "Separate failure from identity", "\"I failed the test.\" is different from \"I'm stupid.\"", "\"My project didn't work.\" is different from \"I'm bad at everything.\"", "One describes an event.", "The other attacks your identity.", "Let yourself be a beginner", "You're supposed to be bad before you're good.", "That's literally how learning works.", "Ask:", "\"What did this teach me?\"", "Instead of:", "\"What does this say about me?\""], "bigSister": "Failure is information. It doesn't have to be a verdict.", "journal": "What would I try if I knew failing wouldn't make me a failure?", "globalNum": "163"}, {"id": "growing-up-29-fear-of-embarrassing-yourself", "uid": 164, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "29", "title": "Fear of Embarrassing Yourself", "body": ["You trip.", "Say something weird.", "Answer incorrectly.", "Fall in front of people.", "Send a message to the wrong person.", "And suddenly:", "\"I need to move countries.\"", "😭", "People usually care less than you think", "Everyone is busy worrying about themselves.", "That embarrassing thing you can't stop thinking about?", "There's a decent chance nobody else remembers it.", "Laugh when you can", "If you accidentally say something weird:", "\"That came out so wrong 😭.\"", "And move on.", "You don't have to make it a huge event.", "Don't avoid everything because you're scared", "If fear of embarrassment stops you from speaking, trying things, meeting people, or participating, you're giving the fear too much control.", "Remember:", "Being embarrassed isn't dangerous.", "It's uncomfortable.", "And uncomfortable feelings pass."], "bigSister": "You are allowed to be cringe. Everyone is cringe sometimes. That's literally being human.", "journal": "What's something embarrassing I survived that felt like the end of the world at the time?", "globalNum": "164"}, {"id": "growing-up-30-caring-too-much-about-what-people-think", "uid": 165, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "30", "title": "Caring Too Much About What People Think", "body": ["You change your outfit.", "Delete the photo.", "Rewrite the text.", "Don't raise your hand.", "Don't post the thing.", "Don't try the hobby.", "Because:", "\"What will people think?\"", "Ask yourself:", "\"Will I care about their opinion in five years?\"", "Probably not.", "Not everyone's opinion deserves equal weight", "Your best friend's opinion? Maybe.", "A teacher you respect? Probably.", "A random person from school who barely knows you? Why are we giving them board-member status? 😭", "You don't need universal approval", "Some people won't like your personality.", "Some won't like your style.", "Some won't agree with your choices.", "You can still be okay.", "Build your own standards", "Ask:", "\"Do I like this?\" \"Is this kind?\" \"Is this safe?\" \"Does this fit my values?\"", "Those questions matter more than:", "\"Will everyone approve?\""], "bigSister": "If you spend your entire life trying to avoid judgment, you accidentally give everyone else control over your life.", "journal": "Whose opinion am I giving way too much power to?", "globalNum": "165"}, {"id": "growing-up-31-making-decisions", "uid": 166, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "31", "title": "Making Decisions", "body": ["Sometimes every choice feels huge.", "Should I join? Should I quit? Should I text them? Should I buy it? Should I change schools? Should I say yes?", "Separate big decisions from small ones", "Not every decision deserves three hours of analysis.", "Small decision: What should I wear? Pick something.", "Big decision: Changing schools. Slow down. Get information. Talk to trusted adults. Think about consequences.", "Ask three questions", "What are my options?", "What could happen with each one?", "Which option matches what I actually want and need?", "Don't make major decisions while extremely emotional", "If you're furious, devastated, or panicking, wait if you safely can.", "Your brain may think differently once you're calmer.", "And remember:", "There is rarely a perfect decision.", "Sometimes you choose the best option with the information you have."], "bigSister": "You don't need certainty to make a good decision.", "journal": "What decision am I avoiding because I'm scared of choosing wrong?", "globalNum": "166"}, {"id": "growing-up-32-making-mistakes", "uid": 167, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "32", "title": "Making Mistakes", "body": ["You messed up.", "Congratulations.", "You're human.", "😭", "Own it", "If you hurt someone: Apologize.", "If you broke something: Try to fix it.", "If you made a bad decision: Learn from it.", "Don't hide everything because you're scared of consequences", "Sometimes hiding a mistake makes it ten times worse.", "Ask yourself:", "What happened? Why did I do it? What was in my control? What wasn't? What can I do differently?", "Don't repeatedly punish yourself", "Guilt can be useful when it pushes you to make things right.", "After that, you need to move forward."], "bigSister": "Making a mistake doesn't mean you have to become the mistake.", "journal": "What can I learn from something I regret?", "globalNum": "167"}, {"id": "growing-up-33-feeling-like-you-re-changing-too-much", "uid": 168, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "33", "title": "Feeling Like You're Changing Too Much", "body": ["One month you love something.", "Next month you hate it.", "New friends. New style. New music. New interests. New opinions.", "And you're like:", "\"Who even am I?\"", "You're allowed to change", "You're growing.", "Your brain, interests, experiences, and environment are changing too.", "You don't need to lock yourself into an identity", "You can try things without deciding:", "\"This is who I am forever.\"", "Keep the things that feel genuinely you", "Maybe your humour. Your values. Your kindness. Your creativity. Your curiosity.", "Those can stay even while everything else changes.", "Don't be scared of becoming someone new", "Sometimes growth means leaving an old version of yourself behind."], "bigSister": "You don't need to have a finished personality at 13. You're still under construction.", "journal": "What's changed about me recently, and do I like the direction I'm going?", "globalNum": "168"}, {"id": "growing-up-34-feeling-like-you-re-growing-apart-from-yourself", "uid": 169, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "34", "title": "Feeling Like You're Growing Apart From Yourself", "body": ["Sometimes you look at old photos and think:", "\"I used to be so happy.\"", "Or:", "\"I don't even recognize myself.\"", "Don't romanticize your past too much", "Your old life probably had problems too.", "You're remembering the good parts because they're easier to miss.", "Ask what changed", "Did you lose hobbies? Stop seeing friends? Get busier? Start comparing yourself more? Become stressed?", "Sometimes you don't miss your old self.", "You miss the things your old self used to do.", "Bring some of them back", "If you used to draw, draw.", "If you loved music, listen again.", "If you used to go outside, take a walk.", "You don't have to become your old self.", "You can bring the good parts forward."], "bigSister": "Growing doesn't mean abandoning everything you used to love.", "journal": "What did I used to enjoy that I could bring back into my life?", "globalNum": "169"}, {"id": "growing-up-35-feeling-like-you-re-too-sensitive", "uid": 170, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "35", "title": "Feeling Like You're Too Sensitive", "body": ["Someone says something.", "It hurts.", "Then someone says:", "\"You're too sensitive.\"", "Maybe.", "Or maybe they were actually being mean.", "Being sensitive isn't automatically bad", "It can mean you're empathetic.", "You notice things.", "You care deeply.", "You pick up on people's emotions.", "Those can be strengths.", "But learn to regulate your emotions", "Feeling something strongly doesn't mean you have to react instantly.", "You can be angry without sending the paragraph.", "You can be hurt without starting an argument.", "You can be upset and wait until you're calmer.", "Ask yourself:", "\"Is this worth reacting to?\"", "Sometimes yes.", "Sometimes no.", "Don't let people use \"you're sensitive\" to dismiss everything", "If someone repeatedly hurts you and then tells you you're the problem for being hurt, that's worth paying attention to."], "bigSister": "You don't need to become emotionless. You just need to learn how to handle your emotions without letting them control every decision.", "journal": "What usually makes my emotions feel overwhelming?", "globalNum": "170"}, {"id": "growing-up-36-crying", "uid": 171, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "36", "title": "Crying", "body": ["You cry because you're angry.", "You cry because you're sad.", "You cry because you're overwhelmed.", "You cry because someone looked at you weird after you've already had a horrible day.", "It happens 😭.", "Crying isn't weakness", "It's one way your body responds to strong emotions.", "You don't need to apologize for having feelings.", "But you can learn what comes after", "Cry. Breathe. Drink water. Wash your face. Take some space.", "Then figure out what actually happened.", "Don't make major decisions while you're extremely upset", "You don't need to: Break up. Quit school. Send the giant paragraph. Delete everyone.", "at 2 a.m. while crying.", "Wait until you're calmer."], "bigSister": "You can feel everything without acting on everything.", "journal": "What usually helps me calm down after I've had a really emotional moment?", "globalNum": "171"}, {"id": "growing-up-37-feeling-angry-all-the-time", "uid": 172, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "37", "title": "Feeling Angry All the Time", "body": ["Sometimes anger is easier to feel than sadness.", "You snap at people.", "Everything annoys you.", "Tiny things make you furious.", "Find the actual feeling underneath", "Ask:", "\"What am I actually feeling?\"", "Maybe you're: Tired. Embarrassed. Ignored. Overwhelmed. Hurt. Scared. Angry.", "The first emotion isn't always the deepest one.", "Give yourself a pause", "Before reacting: Stop. Breathe. Leave the room if you safely can. Get some space. Then talk.", "Find a safe outlet", "Write. Exercise. Walk. Listen to music. Talk to someone.", "You don't have to pretend you're not angry.", "Just don't use anger as permission to hurt people.", "If anger feels impossible to control", "Especially if you're regularly hurting yourself or others, destroying things, or feeling completely out of control, tell a trusted adult and ask for help."], "bigSister": "Anger is a feeling. Hurting people is a behaviour. They're not the same thing.", "journal": "What has been making me angry lately, and what feeling might be underneath it?", "globalNum": "172"}, {"id": "growing-up-38-feeling-overwhelmed", "uid": 173, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "38", "title": "Feeling Overwhelmed", "body": ["Everything needs doing.", "Everyone wants something.", "Your brain is full.", "You don't even know where to start.", "Stop trying to solve everything simultaneously", "Grab paper.", "Write everything down.", "Then choose:", "1 thing I must do now", "2 things I can do later", "Everything else can wait", "Do the first thing", "Not the easiest.", "Not the most fun.", "The thing that genuinely needs attention.", "Take breaks", "Being overwhelmed doesn't mean you need to work harder and harder.", "Sometimes your brain needs ten minutes away from everything.", "Ask for help early", "Don't wait until you're completely drowning.", "Tell someone:", "\"I'm struggling to keep up with everything right now.\"", "That's enough."], "bigSister": "You don't need to carry your entire week in your head at once.", "journal": "What are the three biggest things currently taking up space in my brain?", "globalNum": "173"}, {"id": "growing-up-39-not-feeling-good-enough", "uid": 174, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "39", "title": "Not Feeling Good Enough", "body": ["You get the grade.", "But someone got higher.", "You look good.", "But someone looks better.", "You did well.", "But you think you could've done better.", "There is always another comparison.", "Ask yourself:", "\"Good enough for what?\"", "Sometimes you've created a standard nobody actually asked you to meet.", "Separate improvement from worth", "You can want to improve your grades without believing you're stupid.", "You can want to improve your appearance without believing you're ugly.", "You can want to become more confident without believing you're worthless.", "Notice what you ARE doing", "You survived things you thought you couldn't.", "You learned things you didn't know.", "You changed.", "You kept going.", "That counts.", "You don't have to earn your right to exist", "Your worth isn't a reward for being productive."], "bigSister": "You are a person, not a school report, appearance rating, follower count, or achievement list.", "journal": "What would change if I believed I was already worthy while still working on myself?", "globalNum": "174"}, {"id": "growing-up-40-becoming-the-person-you-actually-want-to-be", "uid": 175, "category": "growing-up", "categoryLabel": "Growing Up", "num": "40", "title": "Becoming the Person You Actually Want to Be", "body": ["At some point, growing up becomes less about:", "\"Who do people want me to be?\"", "and more about:", "\"Who do I want to become?\"", "Think about your values", "Not your aesthetic. Not your job. Not your popularity. Your actual values.", "Do you want to be: Kind? Honest? Independent? Creative? Reliable? Brave? Curious? Funny? Generous?", "Then act like that person in small ways", "Want to be reliable? Keep your promises.", "Want to be confident? Speak up.", "Want to be kind? Treat people well even when nobody's watching.", "Want to be independent? Learn useful skills.", "Don't wait for some future version of yourself", "You don't become that person overnight.", "You build them through tiny choices.", "And don't forget to enjoy your life", "You aren't a self-improvement project that needs constant fixing.", "You're allowed to be messy.", "You're allowed to have bad days.", "You're allowed to change your mind.", "You're allowed to just be a kid sometimes."], "bigSister": "You don't need to become the \"best version of yourself\" every single day. Sometimes the best thing you can do is just live your life, learn something, laugh a lot, and keep going.", "journal": "What kind of person do I want to be when nobody is watching?", "globalNum": "175"}], "challenges": [{"id": "ch-1", "text": "Plan something with friends"}, {"id": "ch-2", "text": "Have a picnic (with friends if wanted)"}, {"id": "ch-3", "text": "Go ice/roller skating"}, {"id": "ch-4", "text": "Go bowling"}, {"id": "ch-5", "text": "Go swimming"}, {"id": "ch-6", "text": "Walk at night/sunset"}, {"id": "ch-7", "text": "Watch the sunset"}, {"id": "ch-8", "text": "Take a timelapse of you being productive"}, {"id": "ch-9", "text": "Make a YT video for fun (fully edited, even if you won't post it)"}, {"id": "ch-10", "text": "Explore the woods"}, {"id": "ch-11", "text": "Do blind karaoke"}, {"id": "ch-12", "text": "Karaoke with friends"}, {"id": "ch-13", "text": "Try a pottery workshop"}, {"id": "ch-14", "text": "Paint pottery"}, {"id": "ch-15", "text": "Face masks and your favorite show/movie"}, {"id": "ch-16", "text": "Stretch"}, {"id": "ch-17", "text": "Write a letter to someone"}, {"id": "ch-18", "text": "Make a super cute letter with stickers for a friend"}, {"id": "ch-19", "text": "Write a letter to your future self"}, {"id": "ch-20", "text": "Make a time capsule"}, {"id": "ch-21", "text": "Drink a big glass of water"}, {"id": "ch-22", "text": "Paint rocks"}, {"id": "ch-23", "text": "Paint shells"}, {"id": "ch-24", "text": "Print out your pictures"}, {"id": "ch-25", "text": "Get rid of any trash in your room"}, {"id": "ch-26", "text": "Plan outfits for future events"}, {"id": "ch-27", "text": "Find a new coffee shop"}], "prompts": [{"id": "pr-1", "text": "Things that make me happy"}, {"id": "pr-2", "text": "Fave songs/books/music/films/photographers"}, {"id": "pr-3", "text": "Nice things people said to me"}, {"id": "pr-4", "text": "Moments of joy"}, {"id": "pr-5", "text": "Things I learnt from my fave book"}, {"id": "pr-6", "text": "Movies that make me happy"}, {"id": "pr-7", "text": "Letters to people I love"}, {"id": "pr-8", "text": "Goals for my future self"}, {"id": "pr-9", "text": "Letters to my future self"}, {"id": "pr-10", "text": "Books I want to read"}, {"id": "pr-11", "text": "Goals for the day"}, {"id": "pr-12", "text": "Manifestation page"}, {"id": "pr-13", "text": "Things I like about myself"}, {"id": "pr-14", "text": "Affirmations"}, {"id": "pr-15", "text": "Wish lists"}, {"id": "pr-16", "text": "Current obsessions"}, {"id": "pr-17", "text": "Fashion trends I want to try"}, {"id": "pr-18", "text": "Places I want to visit"}, {"id": "pr-19", "text": "Pressed flowers, concert tickets, and scrapbook pages"}, {"id": "pr-20", "text": "Daily routines for a good day"}, {"id": "pr-21", "text": "What my dream life looks like"}, {"id": "pr-22", "text": "Fave celebrities and what I can learn from them"}, {"id": "pr-23", "text": "Birthday wishlist"}, {"id": "pr-24", "text": "Planning my wedding / birthday / prom"}, {"id": "pr-25", "text": "Songs that bring me joy"}], "compliments": [{"id": "co-1", "text": "You make people feel comfortable being themselves around you."}, {"id": "co-2", "text": "You notice when someone's having a hard day, even when they don't say it."}, {"id": "co-3", "text": "Your curiosity makes everything around you more interesting."}, {"id": "co-4", "text": "You keep showing up, even on the days it's hard to."}, {"id": "co-5", "text": "The way you talk about the things you love is contagious."}, {"id": "co-6", "text": "You give people your full attention when they're talking to you."}, {"id": "co-7", "text": "You're the kind of person who remembers the little things."}, {"id": "co-8", "text": "You've grown so much, even if it doesn't always feel like it."}, {"id": "co-9", "text": "Your sense of humor makes hard days lighter."}, {"id": "co-10", "text": "You're honest, even when it would be easier not to be."}, {"id": "co-11", "text": "You make space for other people to shine."}, {"id": "co-12", "text": "You keep trying even when things don't come easily."}, {"id": "co-13", "text": "Your kindness isn't loud, but people feel it."}, {"id": "co-14", "text": "You ask good questions — the kind that show you're really listening."}, {"id": "co-15", "text": "You've got really good taste, and you're not afraid to like what you like."}, {"id": "co-16", "text": "You're someone people trust with the real stuff."}, {"id": "co-17", "text": "You bring a calmness into rooms that need it."}, {"id": "co-18", "text": "You're allowed to be proud of how far you've come."}, {"id": "co-19", "text": "Your creativity comes through in how you solve problems."}, {"id": "co-20", "text": "You say sorry when you mean it, and that matters more than people admit."}, {"id": "co-21", "text": "You have a way of making people feel less alone."}, {"id": "co-22", "text": "Your energy is genuinely magnetic when you're excited about something."}, {"id": "co-23", "text": "You're more resilient than you give yourself credit for."}, {"id": "co-24", "text": "You know how to laugh at yourself, and that's a good sign."}, {"id": "co-25", "text": "You're thoughtful about the way your choices affect other people."}, {"id": "co-26", "text": "You don't need to be the loudest person in the room to be memorable."}, {"id": "co-27", "text": "You're doing better than your inner critic gives you credit for."}, {"id": "co-28", "text": "You have really good instincts — trust them more."}, {"id": "co-29", "text": "The people who know you well are lucky to have you."}, {"id": "co-30", "text": "You put real care into the things you make and do."}, {"id": "co-31", "text": "You're growing into exactly who you're supposed to be, one day at a time."}, {"id": "co-32", "text": "You make ordinary days a little more fun just by being there."}, {"id": "co-33", "text": "You're brave in ways that don't always get noticed."}, {"id": "co-34", "text": "Your perspective on things is genuinely worth hearing."}, {"id": "co-35", "text": "You handle setbacks better than you think you do."}, {"id": "co-36", "text": "You're someone's favorite part of their day, probably more often than you know."}, {"id": "co-37", "text": "You have a good heart, and it shows in how you treat people."}, {"id": "co-38", "text": "You're allowed to take up space — and you deserve to."}, {"id": "co-39", "text": "You make things better just by paying attention."}, {"id": "co-40", "text": "You're exactly enough, right now, as you are."}], "studytips": [{"id": "st-1", "text": "Study in 25-minute chunks with 5-minute breaks — it's easier to start than 'study for 3 hours.'"}, {"id": "st-2", "text": "Test yourself instead of rereading notes. Retrieval beats recognition."}, {"id": "st-3", "text": "Explain the topic out loud like you're teaching it to someone else."}, {"id": "st-4", "text": "Do the hardest subject first, while your focus is freshest."}, {"id": "st-5", "text": "Put your phone in another room while you study, not just on silent."}, {"id": "st-6", "text": "Make a short 'must do / should do / can wait' list before you start."}, {"id": "st-7", "text": "Study a little every day instead of cramming the night before."}, {"id": "st-8", "text": "Use flashcards for anything you have to memorize, not just reread."}, {"id": "st-9", "text": "Past papers and practice questions matter more than rereading the textbook."}, {"id": "st-10", "text": "Write a one-line summary of each topic in your own words."}, {"id": "st-11", "text": "Study near daylight if you can — it helps with focus and mood."}, {"id": "st-12", "text": "Batch similar homework together instead of task-switching constantly."}, {"id": "st-13", "text": "If you don't understand something, find a different explanation of it — don't just reread the same one."}, {"id": "st-14", "text": "Keep a running 'confusing topics' list and clear it weekly."}, {"id": "st-15", "text": "Sleep before a big exam matters more than one extra hour of revision."}, {"id": "st-16", "text": "Set a timer for how long a task 'should' take — it keeps you honest."}, {"id": "st-17", "text": "Study the way you'll be tested — if it's written, practice writing it."}, {"id": "st-18", "text": "Take actual breaks. Scrolling on your phone for 5 minutes isn't a break."}, {"id": "st-19", "text": "Color-code by urgency, not by how nice it looks."}, {"id": "st-20", "text": "Reward yourself after finishing a task, not while you're still doing it."}]};
